=begin
  Works in Saga FE!
  Creature Window - Real-Time Creature & Bounty Display

  Creates a dedicated window to display creature information and statuses
  in real time. Supports both Wrayth FE panel and GTK window for Avalon
  and Wizard FEs. Live targets are shown with standardized status indicators
  (stunned, calmed, frozen, held, prone, etc), dead creatures are filtered
  to a separate list, and your current TARGET is highlighted at the top.
  Optionally tracks kill metrics (Avg TTK, Last TTK, KPM) and displays
  bounty task information.

  Target-next mode (*cwtargetnext) has three states, cycled in order (or set
  directly, e.g. "*cwtargetnext off"):
    off        - original behavior: current target floats to its own row at the top
    numbers    - target stays in arrival-order sequence, tagged with its number, asterisked
    no_numbers - target stays in arrival-order sequence (asterisked), numbers hidden
  Numbers are based on when each creature first appeared in the room, tracked
  by its unique game ID, e.g. "1creature **2creature** 3creature 4creature" /
  "5creature". A creature's number sticks with its ID even after it dies and
  moves to the dead-creature list, and resets when you change rooms.

  References:
    Wrayth FE Window: https://discordapp.com/channels/226045346399256576/1339018254517145681
    GTK Window:       https://discordapp.com/channels/226045346399256576/1386507836191670342

  Usage:
    ;creaturewindow              - Start creature window

  In-game Commands (while running):
    *cwttk                        - Toggle time-to-kill metrics display
    *cwbty                        - Toggle bounty task display
    *cwcol <1-10>                 - Set the creature grid's column count
                                  (used when *cwflow is "row")
    *cwrow <1-10>                 - Set the creature grid's row count
                                  (used when *cwflow is "col")
    *cwflow                       - Cycle creature grid fill direction: row -> col -> row
    *cwflow row                   - Jump directly to "row": fills left-to-right
                                  first, then wraps top-to-bottom (uses *cwcol)
    *cwflow col                   - Jump directly to "col": fills top-to-bottom
                                  first, then wraps left-to-right (uses *cwrow)
    *cwdead                       - Toggle keeping dead creatures inline with
                                  the live grid instead of a separate list
    *cwclaim                     - Hide/show claim status
    *cwcustom1                   - Toggle a fixed special layout: counts +
                                  bounty info/task + Gem Onslaught status +
                                  Empyrean kill counter + comma-separated
                                  hazard names, then a hard-coded 3-column,
                                  column-major creature grid that keeps
                                  dead creatures in place (arrival order)
    *cwonslaught timer            - Toggle Gem Onslaught location/timer
                                  display (off by default). Works whether
                                  *cwcustom1 is on or off.
    *cwonslaught counter          - Toggle the Empyrean kill counter display
                                  (off by default; kill tracking itself
                                  always runs in the background regardless
                                  of this toggle). Works whether *cwcustom1
                                  is on or off. Shows two counts: an alien
                                  emoji (total, never resets) and a flying
                                  saucer emoji (resets to 0 whenever an
                                  Empyrean captain's encounter ends).
    *cwicon <empyrean|saucer> <emoji>
                                  - Override the alien/flying-saucer Empyrean
                                  counter icons with a pasted emoji.
    *cwicon <empyrean|saucer> reset
                                  - Revert an icon slot to its default.
    *cwhazard                    - Cycle hazard display: above -> between -> below_dead -> off
    *cwheaders                   - Cycle Creatures:/Hazards:/Dead Creatures: count headers: text -> emoji -> off
    *cwstatus                    - Cycle Saga status display: text -> unicode -> emoji -> text
    *cwtargetnext                - Cycle target-next mode: off -> numbers -> no_numbers
    *cwtargetnext off            - Jump directly to a specific mode (off/numbers/no_numbers)
    *cwhp                        - Cycle target HP display: off -> text -> bar
    *cwtargetid                  - Cycle the target marker icon (Saga emoji mode only)
    *cwucs                       - Toggle UCS display under the current target:
                                  "Pos: N     Tup: Action" ("N     Action" when
                                  *cwheaders is off), showing tracked UCS position
                                  tier and the current tierup vulnerability (if
                                  any); clicking the Tup value attempts that attack
                                  on the current target
    *cwtest                      - Toggle test mode: populate 24 fake creatures
                                  (random statuses, some dead) and 3 fake
                                  hazards for visually testing layouts
                                  without a real room full of creatures, with
                                  the first fake creature set as a fake current
                                  target (fake UCS reading included, for *cwucs)
    *cwgtk                       - Enable GTK window
    *cwherb                      - Run the herb bounty workflow (also triggered by clicking the bounty action link)
    *cwgem                       - Run the gem bounty workflow (also triggered by clicking the bounty action link)
    *cwguild                     - Run the guild bounty workflow (also triggered by clicking the bounty action link)
    *cwguard                     - Run the guard bounty workflow (also triggered by clicking the bounty action link)
    *cwfurrier                   - Run the furrier bounty workflow (also triggered by clicking the bounty action link)
    *cwskin                      - Run the skin bounty workflow (also triggered by clicking the bounty action link)

  Author: Claude Code(Creator and Feature Additions), Codex(Bug Fixes and Review), RuseofFools (Very Little)
  Required: Lich >= 5.20.0
  Tags: wrayth, saga, frontend, mod, window, target, creature, mob, bounty, advguild, avalon, wizard, gtk3
  Version: 1.30.0
  Recently changed:
    v1.30.0  (2026-08-31)
    Added *cwucs: "Pos: N     Tup: Action" ("N     Action" when *cwheaders
    is off) under the current target, showing tracked UCS position tier
    and the current tierup vulnerability; the Tup value is a link that
    attempts that attack on the current target when clicked. *cwtest now
    also picks a fake current target (with a fake UCS reading) so the row
    has something to show while testing.
    v1.29.0 (2026-08-30) - Added the four ghostly goliath forms found in
      the current log to the Empyrean Onslaught kill counter.
    v1.28.0 (2026-08-30) - Added *cwicon <empyrean|saucer> <emoji>/reset,
      letting the two Empyrean counter icons be overridden with a pasted
      emoji (converted to the same XML-numeric-entity form every other
      icon in this file uses) instead of the built-in alien/flying-saucer
      defaults. Built for panelcontrol.lic's emoji-picker button, but works
      the same typed in-game.
    v1.27.0 (2026-08-29) - Both Empyrean counters (alien and flying saucer)
      now also reset to 0 whenever the Gem Onslaught itself transitions
      from active to inactive, per the user, on top of the flying saucer's
      existing per-captain reset.
    v1.26.0 (2026-08-29) - *cwcustom1: moved the flying-saucer counter up
      to row 2, directly under the alien counter in row 1 (was row 3).
      Normal (non-custom1) panel: alien and flying-saucer counters now
      render on the same line as, and before, the onslaught timer text
      (was three separate lines), with each count reserving a fixed
      4-digit (alien) / 3-digit (flying saucer) width so the following
      icon/text doesn't drift as the numbers grow.
    v1.25.0 (2026-08-29) - Added a second Empyrean kill counter (flying
      saucer emoji), tracked alongside the existing alien-emoji one
      (unchanged) under *cwonslaught counter. Unlike the permanent alien
      counter, this one resets to 0 every time a battle-worn Empyrean
      captain's encounter ends (confirmed against Daena's own 2026-08-28
      Empyrean Skyship logs: the captain either flees through a portal or
      is killed and disintegrates, both gender-agnostic), then counts back
      up for the next corridor-fighting phase between captain encounters.
    v1.24.0 (2026-08-29) - Added black metal bomb to the detected hazard list.
    v1.23.0 (2026-08-28) - Added Sounds parsing with the speaker-at-high-volume
      emoji, plus sitting parsing with the chair emoji.
    v1.22.0 (2026-08-28) - *cwonslaught timer/counter now both work whether
      *cwcustom1 is on or off, per the user -- the normal (non-custom1)
      panel gained its own Onslaught line and Empyrean-counter line (shared
      text via the new onslaught_texts helper, same as *cwcustom1's own
      display), and the background "gem onslaught" poll no longer requires
      *cwcustom1 to be active, only *cwonslaught timer itself.
    v1.21.0 (2026-08-28) - Split *cwonslaught into *cwonslaught timer
      (Gem Onslaught location/time display, the old *cwonslaught behavior)
      and *cwonslaught counter (the Empyrean kill counter display) -- the
      counter previously had no toggle of its own and always showed once
      *cwcustom1 was on. Kill tracking itself still always runs in the
      background regardless of the counter toggle, so the count is already
      correct whenever it's turned on.
    v1.20.0 (2026-08-28) - *cwcustom1: added an Empyrean kill counter (alien
      emoji + bare count) to the top-right of row 1, counting only specific
      Hive Onslaught creatures (masked goliath plunderer, tawny armor-clad
      pegasus, radiant-eyed goliath auramancer, burly goliath engineer,
      branded goliath diviner) regardless of room claim, never reset by
      inactivity. Added *cwonslaught to toggle Gem Onslaught tracking/
      display separately from *cwcustom1 itself -- off by default, so the
      onslaught header/detail and its periodic "gem onslaught" poll now
      both stay idle until explicitly turned on.
    v1.19.0 (2026-08-27) - Replaced *cwcol1-8 with a single *cwcol <1-10>
      command, added a matching *cwrow <1-10>, and added *cwflow to pick
      which one governs the grid: "row" (left-to-right first, wraps
      top-to-bottom, per *cwcol) or "col" (top-to-bottom first, wraps
      left-to-right, per *cwrow). Added *cwdead to keep dead creatures
      inline with the live grid instead of listing them separately.
      *cwheaders now cycles text -> emoji -> off instead of a plain
      on/off toggle.
    v1.18.0 (2026-08-27) - Added *cwtest: populates 24 fake creatures with
      random statuses (including some dead) and 3 fake hazards, for
      visually testing layouts (e.g. *cwcustom1) without needing a real
      room full of creatures. Toggle off to return to live data.
    v1.17.1 (2026-08-27) - *cwcustom1 reworked into 3 real side-by-side
      columns (Creatures/Bounty/Onslaught) per the user, instead of
      stacking Onslaught underneath Bounty in one shared text column.
      Creatures gets ~1/4 the width of Bounty/Onslaught (90 of 460px);
      Bounty and Onslaught split the rest evenly. Onslaught's next-start
      time now shows 12-hour clock (was 24-hour) -- no actual timezone
      math needed despite the request, since it's built from the game's
      relative countdown ("... from now)") added to Time.now, which is
      already this system's local time regardless of the server's own
      zone, not from parsing the absolute Elanthian/Eastern clock text.
    v1.17.0 (2026-08-27) - Added Gem Onslaught status to *cwcustom1, third
      in the right column after the bounty rows: "Next Onslaught" + local
      start time when inactive, "<Location> Onslaught" + hours/minutes
      remaining (seconds skipped) when active. Actively polls "gem
      onslaught" (silenced) every 60s while *cwcustom1 is on, since unlike
      bounty there's no passively-tracked field for it.
    v1.16.6 (2026-08-25) - Fixed *cwcustom1's complete-task button being
      wrongly gated on an active task (task_type != :none), which hid the
      "Get New Bounty (AdvGuild)" button entirely whenever no bounty was
      active -- confirmed missing live. Matches the normal panel's own
      gating now (display_bounty only).
    v1.16.5 (2026-08-25) - *cwcustom1: creature grid columns now fill to
      8 rows before spilling into the next column (was 7), per the user.
    v1.16.4 (2026-08-25) - *cwcustom1 row rework per the user: dropped
      bounty_status_line entirely ("Return it to the guard!" etc.); moved
      bounty_task_line up onto the Creature count row; and moved the
      complete-task button off its own row onto the Dead count row.
    v1.16.3 (2026-08-25) - *cwcustom1: added the missing complete-task
      button (bounty_action_line/bounty_action_cmd) as its own full-width
      row under the hazard row -- 1.16.0 only wired up the info/task text
      and had dropped the actual clickable action entirely.
    v1.16.2 (2026-08-25) - *cwcustom1: dead creatures now stay in the
      creature list, in their same arrival-order slot, instead of
      dropping out on death -- rendered as loot links (like the normal
      dead-creature list) rather than target links.
    v1.16.1 (2026-08-25) - *cwcustom1 tuning per the user: removed the
      extra spacer row between hazards and the creature grid; creature
      columns now split the full panel width evenly (was undershooting it
      using the general grid's column width); and each column fills to a
      fixed 7 rows before spilling into the next, regardless of actual
      creature count, instead of spreading thin across all 3 columns.
    v1.16.0 (2026-08-25) - Added *cwcustom1: a fixed special layout (not a
      variation on the normal one -- ignores every other display toggle
      while active). Counts row (Creature/Dead/Hazard, icon+number) paired
      with Bounty Info/Bounty Task text, a comma-separated inline hazard
      name list, then a hard-coded 3-column creature grid filled
      column-major (down column 1 first, then 2, then 3) instead of the
      row-major order used everywhere else. Dead creatures are counted but
      never individually listed.
    v1.15.1 (2026-08-25) - Combined header row (3+ columns) reworked per
      the user: Creatures/Hazards/Dead Creatures order, icon + bare count
      only (no label text or colon), Hazards always shown regardless of
      whether any are present, and moved to fall under the bounty display
      instead of above it.
    v1.15.0 (2026-08-25) - Per the user: at 3+ columns, the Hazards:/
      Creatures:/Dead Creatures: headers now combine onto one row instead
      of stacking, in both the native dialog and GTK window. Also added
      emoji icons for all three headers (warning/skull/rat) when *cwstatus
      is in emoji mode.
    v1.14.2 (2026-08-25) - Fixed the real bug behind "*cwbty doesn't turn
      off": the native dialog's clear='t' does not purge a previously-
      rendered element that's simply left out of a later update, so
      toggling a display_* setting off just froze the bounty/TTK/KPM/
      header rows at their last value instead of hiding them. Bounty,
      Avg TTK, Last TTK, Kills/Min, and the *cwheaders row IDs now always
      render with a blank value when hidden instead of being omitted.
    v1.14.1 (2026-08-25) - Renamed *bty -> *cwbty and *ttk -> *cwttk for
      naming consistency with every other command.
    v1.14.0 (2026-08-25) - Added *cwheaders: toggles the Creatures:/
      Hazards:/Dead Creatures: count headers, in both the native dialog
      and GTK window.

    Older pre-versioning history trimmed 2026-08-31 -- the full "Recently
    changed" list had grown past 20,000 bytes, past the read limit
    repository.lic's uploader uses to find this header's closing =end,
    which was silently breaking author/tags/version-requirement detection
    on upload. Keep this section well under that limit going forward by
    trimming the oldest entries as new ones are added.
=end

no_kill_all

require 'yaml'

module CreatureWindow
  extend self
  include Lich::Common if defined?(Lich::Common)
  BOUNTY_TURNIN_NPC_REGEX = /brother Barnstel|scarred Agarnil kris|healer|herbalist|merchant Kelph|famed baker Leaftoe|Akrash|old Mistress Lomara|dwarven clerk|dwarven guard|gem dealer|jeweler|Zirconia|town guard|Gate guard|Guard Corporal Rex|Guard Private Witlass|Corporal Sleetwood|sergeant|city guardsman|Guardsman|purser|Belle|furrier|Guild Taskmaster|sentry luthrek|fur trader Delosa|bramblefist|Halfwhistle|tavernkeeper|tavern|brindlestoat|Libram Greenleaf|Sparkfinger|Maraene|Bumbleberry|alchemist/i
  GEM_TURNIN_NPC_REGEX = /gem dealer|jeweler|brindlestoat|zirconia/i
  BLOCKED_GEMSHOP_ROOM_IDS = [3845].freeze
  BLOCKED_GEMSHOP_UIDS = [3201285].freeze
  BLOCKED_GEMSHOP_TITLES = /Etaenia's Jewels/i
  GEMSHOP_UID_BY_TOWN = {
    "Cold River" => "u7503259",
  }.freeze
  BOUNTY_POLL_SECONDS = 1
  BOUNTY_WORKFLOW_STOP_SCRIPTS = %w[bigshot go2 eloot hunt3_v2].freeze
  # "gem onslaught" has no passively-tracked Lich-core field the way
  # checkbounty does -- it has to be actively sent and its plain-text
  # response captured, so this polls far less often than bounty (a
  # session lasts ~tens of minutes and the next-one countdown spans hours,
  # so 60s is still plenty fresh without spamming the command).
  ONSLAUGHT_POLL_SECONDS = 60

  # *cwtargetnext cycles through these modes in order:
  #   off        - original behavior: current target floats to its own row at the top
  #   numbers    - target stays in arrival-order sequence, tagged with its number, asterisked
  #   no_numbers - target stays in arrival-order sequence (asterisked), but numbers are hidden
  TARGET_NEXT_MODES = %w[off numbers no_numbers].freeze
  HAZARD_DISPLAY_MODES = %w[above between below_dead off].freeze
  SAGA_STATUS_MODES = %w[text unicode emoji].freeze
  # *cwflow cycles through these (or jumps directly, e.g. "*cwflow col"):
  #   row - creatures fill left-to-right first, then wrap top-to-bottom
  #         (*cwcol's count is the number of columns per row)
  #   col - creatures fill top-to-bottom first, then wrap left-to-right
  #         (*cwrow's count is the number of rows per column)
  GRID_FLOWS = %w[row col].freeze
  # *cwheaders cycles through these:
  #   text  - full "Creatures: N" / "Hazards: N" / "Dead Creatures: N" labels
  #   emoji - compact icon + bare count, combined onto one row
  #   off   - hidden entirely
  HEADER_MODES = %w[text emoji off].freeze
  # Translates Creature[]'s crtrStatus-driven canonical status names (see
  # CRTR_STATUS_FLAGS in lib/common/creature/creature_base.rb) to the words
  # creature_status_fix has always used for its icon-table lookups, so a
  # single label vocabulary works for both. Names absent here (disoriented,
  # kneeling, hovering, hidden) pass through unchanged -- they render as
  # plain text unless they have a direct icon-table entry.
  CRTR_STATUS_DISPLAY_MAP = {
    "immobilized" => "frozen",
    "sleeping"    => "unconscious",
    "calm"        => "calmed"
  }.freeze
  # *cwhp cycles through these modes in order:
  #   off  - no target HP display
  #   text - live "###/### hp" readout (current/max, via Combat::Tracker)
  #   bar  - a 10-segment bar (filled = remaining HP) plus the "###/### hp"
  #          readout on the same line
  TARGET_HP_MODES = %w[off text bar].freeze
  # XML numeric character references, not raw UTF-8 literals -- raw non-ASCII
  # bytes don't reliably survive a dialog control's value='' attribute (see
  # CW_SAGA_STATUS_ICONS_UNICODE/_EMOJI above for the same pattern).
  TARGET_HP_BAR_SEGMENT = "&#x1F7E5;" # U+1F7E5 red square (remaining HP)
  TARGET_HP_BAR_EMPTY_SEGMENT = "&#x2B1B;" # U+2B1B black large square (lost HP)
  TARGET_HP_BAR_SEGMENTS = 10
  # *cwtargetid cycles through these. Emoji-mode only: marks the current
  # target with one icon to its left (not wrapped on both sides like the
  # "**name**" bolding used in text/unicode mode).
  TARGET_MARKER_ICONS = [
    "&#x2297;",  # U+2297 circled times
    "&#x2A01;",  # U+2A01 n-ary circled plus operator
    "&#x1F3AF;"  # U+1F3AF direct hit (target)
  ].freeze
  HAZARD_TARGET_PATTERN = /cloud|sandstorm|vine|web|whirlwind|unearthly silvery blue globe|spiraling ghostly rift|pale hovering runestone/i
  CREATURE_ROW_HEIGHT = 20
  CREATURE_COLUMN_WIDTH = 140
  HAZARD_COLUMN_WIDTH = 170
  # Wide enough that the longest bounty action line ("Task Complete - Go to
  # AdvGuard and Ask About Bounty", 53 chars) fits on one line at the default
  # font size instead of wrapping -- wrapped text still only gets a single
  # CREATURE_ROW_HEIGHT of vertical space (fixed top='' positioning doesn't
  # account for wrap), so a wrap here overlaps whatever renders next.
  BOUNTY_ROW_WIDTH = 460

  # *cwcustom1's Empyrean kill counter (top-right of row 1, per the user) --
  # counts only these specific Hive Onslaught creatures, matched
  # case-insensitively against the creature's full descriptive name (so "a
  # masked goliath plunderer"/"the masked goliath plunderer" both match).
  # Not gated on Lich::Claim like the KPM room-kill counter, and never reset
  # by inactivity -- it's meant to keep counting across the whole event, not
  # just one room/session of kills.
  EMPYREAN_KILL_NAMES = [
    "masked goliath plunderer",
    "tawny armor-clad pegasus",
    "radiant-eyed goliath auramancer",
    "burly goliath engineer",
    "branded goliath diviner",
    "ghostly goliath plunderer",
    "ghostly goliath auramancer",
    "ghostly goliath engineer",
    "ghostly goliath diviner"
  ].freeze
  EMPYREAN_ICON = "&#x1F47D;" # U+1F47D alien

  # Second Empyrean counter, per the user: same kills as EMPYREAN_ICON above
  # (that tracker is untouched -- never resets), but this one resets to 0
  # every time an Empyrean captain encounter ends, tracking "kills since the
  # last captain" for the corridor-fighting phase between captain fights.
  # A captain encounter can end two ways, and the flavor text for each is
  # RANDOMIZED per encounter (confirmed against multiple real captain fights
  # -- an initial fixed-phrase flee pattern missed a later encounter that
  # used entirely different wording), so both patterns key off the common
  # thread across variants rather than one exact phrase, gender-agnostic
  # since the captain's pronoun (he/she) is also randomized per spawn:
  #   - flees through a portal, e.g. "takes a step back ... tears open a
  #     swirling portal of multicolored energy and steps back into it,
  #     disappearing from sight" or "staggers back ... rips open a
  #     rainbowed portal and dives into it, vanishing as the swirling
  #     colors engulf her form and wink away" -- always "captain" +
  #     "portal" + a disappear/vanish/wink-away/dive-into-it verb
  #   - is killed, which is itself TWO separate messages several real
  #     seconds apart (confirmed against Daena's own XML log -- 35 seconds
  #     between them in one fight, with unrelated combat/spell/dialog text
  #     in between): an immediate defeat line ("A look of surprise crosses
  #     a battle-worn Empyrean captain's face, utter disbelief at his own
  #     defeat lasting only moments before he collapses, ...") followed
  #     much later by the actual corpse-disintegration line ("form
  #     stretches and distorts ... fading away with a final shimmer,
  #     leaving nothing behind"). CAPTAIN_DEFEATED_PATTERN matches EITHER
  #     one -- resetting on the earlier "collapses" line is what actually
  #     matters (that's the real moment the fight ends), the later
  #     disintegration line matching too is just a harmless redundant
  #     reset, not a second required trigger.
  EMPYREAN_SINCE_CAPTAIN_ICON = "&#x1F6F8;" # U+1F6F8 flying saucer
  CAPTAIN_FLEE_PATTERN = /battle-worn Empyrean captain.*?portal.*?(?:disappearing from sight|vanishing|wink(?:s|ing)? away|dives? into it)/i.freeze
  CAPTAIN_DEFEATED_PATTERN = /battle-worn Empyrean captain.*?(?:collapses|fading away with a final shimmer|leaving nothing behind)/i.freeze

  # *cwicon <slot> <emoji> lets the player override specific icons without
  # editing the script -- currently just the two Empyrean counters (slots
  # "empyrean"/"saucer"), since those are the only icons this file doesn't
  # already offer a built-in alternative for via *cwstatus. Keys are the
  # slot name, values are already-converted XML numeric-entity strings (see
  # CreatureWindow.set_custom_icon!) ready to drop straight into a label.
  CUSTOM_ICON_SLOTS = %w[empyrean saucer].freeze

  # *cwucs -- valid UCS attack types, matching Lich::Gemstone::Creature#ucs_tierup's
  # values verbatim (lib/gemstone/combat/defs/ucs.rb's TIERUP_PATTERN capture
  # group), lowercase. Only used to pick a random one for *cwtest.
  CW_UCS_ACTIONS = %w[jab punch grapple kick].freeze

  class << self
    attr_accessor :settings, :window_settings, :use_gtk_window,
                  :display_bounty, :display_avg_ttk, :display_last_ttk, :display_kpm,
                  :display_claim, :target_next_mode, :hazard_display_mode, :saga_status_mode,
                  :target_hp_mode, :target_marker_index, :gtk_available,
                  :grid_cols, :grid_rows, :grid_flow, :dead_inline,
                  :header_mode, :custom_layout1, :onslaught_timer_enabled, :onslaught_counter_enabled, :test_mode,
                  :custom_icons, :ucs_mode
  end
end

def CreatureWindow.deep_merge_hash(base, override)
  base.merge(override) do |_k, base_val, override_val|
    if base_val.is_a?(Hash) && override_val.is_a?(Hash)
      CreatureWindow.deep_merge_hash(base_val, override_val)
    else
      override_val
    end
  end
end

def CreatureWindow.coerce_integer(value, min: nil, max: nil, allow_nil: false)
  return nil if allow_nil && value.nil?

  integer =
    case value
    when Integer then value
    when Float then value.to_i
    when String
      stripped = value.strip
      return nil if allow_nil && stripped.empty?
      Integer(stripped, 10)
    else
      return nil if allow_nil
      raise ArgumentError, "invalid integer value: #{value.inspect}"
    end

  integer = [integer, min].max if min
  integer = [integer, max].min if max
  integer
rescue ArgumentError, TypeError
  return nil if allow_nil

  raise
end

CW_DEFAULT_WINDOW_SETTINGS = {
  "creaturewindow" => {
    "grid_cols"              => 2,
    "grid_rows"               => 8,
    "grid_flow"               => "row",
    "dead_inline"             => false,
    "display_avg_ttk"        => false,
    "display_last_ttk"       => false,
    "display_kpm"            => false,
    "display_bounty"         => true,
    "display_claim"          => true,
    "target_next_mode"       => "off",
    "hazard_display_mode"    => "above",
    "saga_status_mode"       => "unicode",
    "target_hp_mode"         => "off",
    "target_marker_index"    => 0,
    "ucs_mode"                => false,
    "x"                      => 1440,
    "y"                      => 1600,
    "width"                  => 420,
    "height"                 => 370,
    "font_size"              => 17,
    "use_gtk_creaturewindow" => true,
    "palette"                => "White on Black",
    "header_mode"            => "text",
    "custom_layout1"         => false,
    "onslaught_timer_enabled"   => false,
    "onslaught_counter_enabled" => false,
    "custom_icons"              => {}
  },
} unless defined?(CW_DEFAULT_WINDOW_SETTINGS)

def CreatureWindow.sanitize_window_settings(settings)
  sanitized = CreatureWindow.deep_merge_hash(CW_DEFAULT_WINDOW_SETTINGS, settings.is_a?(Hash) ? settings : {})
  cw = sanitized["creaturewindow"] ||= {}
  defaults = CW_DEFAULT_WINDOW_SETTINGS["creaturewindow"]

  %w[
    use_gtk_creaturewindow
    display_bounty
    display_avg_ttk
    display_last_ttk
    display_kpm
    display_claim
    dead_inline
    custom_layout1
    onslaught_timer_enabled
    onslaught_counter_enabled
  ].each do |key|
    cw[key] = !!cw[key]
  end

  # Target-next mode: migrate the old boolean (true/false) to the new
  # three-way string, then make sure whatever's left is a known mode.
  case cw["target_next_mode"]
  when true
    cw["target_next_mode"] = "numbers"
  when false, nil
    cw["target_next_mode"] = "off"
  end
  cw["target_next_mode"] = "off" unless CreatureWindow::TARGET_NEXT_MODES.include?(cw["target_next_mode"])

  cw["hazard_display_mode"] = cw["hazard_display_mode"].to_s
  cw["hazard_display_mode"] = "above" unless CreatureWindow::HAZARD_DISPLAY_MODES.include?(cw["hazard_display_mode"])

  cw["saga_status_mode"] = cw["saga_status_mode"].to_s
  cw["saga_status_mode"] = "unicode" unless CreatureWindow::SAGA_STATUS_MODES.include?(cw["saga_status_mode"])

  # Target HP mode: migrate the old boolean (display_target_hp true/false)
  # to the new three-way string, then make sure whatever's left is known.
  case cw["target_hp_mode"]
  when true
    cw["target_hp_mode"] = "text"
  when false, nil
    cw["target_hp_mode"] = cw.key?("display_target_hp") ? (cw["display_target_hp"] ? "text" : "off") : "off"
  end
  cw["target_hp_mode"] = "off" unless CreatureWindow::TARGET_HP_MODES.include?(cw["target_hp_mode"])
  cw.delete("display_target_hp")

  cw["target_marker_index"] = CreatureWindow.coerce_integer(cw["target_marker_index"], min: 0, max: CreatureWindow::TARGET_MARKER_ICONS.size - 1, allow_nil: true) || 0

  # *cwicon overrides -- only known slots, only non-empty string values
  # survive; anything else (including a corrupt/foreign value type) is
  # dropped rather than raising, same rescue-and-rebuild spirit as the rest
  # of this method.
  icons = cw["custom_icons"].is_a?(Hash) ? cw["custom_icons"] : {}
  cw["custom_icons"] = icons.each_with_object({}) do |(slot, value), memo|
    next unless CreatureWindow::CUSTOM_ICON_SLOTS.include?(slot.to_s)
    next unless value.is_a?(String) && !value.empty?

    memo[slot.to_s] = value
  end

  # Grid columns/rows (1-10 each). Falls back to the legacy single "columns"/
  # "single_column" settings for old configs, then drops them.
  cw["grid_cols"] = CreatureWindow.coerce_integer(cw["grid_cols"], min: 1, max: 10, allow_nil: true)
  cw["grid_cols"] ||= CreatureWindow.coerce_integer(cw["columns"], min: 1, max: 10, allow_nil: true) || (cw["single_column"] ? 1 : 2)
  cw["grid_rows"] = CreatureWindow.coerce_integer(cw["grid_rows"], min: 1, max: 10, allow_nil: true) || 8
  cw.delete("columns")
  cw.delete("single_column")

  cw["grid_flow"] = cw["grid_flow"].to_s
  cw["grid_flow"] = "row" unless CreatureWindow::GRID_FLOWS.include?(cw["grid_flow"])

  # Header display mode: migrate the old show_headers boolean (true/false)
  # to the new three-way string, then make sure whatever's left is known.
  if cw["header_mode"].nil?
    cw["header_mode"] = cw.key?("show_headers") ? (cw["show_headers"] ? "text" : "off") : "text"
  end
  cw["header_mode"] = cw["header_mode"].to_s
  cw["header_mode"] = "text" unless CreatureWindow::HEADER_MODES.include?(cw["header_mode"])
  cw.delete("show_headers")

  cw["font_size"] = CreatureWindow.coerce_integer(cw["font_size"], min: 8, max: 30) rescue defaults["font_size"]
  cw["width"] = CreatureWindow.coerce_integer(cw["width"], min: 220, max: 2400, allow_nil: true)
  cw["height"] = CreatureWindow.coerce_integer(cw["height"], min: 120, max: 1800, allow_nil: true)
  cw["x"] = CreatureWindow.coerce_integer(cw["x"], min: -10_000, max: 10_000, allow_nil: true)
  cw["y"] = CreatureWindow.coerce_integer(cw["y"], min: -10_000, max: 10_000, allow_nil: true)
  palette_names = defined?(CreatureWindow::PALETTES) ? CreatureWindow::PALETTES.keys : [defaults["palette"]]
  cw["palette"] = defaults["palette"] unless palette_names.include?(cw["palette"])

  sanitized
rescue StandardError
  CreatureWindow.deep_merge_hash(CW_DEFAULT_WINDOW_SETTINGS, {})
end

def CreatureWindow.window_settings_path(name: Char.name)
  # Use $data_dir and XMLData.game for Lich data structure
  base_dir = "#{$data_dir}#{XMLData.game}/#{name}"
  Dir.mkdir("#{$data_dir}#{XMLData.game}") unless File.exist?("#{$data_dir}#{XMLData.game}")
  Dir.mkdir(base_dir) unless File.exist?(base_dir)
  File.join(base_dir, "lichwindows.yaml")
end

def CreatureWindow.load_window_settings(name: Char.name)
  filename = CreatureWindow.window_settings_path(name: name)
  settings_hash = nil

  if File.exist?(filename) && name == Char.name
    begin
      raw = File.read(filename)
      parsed = YAML.safe_load(raw, permitted_classes: [Hash, Array, String, Integer, Float, TrueClass, FalseClass, NilClass], aliases: false)
      settings_hash = CreatureWindow.sanitize_window_settings(parsed)
      File.write(filename, settings_hash.to_yaml) if parsed != settings_hash
    rescue => e
      echo "Window settings: Corrupt settings file detected (#{e.message}). Rebuilding defaults..."
      settings_hash = CreatureWindow.sanitize_window_settings({})
      File.write(filename, settings_hash.to_yaml)
    end
  elsif !File.exist?(filename) && name != Char.name
    echo "Window settings: Attempt to load a profile (#{name}) that does not exist."
    settings_hash = nil
  elsif !File.exist?(filename) && name == Char.name
    echo "Window settings: No current settings found. Loading defaults..."
    settings_hash = CreatureWindow.sanitize_window_settings({})
    File.write(filename, settings_hash.to_yaml)
  else
    echo "Window settings: Unknown error loading profile (#{name})"
    settings_hash = nil
  end

  settings_hash
end

def CreatureWindow.save_window_settings(settings, name: Char.name)
  filename = CreatureWindow.window_settings_path(name: name)
  File.write(filename, CreatureWindow.sanitize_window_settings(settings).to_yaml)
end

# Set the grid column count (1-10, used when *cwflow is "row"), persist it,
# and refresh both windows. Returns the applied count.
def CreatureWindow.apply_grid_cols(window_settings, n)
  n = CreatureWindow.coerce_integer(n, min: 1, max: 10) || 2
  CreatureWindow.grid_cols = n
  window_settings["creaturewindow"] ||= {}
  window_settings["creaturewindow"]["grid_cols"] = n
  CreatureWindow.save_window_settings(window_settings)
  CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push("update_window")
  CreatureWindow.refresh_creature_windows(CreatureWindow.current_targets_now)
  n
end

# Set the grid row count (1-10, used when *cwflow is "col"), persist it,
# and refresh both windows. Returns the applied count.
def CreatureWindow.apply_grid_rows(window_settings, n)
  n = CreatureWindow.coerce_integer(n, min: 1, max: 10) || 8
  CreatureWindow.grid_rows = n
  window_settings["creaturewindow"] ||= {}
  window_settings["creaturewindow"]["grid_rows"] = n
  CreatureWindow.save_window_settings(window_settings)
  CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push("update_window")
  CreatureWindow.refresh_creature_windows(CreatureWindow.current_targets_now)
  n
end

# Reorders `items` for column-major rendering (top-to-bottom within a
# column first, then left-to-right to the next column) against a fixed
# row count, for use with a plain row-major each_slice(cols) renderer.
# Returns [ordered_items, cols] -- cols is derived from item count so
# every creature/hazard/dead-creature still gets shown (grid_rows caps
# rows per column, it never hides items).
def CreatureWindow.column_major_order(items, rows)
  return [items, 1] if items.empty?

  rows = [rows.to_i, 1].max
  cols = (items.size.to_f / rows).ceil
  ordered = Array.new(rows * cols)
  items.each_with_index do |item, idx|
    col = idx / rows
    row = idx % rows
    ordered[(row * cols) + col] = item
  end
  [ordered.compact, cols]
end

# Applies *cwflow: "row" needs no reordering (each_slice(grid_cols) is
# already left-to-right-then-wrap), "col" reorders against grid_rows.
# Returns [ordered_items, cols] ready for items.each_slice(cols).
def CreatureWindow.flow_grid(items)
  if CreatureWindow.grid_flow == "col"
    CreatureWindow.column_major_order(items, CreatureWindow.grid_rows)
  else
    [items, [CreatureWindow.grid_cols, 1].max]
  end
end

# Renders a single creature grid cell -- a live "target ##<id>" link for
# an alive creature, or a "loot ##<id>" link (via saga_dead_label) for a
# dead one (used when *cwdead keeps dead creatures inline). Shared by the
# live grid, the inline-dead-merged grid, and the separate dead-creature
# grid.
def CreatureWindow.creature_cell_xml(id, creature, left, top, width, height, is_target)
  if creature.status.to_s.downcase == 'dead'
    noun = CreatureWindow.with_sequence_number(creature.noun.to_s, creature.id)
    label = CreatureWindow.saga_dead_label(CreatureWindow.sanitize_xml(noun))
    return "<link id='#{id}' value='#{label}' cmd='loot ##{creature.id}' echo='loot ##{creature.id}' justify='bottom' left='#{left}' top='#{top}' width='#{width}' height='#{height}' />"
  end

  status = CreatureWindow.creature_status_fix(creature.status, creature.name, creature.id)
  base_label = CreatureWindow.saga_wrap_status(creature.noun, status)
  label_value = CreatureWindow.with_sequence_number(base_label, creature.id)
  cmd = "target ##{creature.id}"
  display = CreatureWindow.finalize_creature_label(label_value, is_target)
  name_left = !is_target && CreatureWindow.riding?(creature.id) && $frontend == 'saga' && CreatureWindow.saga_status_mode == 'emoji' ? left + 22 : left
  name_width = width - (name_left - left)
  rider_xml = CreatureWindow.riding_marker_xml(id, creature.id, left, top, height, cmd, is_target)
  "#{rider_xml}<link id='#{id}' value='#{display}' cmd='#{cmd}' echo='Targeting #{CreatureWindow.sanitize_xml(creature.name)}' justify='bottom' left='#{name_left}' top='#{top}' width='#{name_width}' height='#{height}' />"
end

def CreatureWindow.claim_label
  defined?(Lich::Claim) && Lich::Claim.mine? ? "True" : "False"
rescue StandardError
  "False"
end

def CreatureWindow.claim_status_text
  display_claim ? " CLAIM: #{claim_label}" : ""
end

# *cwtest -- fake data for visually testing layouts (mainly *cwcustom1's
# 3-column redesign) without needing a real room full of creatures and
# hazards. Only needs id/noun/name/status/contents -- every real method
# called on a target/hazard elsewhere in this file (creature_status_fix,
# saga_wrap_status, with_sequence_number, riding?, hazard_action_for,
# etc.) only ever touches those. IDs start at a large negative offset so
# they can never collide with a real GameObj id.
CW_TEST_CREATURE = Struct.new(:id, :noun, :name, :status, :contents)

CW_TEST_STATUSES = [nil, nil, nil, "kneeling", "prone", "stunned", "webbed", "rooted", "held", "frozen", "calmed", "unconscious", "flying", "dead"].freeze
CW_TEST_CREATURE_NOUNS = %w[rat bat wolf ghast troll orc goblin spider snake bear lion tiger ogre imp wraith zombie skeleton golem harpy wyvern kobold].freeze
CW_TEST_HAZARD_NAMES = ["acidic cloud of mist", "glimmering boltstone apparatus", "pale hovering runestone", "unearthly silvery blue globe", "spiraling ghostly rift", "windy vortex", "gigantic sticky web", "swirling sandstorm", "black metal bomb", "black void", "raging whirlwind"].freeze

def CreatureWindow.generate_test_data!
  @cw_test_targets = (1..24).map do |i|
    CW_TEST_CREATURE.new(-1000 - i, CW_TEST_CREATURE_NOUNS.sample, "test #{CW_TEST_CREATURE_NOUNS.sample} #{i}", CW_TEST_STATUSES.sample, [])
  end
  @cw_test_hazards = CW_TEST_HAZARD_NAMES.sample(3).map.with_index do |name, i|
    CW_TEST_CREATURE.new(-2000 - i, name, name, nil, [])
  end
  # XMLData.current_target_id reflects the real game, which never matches
  # a fake -1000-ish id, so *cwtest picks its own current target -- and a
  # fake UCS reading to go with it -- so *cwucs has something to render
  # while testing layouts.
  @cw_test_current_target_id = @cw_test_targets.first&.id
  @cw_test_ucs_position = [1, 2, 3].sample
  @cw_test_ucs_tierup = CreatureWindow::CW_UCS_ACTIONS.sample
end

# Real current-target id everywhere except *cwtest, where XMLData's real
# value would never match one of the fake -1000-ish creature ids and the
# current-target row (and now the UCS row) would just never appear.
def CreatureWindow.current_target_id_for_display
  return @cw_test_current_target_id if CreatureWindow.test_mode

  XMLData.current_target_id
end

# Live UCS (position tier 1-3 / tierup vulnerability) for the current
# target, sourced from Lich::Gemstone::Creature's own tracking (populated
# by Combat::Tracker as "You have good positioning against..."/"Strike
# leaves foe vulnerable to a followup X attack!" lines are parsed) so this
# window never has to parse combat text itself. Returns nil (not a
# both-nil hash) whenever there's nothing to show, so callers can use a
# plain truthiness check.
def CreatureWindow.ucs_data_for(target_creature)
  return nil unless target_creature

  if CreatureWindow.test_mode
    return { position: @cw_test_ucs_position, tierup: @cw_test_ucs_tierup }
  end

  creature = Creature[target_creature.id] rescue nil
  return nil unless creature

  position = creature.ucs_position
  tierup = creature.ucs_tierup
  return nil unless position || tierup

  { position: position, tierup: tierup }
rescue StandardError
  nil
end

def CreatureWindow.current_hazards
  return (@cw_test_hazards || []) if CreatureWindow.test_mode

  GameObj.loot.select do |obj|
    obj.name &&
      obj.name !~ /disk/i &&
      obj.name =~ /\b(acidic cloud of mist|glimmering boltstone apparatus|pale hovering runestone|cloud|unearthly silvery blue globe|spiraling ghostly rift|sandstorm|vine|black metal bomb|black void|windy vortex|web|whirlwind)\b/i
  end
end

# Centralizes the dead-creature lookup (previously inlined at every call
# site) so *cwtest's fake dead creatures show up everywhere real ones
# would -- GameObj.npcs returns nil (not []) when the room's registry is
# empty.
def CreatureWindow.dead_creatures_now
  if CreatureWindow.test_mode
    return (@cw_test_targets || []).select { |t| t.status.to_s.downcase == 'dead' }
  end

  (GameObj.npcs || []).select { |t| t.status.to_s.downcase == 'dead' }
end

# Same idea as dead_creatures_now, but the ALIVE half of *cwtest's fake
# pool -- everywhere GameObj.targets would normally be read.
def CreatureWindow.current_targets_now
  if CreatureWindow.test_mode
    return (@cw_test_targets || []).reject { |t| t.status.to_s.downcase == 'dead' }
  end

  GameObj.targets
end

def CreatureWindow.hazards_enabled?
  CreatureWindow.hazard_display_mode != "off"
end

def CreatureWindow.hazard_action_for(hazard_name)
  if defined?(CMan) && CMan.known?('Spell Cleave') && hazard_name =~ CreatureWindow::HAZARD_TARGET_PATTERN
    return :cleave
  end

  return 209 if Spell[209].known? && hazard_name =~ /web/i
  return 602 if Spell[602].known? && hazard_name =~ /glimmering boltstone apparatus/i
  return 1218 if Spell[1218].known? && hazard_name =~ CreatureWindow::HAZARD_TARGET_PATTERN
  return 1013 if Spell[1013].known? && hazard_name =~ CreatureWindow::HAZARD_TARGET_PATTERN
  return 119 if Spell[119].known? && hazard_name =~ CreatureWindow::HAZARD_TARGET_PATTERN
  return 418 if Spell[418].known? && hazard_name =~ CreatureWindow::HAZARD_TARGET_PATTERN

  nil
end

def CreatureWindow.perform_hazard_action(hazard)
  return unless hazard

  action = CreatureWindow.hazard_action_for(hazard.name)
  case action
  when :cleave
    fput("cman scleave ##{hazard.id}") if defined?(CMan) && CMan.affordable?('Spell Cleave')
  when Integer
    if Spell[action].affordable? && Spell[action].known?
      fput('release') if checkprep != 'None'
      fput("prep #{action}")
      fput("cast ##{hazard.id}")
    end
  end
end

def CreatureWindow.hazard_dialog_command(hazard)
  action = CreatureWindow.hazard_action_for(hazard.name)
  case action
  when :cleave
    ";e if defined?(CMan) && CMan.affordable?('Spell Cleave'); fput('cman scleave ##{hazard.id}'); end"
  when Integer
    ";e if Spell[#{action}].affordable? && Spell[#{action}].known?; fput('release') if checkprep != 'None'; fput('prep #{action}'); fput('cast ##{hazard.id}'); end"
  else
    nil
  end
end

CreatureWindow.settings = CreatureWindow.load_window_settings
CreatureWindow.settings ||= CreatureWindow.deep_merge_hash(CW_DEFAULT_WINDOW_SETTINGS, {})
CreatureWindow.window_settings = CreatureWindow.settings["creaturewindow"] ||= {}
CreatureWindow.use_gtk_window = CreatureWindow.window_settings["use_gtk_creaturewindow"] || false
CreatureWindow.display_bounty   = CreatureWindow.window_settings.fetch("display_bounty",   true) # default _on_ so you see an actual bounty line
CreatureWindow.display_avg_ttk  = CreatureWindow.window_settings.fetch("display_avg_ttk",  false)
CreatureWindow.display_last_ttk = CreatureWindow.window_settings.fetch("display_last_ttk", false)
CreatureWindow.display_kpm      = CreatureWindow.window_settings.fetch("display_kpm",      false)
CreatureWindow.display_claim    = CreatureWindow.window_settings.fetch("display_claim",    true)
CreatureWindow.target_next_mode = CreatureWindow.window_settings.fetch("target_next_mode", "off")
CreatureWindow.hazard_display_mode = CreatureWindow.window_settings.fetch("hazard_display_mode", "above")
CreatureWindow.saga_status_mode = CreatureWindow.window_settings.fetch("saga_status_mode", "unicode")
CreatureWindow.target_hp_mode = CreatureWindow.window_settings.fetch("target_hp_mode", "off")
CreatureWindow.target_marker_index = CreatureWindow.window_settings.fetch("target_marker_index", 0)
CreatureWindow.ucs_mode = CreatureWindow.window_settings.fetch("ucs_mode", false)
CreatureWindow.grid_cols        = CreatureWindow.window_settings.fetch("grid_cols", 2)
CreatureWindow.grid_rows        = CreatureWindow.window_settings.fetch("grid_rows", 8)
CreatureWindow.grid_flow        = CreatureWindow.window_settings.fetch("grid_flow", "row")
CreatureWindow.dead_inline      = CreatureWindow.window_settings.fetch("dead_inline", false)
CreatureWindow.header_mode      = CreatureWindow.window_settings.fetch("header_mode", "text")
CreatureWindow.custom_layout1   = CreatureWindow.window_settings.fetch("custom_layout1", false)
CreatureWindow.onslaught_timer_enabled = CreatureWindow.window_settings.fetch("onslaught_timer_enabled", false)
CreatureWindow.onslaught_counter_enabled = CreatureWindow.window_settings.fetch("onslaught_counter_enabled", false)
CreatureWindow.custom_icons     = CreatureWindow.window_settings.fetch("custom_icons", {})

CreatureWindow.gtk_available = begin
  require 'gtk3'
  true
rescue LoadError => e
  echo "Creaturewindow: GTK unavailable (#{e.message})."
  false
end

def CreatureWindow.gtk_enabled?
  CreatureWindow.gtk_available && CreatureWindow.use_gtk_window
end

def CreatureWindow.start_gtk_main_if_needed
  return unless CreatureWindow.gtk_available
  Gtk.main if Gtk.main_level == 0
end

def CreatureWindow.ensure_runtime_state!
  @cw_recent_lines ||= []
  @cw_creature_timestamps ||= {}
  @cw_creature_targeted ||= {}
  @cw_custom_status_cache ||= {}
  @cw_time_to_kill_list ||= []
  @cw_counted_dead_creature_ids ||= {}
  @cw_empyrean_counted_ids ||= {}
  @cw_empyrean_kill_count ||= 0
  @cw_empyrean_since_captain_counted_ids ||= {}
  @cw_empyrean_since_captain_kill_count ||= 0
  @cw_owned_room_kill_count ||= 0
  @cw_owned_room_kill_started_at ||= nil
  @cw_last_kill_activity_at ||= nil
  @cw_last_kill_time ||= nil
  @cw_last_kill_name ||= nil
  @cw_herb_workflow_running ||= false
  @cw_gem_workflow_running ||= false
  @cw_guild_workflow_running ||= false
  @cw_guard_workflow_running ||= false
  @cw_furrier_workflow_running ||= false
  @cw_skin_workflow_running ||= false
  @cw_creature_sequence ||= {}
  @cw_creature_sequence_next ||= 1
  @cw_sequence_room_id ||= nil
end

# Assign a persistent arrival-order number to every creature ID we haven't
# seen yet in the current room (living or dead). Numbers are keyed by the
# creature's unique ID, so they survive the creature dying and moving to the
# dead-creature list. Numbering resets when the room changes.
def CreatureWindow.assign_sequence_numbers!(npcs)
  ensure_runtime_state!

  room_id = Room.current.id
  if @cw_sequence_room_id != room_id
    @cw_sequence_room_id = room_id
    @cw_creature_sequence = {}
    @cw_creature_sequence_next = 1
  end

  npcs.each do |npc|
    next if @cw_creature_sequence.key?(npc.id)
    @cw_creature_sequence[npc.id] = @cw_creature_sequence_next
    @cw_creature_sequence_next += 1
  end
end

def CreatureWindow.sequence_number_for(id)
  ensure_runtime_state!
  @cw_creature_sequence[id]
end

# True for either inline mode ("numbers" or "no_numbers") -- i.e. whenever the
# current target should stay in its sequence slot instead of floating to top.
def CreatureWindow.target_next_inline?
  CreatureWindow.target_next_mode != "off"
end

# True only when arrival-order numbers should actually be displayed.
def CreatureWindow.target_next_numbers?
  CreatureWindow.target_next_mode == "numbers"
end

# Prefix a creature's display label with its arrival-order number, if known
# and if numbers are currently enabled. No-op (returns label unchanged)
# otherwise, so callers don't need to branch.
def CreatureWindow.with_sequence_number(label, id)
  return label unless CreatureWindow.target_next_numbers?
  seq = CreatureWindow.sequence_number_for(id)
  seq ? "#{seq}#{label}" : label
end

def CreatureWindow.push_recent_line(line)
  CreatureWindow.ensure_runtime_state!
  @cw_recent_lines << line
  @cw_recent_lines.shift if @cw_recent_lines.size > 25
end

@cw_startup_request_gtk = (CreatureWindow.use_gtk_window || !Frontend.supports_room_window?)

if Frontend.supports_room_window?
  _respond("<closeDialog id='CreatureWindow'/><openDialog type='dynamic' id='CreatureWindow' title='Creatures' target='CreatureWindow' resident='true'><dialogData id='CreatureWindow'></dialogData></openDialog>")
end

@cw_last_targets = []
@cw_last_targets_snapshot = nil
@cw_last_ui_refresh_at = Time.at(0)
@cw_creature_timestamps = {}
@cw_creature_status_changed = {}
@cw_time_to_kill_list = []
@cw_owned_room_kill_count = 0
@cw_owned_room_kill_started_at = nil
@cw_counted_dead_creature_ids = {}
@cw_last_kill_activity_at = nil
@cw_creature_targeted = {}
@cw_custom_status_cache = {}
@cw_creature_sequence = {}
@cw_creature_sequence_next = 1
@cw_sequence_room_id = nil
@cw_bounty_origin_room_id = Room.current.id
@cw_bounty_origin_npc_id = nil
@cw_bounty_origin_npc_noun = nil

CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE = Queue.new unless defined?(CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE)
CreatureWindow::TARGET_CMD_QUEUE = Queue.new unless defined?(CreatureWindow::TARGET_CMD_QUEUE)

@cw_recent_lines ||= []

# --- 1) Define your palettes ------------------------------------------------
CreatureWindow::PALETTES = {
  "Lich Dark Mode"     => { bg: "#2E2E2E", fg: "#DADADA" },
  "Lich Light Mode"    => { bg: "#E6E6E6", fg: "#202020" },
  "Middle Ground"      => { bg: "#333333", fg: "#FFFFFF" },
  "White on Black"     => { bg: "#000000", fg: "#FFFFFF" },
  "NQWhite on NQBlack" => { bg: "#111111", fg: "#f6f6f6" },
  "Black on White"     => { bg: "#FFFFFF", fg: "#000000" },
} unless defined?(CreatureWindow::PALETTES)

class CreatureWindowGtk
  @window       = nil
  @css_provider = nil
  @font_size    = nil
  # --- 2) Regenerate & apply CSS using the chosen palette --------------------
  def self.reload_css
    # Load persisted palette choice (default to "White on Black")
    settings = CreatureWindow.load_window_settings
    cw       = settings["creaturewindow"] ||= {}
    pal_name = cw["palette"] || "White on Black"
    colors   = CreatureWindow::PALETTES[pal_name]

    css = <<~CSS
      /* window frame */
      window#creaturewindow {
        background-color: #{colors[:bg]};
        color:            #{colors[:fg]};
        border:           0px solid #888888;
        border-radius:    4px;
      }

      window#creaturewindow .palette-btn,
      window#creaturewindow popover .palette-btn,
      window#creaturewindow GtkPopover .palette-btn {
        background: #{colors[:bg]};
        color: #{colors[:fg]};
      }

      window#creaturewindow .palette-btn:checked {
        background: #{colors[:bg]};
        color: #{colors[:fg]};
      }

      /* header bar */
      window#creaturewindow headerbar {
        background-color: #{colors[:bg]};
        color:            #{colors[:fg]};
      }

      /* header bar buttons / toggles */
      window#creaturewindow headerbar .header-toggle {
        margin:      0 2px;
        padding:     2px 4px;
        background-image: none;
        background-color: transparent;
        color:            #{colors[:fg]};
        border:           none;
        box-shadow:       none;
      }

      /* "on" state for toggles */
      window#creaturewindow headerbar .header-toggle:checked {
        background-color: #0a84ff; /* system blue */
        color:            #FFFFFF;
      }

      /* content labels */
      window#creaturewindow label {
        font-size: #{@font_size}px;
        color:     #{colors[:fg]};
      }

      /* scrolled area & flowbox */
      window#creaturewindow GtkScrolledWindow,
      window#creaturewindow GtkFlowBox {
        background-color: #{colors[:bg]};
      }
  window#creaturewindow .creature-btn,
  window#creaturewindow button.creature-btn {
        background: #{colors[:bg]};
        color: #{colors[:fg]};
    border-radius: 6px;
    border-width: 1px;
    border-style: solid;
    border-color: #888888;
    padding: 5px;
    font-weight: normal;
    transition: background 0.2s;
  }

  window#creaturewindow .creature-btn:active,
  window#creaturewindow button.creature-btn:active {
        background: #{colors[:bg]};
        color: #{colors[:fg]};
  }
    CSS

    @css_provider.load(data: css)
  end

  def self.create_main_window
    return if @window

    # --- load persisted settings ---
    settings = CreatureWindow.load_window_settings
    cw       = settings["creaturewindow"] ||= {}
    @font_size = cw["font_size"] || 14
    cw["palette"] || "White on Black"

    # --- build top-level window & HeaderBar ---
    @window = Gtk::Window.new(:toplevel)
    @window.set_name("creaturewindow")
    @window.set_border_width(10)
    @window.set_type_hint(Gdk::WindowTypeHint::UTILITY)
    @window.set_keep_above(true)

    header = Gtk::HeaderBar.new
    header.show_close_button = true
    header.title = "CW"

    # - Font size buttons -
    dec_btn = Gtk::Button.new(label: "A-")
    inc_btn = Gtk::Button.new(label: "A+")
    [dec_btn, inc_btn].each do |b|
      b.style_context.add_class("header-toggle")
      header.pack_start(b)
    end
    dec_btn.signal_connect("clicked") do
      @font_size = [@font_size - 1, 8].max
      fresh = CreatureWindow.load_window_settings
      fresh["creaturewindow"]["font_size"] = @font_size
      CreatureWindow.save_window_settings(fresh)
      reload_css
    end
    inc_btn.signal_connect("clicked") do
      @font_size = [@font_size + 1, 30].min
      fresh = CreatureWindow.load_window_settings
      fresh["creaturewindow"]["font_size"] = @font_size
      CreatureWindow.save_window_settings(fresh)
      reload_css
    end

    # - Palette selector -
    # build your MenuButton
    palette_btn = Gtk::MenuButton.new
    palette_btn.style_context.add_class("header-toggle")
    img = Gtk::Image.new(
      icon_name: "preferences-desktop-color-symbolic",
      icon_size: Gtk::IconSize::SMALL_TOOLBAR
    )
    palette_btn.set_image(img)
    palette_btn.set_always_show_image(true)

    # create the Popover and position it _before_ attaching it
    popover = Gtk::Popover.new(palette_btn)
    popover.set_position(Gtk::PositionType::TOP) # <- do this first

    # now fill your popover
    listbox = Gtk::Box.new(:vertical, 0)
    CreatureWindow::PALETTES.each_key do |name|
      btn = Gtk::ToggleButton.new(label: name)
      btn.style_context.add_class("header-toggle")
      btn.style_context.add_class("palette-btn")
      btn.active = (name == cw["palette"])
      btn.set_sensitive(true) # <- This ensures it's clickable
      btn.signal_connect("clicked") do
        settings = CreatureWindow.load_window_settings
        settings["creaturewindow"] ||= {}
        settings["creaturewindow"]["palette"] = name
        CreatureWindow.save_window_settings(settings)
        reload_css
      end
      listbox.add(btn)
    end
    popover.add(listbox)
    listbox.show_all

    # *only now* attach the popover to the button
    palette_btn.set_popover(popover)

    # and finally pack it into your header
    header.pack_end(palette_btn)

    @window.set_titlebar(header)

    # - CSS provider & initial styling -
    @css_provider = Gtk::CssProvider.new
    reload_css
    screen = Gdk::Screen.default
    Gtk::StyleContext.add_provider_for_screen(
      screen,
      @css_provider,
      Gtk::StyleProvider::PRIORITY_APPLICATION
    )

    # - Restore geometry -
    begin
      @window.resize(cw["width"], cw["height"]) if cw["width"] && cw["height"]
      @window.move(cw["x"], cw["y"]) if cw["x"] && cw["y"]
    rescue StandardError => e
      echo "Creaturewindow: Ignoring invalid saved GTK geometry (#{e.message})."
    end

    @scroll = Gtk::ScrolledWindow.new
    @scroll.set_policy(Gtk::PolicyType::AUTOMATIC, Gtk::PolicyType::AUTOMATIC)
    @scroll.set_hexpand(true)
    @scroll.set_vexpand(true)

    @flow = Gtk::FlowBox.new
    @flow.selection_mode        = :none
    @flow.max_children_per_line = [CreatureWindow.grid_cols, 1].max
    @flow.column_spacing        = 0
    @flow.row_spacing           = 0
    @flow.set_vexpand(true)
    @flow.valign                = Gtk::Align::START
    @flow.homogeneous           = false
    @scroll.add(@flow)

    @cw_bounty_box = Gtk::Box.new(:vertical)
    @cw_bounty_box.set_hexpand(true)
    @cw_bounty_box.set_vexpand(false)
    @cw_bounty_box.set_halign(Gtk::Align::START)
    @cw_bounty_box.set_valign(Gtk::Align::START)
    @cw_bounty_box.hide

    @main_box = Gtk::Box.new(:vertical)
    @main_box.pack_start(@cw_bounty_box, expand: false, fill: true, padding: 0)
    @main_box.pack_start(@scroll, expand: true, fill: true, padding: 0)
    @window.add(@main_box)

    # --- save geometry on move/resize ------------------------------------
    @ignore_next_configure = true
    @window.signal_connect("configure_event") do |_w, _ev|
      if @ignore_next_configure
        @ignore_next_configure = false
      else
        x, y = @window.position
        w, h = @window.size
        s = CreatureWindow.load_window_settings
        s["creaturewindow"] ||= {}
        s["creaturewindow"].merge!("x" => x, "y" => y, "width" => w, "height" => h)
        CreatureWindow.save_window_settings(s)
      end
      false
    end

    # --- replace the default destroy->Gtk.main_quit handler ---------------
    # 1) First, connect Gtk.main_quit *yourself* and capture its handler ID:
    default_quit_id = @window.signal_connect("destroy") do
      Gtk.main_quit
    end

    # 2) Immediately disconnect that handler:
    @window.signal_handler_disconnect(default_quit_id)

    # 3) Now install *your* destroy handler that only closes this window:
    @window.signal_connect("destroy") do
      @window = nil
      # NO Gtk.main_quit here!
    end

    @window.show_all
  end # <- end create_main_window

  # -----------------------------------------------------------------------
  # now the updater lives _outside_ of create_main_window
  def self.add_full_row(text = "")
    lbl = Gtk::Label.new(text)
    lbl.set_xalign(0)
    @flow.add(lbl)
    # Pad with blank cells so the header/line occupies a full row. Reads
    # back @flow's own current max_children_per_line (set once per
    # update_creatures call) rather than recomputing it, so header/hazard/
    # creature/dead rows all stay aligned to the same column count even
    # when *cwflow is "col" (where that count is derived dynamically).
    cols = [@flow.max_children_per_line, 1].max
    (cols - 1).times { @flow.add(Gtk::Label.new("")) }
  end

  def self.add_hazards(hazards)
    return if !CreatureWindow.hazards_enabled? || hazards.empty?

    add_full_row("")
    if CreatureWindow.header_mode == "text"
      add_full_row("Hazards: #{hazards.size}")
    elsif CreatureWindow.header_mode == "emoji"
      add_full_row("#{CreatureWindow.header_icon_gtk(:hazards)}#{hazards.size}")
    end
    hazards.each do |hazard|
      action = CreatureWindow.hazard_action_for(hazard.name)
      if action
        btn = Gtk::Button.new(label: hazard.name)
        btn.set_size_request(CreatureWindow::HAZARD_COLUMN_WIDTH, -1)
        btn.style_context.add_class("creature-btn")
        btn.signal_connect("clicked") do
          CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push(["hazard_action", hazard.id])
        end
        @flow.add(btn)
      else
        lbl = Gtk::Label.new(hazard.name)
        lbl.set_xalign(0)
        lbl.set_size_request(CreatureWindow::HAZARD_COLUMN_WIDTH, -1)
        @flow.add(lbl)
      end
    end
  end

  # Builds a single creature grid button -- a "target ##<id>" click for a
  # live creature, or a "loot ##<id>" click (labeled "(dead) ...") for a
  # dead one when *cwdead keeps dead creatures inline.
  def self.build_creature_button(t, bold:)
    is_dead = t.status.to_s.downcase == 'dead'
    if is_dead
      label = "(dead) #{CreatureWindow.with_sequence_number(t.noun.to_s, t.id)}"
    else
      st = CreatureWindow.creature_status_fix(t.status, t.name, t.id)
      label = st ? "#{t.noun} (#{st})" : t.noun.to_s
      label = CreatureWindow.with_sequence_number(label, t.id) if CreatureWindow.target_next_inline?
    end
    label = "**#{label}**" if bold

    btn = Gtk::Button.new(label: label)
    btn.set_size_request(CreatureWindow::CREATURE_COLUMN_WIDTH, -1)
    btn.style_context.add_class("creature-btn")
    btn.signal_connect("clicked") do
      CreatureWindow::TARGET_CMD_QUEUE << (is_dead ? "loot ##{t.id}" : "target ##{t.id}")
    end
    btn
  end

  # --- completely replace your old update_creatures with this ---
  def self.update_creatures(targets,
                            hazards:,
                            avg_ttk:,
                            last_ttk:,
                            kpm:,
                            bounty_task:,
                            bounty_status:,
                            bounty_action:,
                            display_avg_ttk:,
                            display_last_ttk:,
                            display_kpm:,
                            display_bounty:)
    return unless @window

    Gtk.queue do
      # A single column count governs header padding, hazards, the
      # creature grid, and the dead-creature grid for this whole render --
      # derived once here (from the live target list) exactly like the
      # Saga panel's own `cols` reference, so everything stays aligned.
      if CreatureWindow.grid_flow == "col"
        _, cols = CreatureWindow.column_major_order(targets, CreatureWindow.grid_rows)
        cols = [cols, 1].max
      else
        cols = [CreatureWindow.grid_cols, 1].max
      end
      @flow.max_children_per_line = cols

      # - first, clear & repopulate bounty_box -
      @cw_bounty_box.each { |c| @cw_bounty_box.remove(c) }
      if display_bounty
        @cw_bounty_box.show
        unless bounty_task == "No Bounty"
          [bounty_task, bounty_status].each do |txt|
            next if txt.nil? || txt.empty?
            lbl = Gtk::Label.new(txt)
            lbl.set_xalign(0)
            @cw_bounty_box.add(lbl)
          end
        end
        if bounty_action
          action_btn = Gtk::Button.new(label: bounty_action)
          action_btn.style_context.add_class("creature-btn")
          action_btn.signal_connect("clicked") do
            action_cmd = CreatureWindow.bounty_action_cmd
            if action_cmd == "*cwgem"
              CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push("run_gem_bounty_workflow")
            elsif action_cmd == "*cwherb"
              CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push("run_herb_bounty_workflow")
            elsif action_cmd == "*cwguild"
              CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push("run_guild_bounty_workflow")
            elsif action_cmd == "*cwguard"
              CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push("run_guard_bounty_workflow")
            elsif action_cmd == "*cwfurrier"
              CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push("run_furrier_bounty_workflow")
            elsif action_cmd == "*cwskin"
              CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push("run_skin_bounty_workflow")
            end
          end
          @cw_bounty_box.add(action_btn)
        end

        # <-- here:
        @cw_bounty_box.show_all
      else
        @cw_bounty_box.hide
      end

      # 4) Creature count
      @flow.children.each { |c| @flow.remove(c) }
      if CreatureWindow.header_mode == "text"
        add_full_row("Creatures: #{targets.size}#{CreatureWindow.claim_status_text}")
      elsif CreatureWindow.header_mode == "emoji"
        add_full_row("#{CreatureWindow.header_icon_gtk(:creatures)}#{targets.size}")
      end

      if display_avg_ttk
        add_full_row("Avg TTK: #{avg_ttk}")
      end

      if display_last_ttk
        add_full_row("Last TTK: #{last_ttk}")
      end

      if display_kpm
        add_full_row("Kills/Min: #{kpm}")
      end

      add_hazards(hazards) if CreatureWindow.hazard_display_mode == "above"

      # *cwdead: fold dead creatures into the live grid below instead of
      # listing them separately further down.
      dead_pool = CreatureWindow.dead_inline ? CreatureWindow.dead_creatures_now : []

      if CreatureWindow.target_next_inline?
        # Keep the current target inline with the others, in arrival order,
        # tagged with its sequence number and wrapped in asterisks -- instead
        # of floating it to its own row at the top.
        ordered_creatures = (targets + dead_pool).sort_by { |t| CreatureWindow.sequence_number_for(t.id) || Float::INFINITY }
        render_list = CreatureWindow.grid_flow == "col" ? CreatureWindow.column_major_order(ordered_creatures, CreatureWindow.grid_rows)[0] : ordered_creatures
        render_list.each { |t| @flow.add(build_creature_button(t, bold: t.id == XMLData.current_target_id)) }
      else
        # 5) Current target
        curr = targets.find { |t| t.id == XMLData.current_target_id }
        if curr
          st   = CreatureWindow.creature_status_fix(curr.status, curr.name, curr.id)
          txt  = st ? "#{curr.noun} (#{st})" : curr.noun.to_s
          add_full_row("**#{txt}**")
        end

        # Other living creatures (plus dead ones, if *cwdead is on) as buttons
        other = ((targets - [curr]) + dead_pool).sort_by { |t| CreatureWindow.sequence_number_for(t.id) || Float::INFINITY }
        render_list = CreatureWindow.grid_flow == "col" ? CreatureWindow.column_major_order(other, CreatureWindow.grid_rows)[0] : other
        render_list.each { |t| @flow.add(build_creature_button(t, bold: false)) }
      end

      # -- pad the current partial row so the dead header starts fresh --
      pad = (cols - (@flow.children.size % cols)) % cols
      pad.times { @flow.add(Gtk::Label.new("")) }

      add_hazards(hazards) if CreatureWindow.hazard_display_mode == "between"

      # 7) Dead creatures - force a full row for the count, then list
      # (skipped entirely when *cwdead already merged them into the grid
      # above).
      unless CreatureWindow.dead_inline
        dead = CreatureWindow.dead_creatures_now
        add_full_row("")
        if CreatureWindow.header_mode == "text"
          add_full_row("Dead Creatures: #{dead.size}")
        elsif CreatureWindow.header_mode == "emoji"
          add_full_row("#{CreatureWindow.header_icon_gtk(:dead)}#{dead.size}")
        end
        dead_render_list = CreatureWindow.grid_flow == "col" ? CreatureWindow.column_major_order(dead, CreatureWindow.grid_rows)[0] : dead
        dead_render_list.each do |t|
          lbl = Gtk::Label.new(CreatureWindow.with_sequence_number(t.noun.to_s, t.id))
          lbl.set_xalign(0)
          lbl.set_size_request(CreatureWindow::CREATURE_COLUMN_WIDTH, -1)
          @flow.add(lbl)
        end
      end

      add_hazards(hazards) if CreatureWindow.hazard_display_mode == "below_dead"

      @flow.show_all
    end
  end
end

if @cw_startup_request_gtk
  if CreatureWindow.gtk_available
    respond ""
    respond " Initiating GTK window."
    respond ""
    respond " GTK Creaturewindow is active."
    respond ""
    Gtk.queue { CreatureWindowGtk.create_main_window }
    Thread.new { CreatureWindow.start_gtk_main_if_needed }
  else
    CreatureWindow.use_gtk_window = false
    CreatureWindow.window_settings["use_gtk_creaturewindow"] = false
    fresh = CreatureWindow.load_window_settings
    fresh["creaturewindow"]["use_gtk_creaturewindow"] = false
    CreatureWindow.save_window_settings(fresh)
    respond ""
    respond " GTK Creaturewindow disabled: gtk3 gem not available."
    respond ""
  end
end

def CreatureWindow.creature_status_fix(status, name = nil, id = nil)
  CreatureWindow.ensure_runtime_state!
  custom_statuses = []

  if name&.match?(/cold wyrm/i)
    if @cw_recent_lines.any? { |line| line =~ /cold wyrm plummets toward the ground.*radiating wall of devastation/i }
      custom_statuses << "grounded"
    elsif @cw_recent_lines.any? { |line| line =~ /cold wyrm's muscles bunch and she launches herself into the air/i }
      custom_statuses << "airborne"
    elsif @cw_recent_lines.any? { |line| line =~ /Corruscations of color play along a silver-scaled cold wyrm's scaled hide.*disrupting the attack/i }
      custom_statuses << "shielded"
    end

    # Cache logic
    if !custom_statuses.empty? && id
      @cw_custom_status_cache[id] = custom_statuses
    elsif id && @cw_custom_status_cache.key?(id)
      custom_statuses = @cw_custom_status_cache[id]
    end
  end

  # Text-parsed fallback (GameObj's "that appears X" room text). Still needed
  # for "held" and "frozen"/"terrified", which crtrStatus and the combat
  # message parser don't currently track under any canonical name -- but this
  # can only ever surface ONE word, since the room text itself only ever
  # names one status even when several are simultaneously active.
  text_status = case status
                when /calmed|calm/i then "calmed"
                when /frozen|immobilized|terrified/i then "frozen"
                when /held/i then "held"
                when /rooted/i then "rooted"
                when /unconscious|slumber|sleeping/i then "unconscious"
                when /webbed|webbing/i then "webbed"
                when /stunned/i then "stunned"
                when /prone|lying down|knocked to the ground/i then "prone"
                when /flying/i then "flying"
                when /sitting/i then "sitting"
                when /sounds/i then "sounds"
                when /kneeling/i then "kneeling"
                else nil
                end

  # crtrStatus-driven statuses (Creature[id].statuses) can hold several
  # simultaneously-true flags at once (e.g. stunned AND prone), unlike the
  # room text above which only ever mentions one. This is the primary,
  # multi-value source; text_status only adds words it can't otherwise cover.
  crtr_statuses = CreatureWindow.crtr_status_list(id)

  all_statuses = crtr_statuses.dup
  all_statuses << text_status if text_status
  all_statuses.concat(custom_statuses)
  all_statuses = all_statuses.compact.uniq
  all_statuses.empty? ? nil : all_statuses.join(" ")
end

# Live crtrStatus-driven status list for a creature (see
# CRTR_STATUS_DISPLAY_MAP), translated to creature_status_fix's icon-table
# vocabulary. Returns [] when there's no id or no matching Creature record.
def CreatureWindow.crtr_status_list(id)
  return [] unless id

  creature = Creature[id] rescue nil
  return [] unless creature

  (creature.statuses || []).map { |s| CreatureWindow::CRTR_STATUS_DISPLAY_MAP[s] || s }
end

# Values are XML numeric character references (not raw UTF-8 literals).
# Raw non-ASCII bytes embedded directly in a dialog control's value=''
# attribute don't survive Saga's dialog-control rendering intact; numeric
# character references are plain ASCII text that any XML-ish parser decodes
# reliably, same idea as how sanitize_xml already escapes & < > ' " for
# these same attributes.
CW_SAGA_STATUS_ICONS_UNICODE = {
  /\bcalmed\b/i      => "&#x262E;",   # U+262E peace symbol
  /\bfrozen\b/i      => "&#x2744;",   # U+2744 snowflake
  /\bheld\b/i        => "&#x2327;",   # U+2327 x in a rectangle box
  /\brooted\b/i      => "&#x2693;",   # U+2693 anchor
  /\bunconscious\b/i => "&#x1DBB;&#x1DBB;&#x1DBB;", # U+1DBB x3 modifier letter small z
  /\bwebbed\b/i      => "&#x203B;",   # U+203B reference mark
  /\bstunned\b/i     => "&#x2739;",   # U+2739 six pointed black star
  /\bprone\b/i       => "&#x21D3;",   # U+21D3 downwards double arrow
  /\bflying\b/i      => "&#x21D1;",   # U+21D1 upwards double arrow
  /\bnatures_decay\b/i => "&#x273F;"  # U+273F black florette
}.freeze

CW_SAGA_STATUS_ICONS_EMOJI = {
  /\bcalmed\b/i      => "&#x1F60C;",           # U+1F60C relieved face
  /\bfrozen\b/i      => "&#x2744;&#xFE0F;",    # U+2744 snowflake
  /\bheld\b/i        => "&#x26D3;&#xFE0F;",    # U+26D3 chains
  /\brooted\b/i      => "&#x1FAB5;",           # U+1FAB5 wood log
  /\bunconscious\b/i => "&#x1F4A4;",           # U+1F4A4 zzz
  /\bwebbed\b/i      => "&#x1F578;&#xFE0F;",   # U+1F578 spider web
  /\bstunned\b/i     => "&#x26A1;",            # U+26A1 high voltage
  /\bprone\b/i       => "&#x2B07;&#xFE0F;",    # U+2B07 down arrow
  /\bflying\b/i      => "&#x1FABD;",           # U+1FABD wing
  /\bsitting\b/i     => "&#x1FA91;",           # U+1FA91 chair
  /\bkneeling\b/i    => "&#x1F9CE;",           # U+1F9CE person kneeling (from playerwindow)
  /\bsounds\b/i      => "&#x1F50A;",           # U+1F50A speaker high volume
  /\bnatures_decay\b/i => "&#x1F940;"          # U+1F940 wilted flower
}.freeze

CW_SAGA_DEAD_ICON_EMOJI = "&#x1F480;" # U+1F480 skull

def CreatureWindow.saga_status_icon_table
  case CreatureWindow.saga_status_mode
  when "emoji"
    CW_SAGA_STATUS_ICONS_EMOJI
  when "unicode"
    CW_SAGA_STATUS_ICONS_UNICODE
  else
    nil
  end
end

# Hazards:/Creatures:/Dead Creatures: header icons, per the user. Two
# separate tables since the two dialog flavors need two different
# encodings of the same glyph: the native/Saga dialog renders raw XML, so
# its icons are numeric character entities (must be concatenated onto
# already-sanitized text, never run through sanitize_xml themselves, same
# rule saga_status_display's own doc comment calls out); the GTK window is
# a real Gtk::Label with no entity parsing at all, so it needs the actual
# UTF-8 codepoint, written here as a \u{} escape to keep this source file
# itself plain ASCII.
CW_HEADER_ICONS_SAGA = {
  hazards:   "&#x26A0;&#xFE0F; ",
  dead:      "&#x1F480; ",
  creatures: "&#x1F400; "
}.freeze
CW_HEADER_ICONS_GTK = {
  hazards:   "\u{26A0}\u{FE0F} ",
  dead:      "\u{1F480} ",
  creatures: "\u{1F400} "
}.freeze

# Native/Saga dialog header icon -- "" unless this is actually a Saga
# client (the numeric-entity technique only works there; Wrayth/Stormfront
# would show the literal "&#x..." text). Only ever called from the *cwheaders
# "emoji" mode path, so no separate mode gate is needed here.
def CreatureWindow.header_icon(kind)
  return "" unless $frontend == 'saga'

  CreatureWindow::CW_HEADER_ICONS_SAGA[kind] || ""
end

# GTK window header icon. Not gated on $frontend, unlike header_icon above:
# GTK rendering doesn't go through Saga's text stream at all, so the real
# UTF-8 glyph renders the same regardless of which client the GTK window
# happens to be running alongside. Only ever called from the *cwheaders
# "emoji" mode path.
def CreatureWindow.header_icon_gtk(kind)
  CreatureWindow::CW_HEADER_ICONS_GTK[kind] || ""
end

# Icon + bare count, no label text or colon -- the combined-header-row
# format from *cwheaders' 3+-column layout, reused as-is by *cwcustom1.
def CreatureWindow.combined_header_value(count, icon_kind)
  "#{CreatureWindow.header_icon(icon_kind)}#{count}"
end

# Saga-panel-only status text -> XML-numeric-entity substitution, gated by
# CreatureWindow.saga_status_mode ("text"/"unicode"/"emoji", cycled via
# *cwstatus). Must run AFTER sanitize_xml (which would otherwise escape the
# '&' in these entity references). GTK and other frontends keep the plain
# text from CreatureWindow.creature_status_fix untouched.
def CreatureWindow.saga_status_display(sanitized_text)
  return sanitized_text if sanitized_text.nil? || $frontend != 'saga'

  table = CreatureWindow.saga_status_icon_table
  return sanitized_text unless table

  display = sanitized_text.dup
  table.each { |pattern, icon| display.gsub!(pattern, icon) }
  # Word-separating spaces survive substitution as gaps in front of and
  # between the now-adjacent icons (name-to-first-icon, and icon-to-icon for
  # multiple simultaneous statuses); collapse any whitespace that sits
  # directly in front of an entity reference so icons sit flush against the
  # name and each other. Only matches whitespace immediately before "&#x", so
  # a plain-text status word with no icon (e.g. custom_statuses) keeps its
  # separating space either side, since nothing after it is an entity.
  display.gsub!(/\s+&#x/, '&#x')
  display
end

# Prefixes a dead-creature label with the dead icon when in emoji mode.
# There's no dedicated unicode glyph for "dead" in the special-character
# set, so text/unicode modes leave the label as-is (the "Dead Creatures:"
# section header already conveys it).
def CreatureWindow.saga_dead_label(sanitized_text)
  return sanitized_text if sanitized_text.nil? || $frontend != 'saga'
  return sanitized_text unless CreatureWindow.saga_status_mode == "emoji"

  "#{CW_SAGA_DEAD_ICON_EMOJI}#{sanitized_text}"
end

# Enables the shared Combat::Tracker damage/UCS feed (lib/gemstone/combat)
# when *cwhp or *cwucs needs it, so current_hp/hp_percent reflect actual
# damage (instead of always reading full health) and Creature[id]'s
# ucs_position/ucs_tierup actually get populated. Combat::Tracker is a
# single per-character toggle shared with other scripts (e.g.
# eo_creaturebar.lic), so this only turns it ON when needed -- it's never
# turned back off from here, since other scripts/windows may also depend
# on it staying enabled.
def CreatureWindow.ensure_hp_tracking!
  return unless defined?(Combat::Tracker)
  return if Combat::Tracker.enabled?

  Combat::Tracker.enable!
  respond "Creaturewindow: enabled Combat::Tracker damage/UCS tracking (needed for *cwhp/*cwucs)."
rescue StandardError => e
  respond "Creaturewindow: could not enable Combat::Tracker (#{e.message})."
end

# `gameobj` is a GameObj entry (from GameObj.targets), which has no HP data
# of its own, so this looks up the matching Creature[] record.
def CreatureWindow.target_hp_creature(gameobj)
  return nil unless gameobj

  Creature[gameobj.id] rescue nil
end

# Live "###/### hp" readout (current/max) for the current target, driven by
# Combat::Tracker's damage tracking (see ensure_hp_tracking!). Returns nil
# when there's no Creature record or its max_hp isn't known.
def CreatureWindow.target_hp_line(gameobj)
  creature = CreatureWindow.target_hp_creature(gameobj)
  max_hp = creature&.max_hp
  return nil unless max_hp && max_hp > 0

  "#{creature.current_hp}/#{max_hp} hp"
end

# 10-segment HP bar for the current target, filled left-to-right by
# hp_percent (red = remaining, black = lost). Returns nil under the same
# conditions as target_hp_line.
def CreatureWindow.target_hp_bar(gameobj)
  creature = CreatureWindow.target_hp_creature(gameobj)
  max_hp = creature&.max_hp
  return nil unless max_hp && max_hp > 0

  filled = ((creature.hp_percent || 0) / 100.0 * CreatureWindow::TARGET_HP_BAR_SEGMENTS).round
  filled = filled.clamp(0, CreatureWindow::TARGET_HP_BAR_SEGMENTS)
  empty = CreatureWindow::TARGET_HP_BAR_SEGMENTS - filled

  (CreatureWindow::TARGET_HP_BAR_SEGMENT * filled) + (CreatureWindow::TARGET_HP_BAR_EMPTY_SEGMENT * empty)
end

# Appends a single target-HP row (bar segments + "###/### hp" text, both on
# one line when target_hp_mode is "bar"; just the text in "text" mode) to
# `output` at `left`/`top`, returning the updated [output, top] so callers
# can keep advancing their own layout. No-op (output/top unchanged) when the
# mode is "off" or there's no target/HP data.
#
# font='small' is the only working size lever here -- a numeric fontSize
# attribute exists on these dialog labels but is inert (confirmed unused by
# Saga's dialog renderer); font='small'/'normal' is the keyword attribute
# this codebase already relies on elsewhere (see exitwindow.lic's trash
# labels) for actually shrinking a label's text.
def CreatureWindow.append_target_hp_rows(output, target_creature, left, top, width, row_height)
  return [output, top] if CreatureWindow.target_hp_mode == "off" || !target_creature

  hp_line = CreatureWindow.target_hp_line(target_creature)
  return [output, top] unless hp_line

  parts = []
  if CreatureWindow.target_hp_mode == "bar" && (bar = CreatureWindow.target_hp_bar(target_creature))
    parts << bar
  end
  parts << CreatureWindow.sanitize_xml(hp_line)

  output += "<label id='target_creature_hp' value='#{parts.join(' ')}' justify='left' left='#{left}' top='#{top}' width='#{width * 2}' height='#{row_height}' font='small' />"
  top += row_height

  [output, top]
end

# Appends a single UCS row for the current target (*cwucs): "Pos: N" and
# "Tup: <action>" (headers dropped to bare "N     <action>" when
# header_mode is "off", matching how the Creatures:/Hazards:/Dead
# Creatures: headers already behave elsewhere in this file). Both values
# render as <link>s rather than <label>s -- per Saga 0.9.8, <label> text
# never tracks any font override/preset at all, only <link> does -- with
# the position link left inert (blank cmd) since it's display-only, while
# the Tup link, when a tierup is actually open, doubles as the action
# button for it (clicking it throws that attack at the current target).
# No-op (output/top unchanged) when the mode is off or nothing's tracked
# yet for this target.
def CreatureWindow.append_target_ucs_row(output, target_creature, left, top, width, row_height)
  return [output, top] unless CreatureWindow.ucs_mode && target_creature

  ucs = CreatureWindow.ucs_data_for(target_creature)
  return [output, top] unless ucs

  show_headers = CreatureWindow.header_mode != "off"
  pos_text = ucs[:position] ? ucs[:position].to_s : "-"
  tierup_text = ucs[:tierup] ? ucs[:tierup].capitalize : "-"

  pos_value = show_headers ? "Pos: #{pos_text}" : pos_text
  tup_value = show_headers ? "Tup: #{tierup_text}" : tierup_text

  pos_width = (width * 0.35).round
  tup_width = width - pos_width
  tup_left = left + pos_width

  output += "<link id='ucs_position' value='#{pos_value}' cmd='' echo='' justify='left' left='#{left}' top='#{top}' width='#{pos_width}' height='#{row_height}' />"

  tierup_cmd = ucs[:tierup] ? "#{ucs[:tierup]} ##{target_creature.id}" : ''
  tierup_echo = ucs[:tierup] ? "#{tierup_text} attempt" : ''
  output += "<link id='ucs_tierup' value='#{tup_value}' cmd='#{tierup_cmd}' echo='#{tierup_echo}' justify='left' left='#{tup_left}' top='#{top}' width='#{tup_width}' height='#{row_height}' />"

  top += row_height
  [output, top]
end

# Builds "name (status)" normally, but drops the parentheses when the Saga
# panel is about to render status as a unicode/emoji symbol instead of a
# word -- "Rat" plus the symbol reads better than "Rat (symbol)". The space
# kept here (rather than joining flush) is required for saga_status_display's
# \b word-boundary icon matching to find the first status word -- "Ratstunned"
# has no boundary between the two words, so the icon substitution would
# silently fail and leave the literal word behind. saga_status_display strips
# this space back out once it's confirmed an icon actually replaced the word.
def CreatureWindow.saga_wrap_status(name, status)
  return name.to_s if status.nil?
  return "#{name} #{status}" if $frontend == 'saga' && CreatureWindow.saga_status_mode != 'text'

  "#{name} (#{status})"
end

# Builds the final <link> value='' contents for a creature label: applies
# saga status-icon substitution, then (when is_target) marks it as the
# current target -- "**label**" bolding in text/unicode mode, or a single
# left-side icon (*cwtargetid) in Saga emoji mode instead of wrapping both
# sides. The icon has to be added AFTER sanitize_xml/status-icon
# substitution, since it's an XML numeric entity that sanitize_xml would
# otherwise escape (same reason saga_status_display runs post-sanitize).
def CreatureWindow.finalize_creature_label(label_value, is_target)
  emoji_target = is_target && $frontend == 'saga' && CreatureWindow.saga_status_mode == 'emoji'
  label_value = "**#{label_value}**" if is_target && !emoji_target

  display = CreatureWindow.saga_status_display(CreatureWindow.sanitize_xml(label_value))

  if emoji_target
    icon = CreatureWindow::TARGET_MARKER_ICONS[CreatureWindow.target_marker_index] || CreatureWindow::TARGET_MARKER_ICONS.first
    display = "#{icon}#{display}"
  end

  display
end

def CreatureWindow.riding?(creature_id)
  creature = Creature[creature_id] rescue nil
  creature&.crtr_flag?(:rider) == true
end

def CreatureWindow.riding_marker_xml(id_prefix, creature_id, left, top, row_height, cmd, is_target = false)
  return "" unless $frontend == 'saga' && CreatureWindow.saga_status_mode == 'emoji'
  return "" if is_target
  return "" unless CreatureWindow.riding?(creature_id)

  marker_height = [row_height / 2 + 2, 1].max
  mammoth = "&#x1F9A3;"
  first_id = "#{id_prefix}_rider_top"
  second_id = "#{id_prefix}_rider_bottom"
  marker = "<link id='#{first_id}' value='#{mammoth}' cmd='#{cmd}' echo='Riding' justify='left' left='#{left}' top='#{top}' width='20' height='#{marker_height}' />"
  marker << "<link id='#{second_id}' value='#{mammoth}' cmd='#{cmd}' echo='Riding' justify='left' left='#{left}' top='#{top + marker_height}' width='20' height='#{marker_height}' />"
  marker
end

def CreatureWindow.calculate_avg_ttk
  CreatureWindow.ensure_runtime_state!
  return "N/A" if @cw_time_to_kill_list.empty?
  avg_ttk = @cw_time_to_kill_list.sum / @cw_time_to_kill_list.size
  format("%.2f sec", avg_ttk)
end

def CreatureWindow.register_kill_activity
  CreatureWindow.ensure_runtime_state!
  @cw_last_kill_activity_at = Time.now
end

def CreatureWindow.reset_kill_metrics_if_inactive(dead_creatures, inactivity_seconds: 300)
  CreatureWindow.ensure_runtime_state!
  return if @cw_last_kill_activity_at.nil?
  return if (Time.now - @cw_last_kill_activity_at) < inactivity_seconds

  @cw_time_to_kill_list.clear
  @cw_last_kill_time = nil
  @cw_last_kill_name = nil
  @cw_owned_room_kill_count = 0
  @cw_owned_room_kill_started_at = nil
  @cw_counted_dead_creature_ids = dead_creatures.to_h { |creature| [creature.id, Time.now] }
  @cw_last_kill_activity_at = nil
end

def CreatureWindow.claim_owned_room?
  defined?(Lich::Claim) && Lich::Claim.mine?
rescue StandardError
  false
end

def CreatureWindow.track_owned_room_kills(dead_creatures)
  CreatureWindow.ensure_runtime_state!
  return unless CreatureWindow.claim_owned_room?

  @cw_owned_room_kill_started_at ||= Time.now
  current_dead_ids = dead_creatures.map(&:id)

  dead_creatures.each do |creature|
    creature_id = creature.id
    next if @cw_counted_dead_creature_ids.key?(creature_id)

    @cw_counted_dead_creature_ids[creature_id] = Time.now
    @cw_owned_room_kill_count += 1
    CreatureWindow.register_kill_activity
  end

  @cw_counted_dead_creature_ids.delete_if { |creature_id, _| !current_dead_ids.include?(creature_id) }
end

def CreatureWindow.empyrean_creature?(name)
  n = name.to_s.downcase
  CreatureWindow::EMPYREAN_KILL_NAMES.any? { |target| n.include?(target) }
end

# *cwicon empyrean/*cwicon saucer -- custom_icons["empyrean"/"saucer"]
# overrides EMPYREAN_ICON/EMPYREAN_SINCE_CAPTAIN_ICON when set, falling
# back to the built-in default otherwise. Both return an already-safe XML
# numeric-entity string (see set_custom_icon!), never a raw literal
# character, so callers can drop the result straight into a label value
# with no further sanitizing.
def CreatureWindow.empyrean_icon
  CreatureWindow.custom_icons["empyrean"] || CreatureWindow::EMPYREAN_ICON
end

def CreatureWindow.empyrean_since_captain_icon
  CreatureWindow.custom_icons["saucer"] || CreatureWindow::EMPYREAN_SINCE_CAPTAIN_ICON
end

# Converts a raw UTF-8 emoji (or short string of them, e.g. a base emoji
# plus a variation selector) into the XML-numeric-entity form every other
# icon in this file already uses (e.g. "&#x1F47D;"), then persists it under
# `slot` ("empyrean"/"saucer"). Literal non-ASCII characters don't reliably
# survive a Saga dialog's value='' attribute -- see the identical reasoning
# on EMPYREAN_ICON and every CW_SAGA_STATUS_ICONS_* table -- so the raw
# character a player pastes/clicks (e.g. from panelcontrol.lic's emoji
# picker) must be converted before it's ever stored or rendered. Returns
# the entity string on success, nil if `slot` isn't recognized or `emoji`
# has no characters to convert.
def CreatureWindow.set_custom_icon!(slot, emoji)
  return nil unless CreatureWindow::CUSTOM_ICON_SLOTS.include?(slot.to_s)

  entity = emoji.to_s.each_codepoint.map { |cp| "&#x#{cp.to_s(16).upcase};" }.join
  return nil if entity.empty?

  window_settings = CreatureWindow.load_window_settings
  CreatureWindow.custom_icons = CreatureWindow.custom_icons.merge(slot.to_s => entity)
  window_settings["creaturewindow"]["custom_icons"] = CreatureWindow.custom_icons
  CreatureWindow.save_window_settings(window_settings)
  entity
end

# *cwicon <slot> reset/default -- clears the override, reverting to the
# slot's built-in icon.
def CreatureWindow.reset_custom_icon!(slot)
  return false unless CreatureWindow::CUSTOM_ICON_SLOTS.include?(slot.to_s)
  return false unless CreatureWindow.custom_icons.key?(slot.to_s)

  window_settings = CreatureWindow.load_window_settings
  CreatureWindow.custom_icons = CreatureWindow.custom_icons.reject { |key, _| key == slot.to_s }
  window_settings["creaturewindow"]["custom_icons"] = CreatureWindow.custom_icons
  CreatureWindow.save_window_settings(window_settings)
  true
end

# True while the room title (e.g. "[Skyship, Deep Chambers]") includes
# "Skyship" -- per the user, only the flying-saucer "since last captain"
# counter is gated on this (it's specifically about the corridor-fighting
# phase between captain encounters); the permanent alien counter tracks
# every matching kill regardless of location.
def CreatureWindow.on_empyrean_skyship?
  # XMLData.room_title, not Room.current.title -- Room.current resolves
  # through Lich's static local map database (lib/common/map/map_gs.rb),
  # which the Hive Onslaught's Empyrean Skyship rooms are dynamically
  # instanced and never present in (confirmed: this was tried first and
  # broke the tracker entirely, since Room.current couldn't resolve these
  # rooms at all). XMLData.room_title is parsed live off the stream's own
  # subtitle every room change, independent of the map database, so it
  # stays accurate for unmapped/instanced content too.
  XMLData.room_title.to_s =~ /skyship/i ? true : false
rescue StandardError
  false
end

# Counts each matching dead creature exactly once (by ID), same
# dedup-by-ID technique as track_owned_room_kills, but its own independent
# counted-IDs set -- not gated on room claim, and never cleared by
# reset_kill_metrics_if_inactive, so it keeps counting across the whole
# Hive Onslaught event rather than resetting between kill lulls. Per the
# user: the alien counter tracks every matching kill anywhere, but the
# flying-saucer "since last captain" counter only counts kills made while
# on_empyrean_skyship? (it resets on every captain encounter's end -- see
# reset_empyrean_since_captain_count! -- which only ever makes sense
# aboard the skyship).
def CreatureWindow.track_empyrean_kills(dead_creatures)
  CreatureWindow.ensure_runtime_state!
  on_skyship = CreatureWindow.on_empyrean_skyship?

  dead_creatures.each do |creature|
    next unless CreatureWindow.empyrean_creature?(creature.name)

    unless @cw_empyrean_counted_ids.key?(creature.id)
      @cw_empyrean_counted_ids[creature.id] = true
      @cw_empyrean_kill_count += 1
    end

    # Same dead creature, but tracked in a separate dedup set so resetting
    # this counter (see reset_empyrean_since_captain_count!) never touches
    # the permanent alien-icon counter above.
    next unless on_skyship

    unless @cw_empyrean_since_captain_counted_ids.key?(creature.id)
      @cw_empyrean_since_captain_counted_ids[creature.id] = true
      @cw_empyrean_since_captain_kill_count += 1
    end
  end
end

# *cwonslaught counter's flying-saucer tracker -- fired from the
# DownstreamHook whenever a battle-worn Empyrean captain's encounter ends
# (flees or is killed -- see CAPTAIN_FLEE_PATTERN/CAPTAIN_DEFEATED_PATTERN),
# so it starts counting fresh for the next corridor-fighting phase.
def CreatureWindow.reset_empyrean_since_captain_count!
  CreatureWindow.ensure_runtime_state!
  @cw_empyrean_since_captain_counted_ids = {}
  @cw_empyrean_since_captain_kill_count = 0
end

# Resets BOTH Empyrean counters -- fired from parse_onslaught_text whenever
# the Gem Onslaught itself transitions from active to inactive (per the
# user), on the theory that once the whole event has ended there's nothing
# left to keep a running kill count toward. Pushes its own update_window
# rather than relying on the main loop's own before/after @cw_onslaught_active
# comparison (that comparison lives in the top-level loop, a different
# self/ivar table than parse_onslaught_text's CreatureWindow methods, so it
# never actually observes this change).
def CreatureWindow.reset_empyrean_counts!
  CreatureWindow.ensure_runtime_state!
  @cw_empyrean_counted_ids = {}
  @cw_empyrean_kill_count = 0
  CreatureWindow.reset_empyrean_since_captain_count!
  CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push("update_window")
end

def CreatureWindow.calculate_owned_room_kpm
  CreatureWindow.ensure_runtime_state!
  kill_count = @cw_owned_room_kill_count.to_i
  return "N/A" if @cw_owned_room_kill_started_at.nil? || kill_count.zero?

  elapsed_minutes = (Time.now - @cw_owned_room_kill_started_at) / 60.0
  return "N/A" if elapsed_minutes <= 0

  format("%.2f (%d)", kill_count / elapsed_minutes, kill_count)
end

def CreatureWindow.track_creature_kill(creature_id, creature_name)
  CreatureWindow.ensure_runtime_state!
  return unless @cw_creature_timestamps[creature_id]
  return unless @cw_creature_targeted[creature_id]

  time_alive = Time.now - @cw_creature_timestamps[creature_id]
  @cw_time_to_kill_list << time_alive

  @cw_last_kill_time = time_alive
  @cw_last_kill_name = creature_name
  CreatureWindow.register_kill_activity

  @cw_creature_timestamps.delete(creature_id)
  @cw_creature_targeted.delete(creature_id)
  @cw_custom_status_cache.delete(creature_id)
end

def CreatureWindow.sanitize_xml(value)
  value.to_s.gsub("&", "&amp;").gsub("<", "&lt;").gsub(">", "&gt;").gsub("'", "&apos;").gsub('"', "&quot;")
end

# Parses the plain-text "gem onslaught" response into either the
# "not active, here's when the next one starts" state or the "active
# right now, here's where and how long" state. Each captured component is
# optional (days/hours/minutes for the countdown, hours/minutes/seconds
# for the active-remaining line) since the game only includes the units
# that are actually nonzero.
def CreatureWindow.parse_onslaught_text(text)
  if text =~ /There is no Onslaught currently active\./i
    # Only an active->inactive transition resets the counters -- not every
    # poll while it's already inactive, and not the very first poll (where
    # @cw_onslaught_active starts as nil, not true).
    became_inactive = @cw_onslaught_active == true
    @cw_onslaught_active = false
    @cw_onslaught_location = nil
    @cw_onslaught_remaining = nil
    CreatureWindow.reset_empyrean_counts! if became_inactive
    m = text.match(/\(\s*(?:(\d+)\s*days?,?\s*)?(?:(\d+)\s*hours?,?\s*)?(?:(\d+)\s*minutes?,?\s*)?(?:(\d+)\s*seconds?)?\s*from now\)/i)
    if m
      total = (m[1].to_i * 86400) + (m[2].to_i * 3600) + (m[3].to_i * 60) + m[4].to_i
      @cw_onslaught_next_at = Time.now + total if total > 0
    end
  elsif text =~ /There is currently an Onslaught active somewhere around (.+?)\./i
    @cw_onslaught_active = true
    @cw_onslaught_location = Regexp.last_match(1)
    @cw_onslaught_next_at = nil
    m = text.match(/active for\s*(?:(\d+)\s*hours?,?\s*)?(?:(\d+)\s*minutes?,?\s*)?(?:(\d+)\s*seconds?)?\./i)
    if m
      @cw_onslaught_remaining = (m[1].to_i * 3600) + (m[2].to_i * 60) + m[3].to_i
    end
  end
end

# Active poll -- "gem onslaught" has no passively-tracked field the way
# checkbounty does, so this actively sends the command (silenced, like
# *exp refresh in exp_sagapanel.lic) and captures its response via a
# temporary DownstreamHook, swallowing only the specific status line it
# matched so it doesn't clutter the main window. Must run from the main
# loop's own thread (not from inside an UpstreamHook/DownstreamHook proc)
# since it uses put/silence_me/wait_until.
def CreatureWindow.refresh_onslaught!
  done = false
  seen_status = false
  hook_id = "cw_onslaught_capture"
  DownstreamHook.remove(hook_id) rescue nil
  DownstreamHook.add(hook_id, proc do |server_string|
    plain = server_string.gsub(/<[^>]*>/, '')
    if !seen_status && plain =~ /There is (?:no Onslaught currently active|currently an Onslaught active)/i
      CreatureWindow.parse_onslaught_text(plain)
      seen_status = true
      next(nil)
    # "gem onslaught" always answers with exactly these two lines, the
    # status line above followed immediately by this one -- confirmed
    # against real logs. Without also swallowing it, this poll (every
    # ONSLAUGHT_POLL_SECONDS while *cwonslaught timer is on) leaked
    # "Codices found this week: N/10" into the player's main window every
    # single time, since the hook used to remove itself the instant it saw
    # the status line, before this second line ever arrived. The prior
    # ^...\s*\z-anchored regex was too strict (Ruby's ^/$ are line-anchors,
    # not whole-string ones, but a stray embedded tag or trailing byte was
    # enough to break \z) -- match the phrase anywhere in the (tag-stripped)
    # line instead, the same loose style already used for the status line.
    elsif seen_status && plain =~ /Codices found this week: \d+\/\d+/i
      DownstreamHook.remove(hook_id)
      done = true
      next(nil)
    end
    server_string
  end)
  silence_me
  put "gem onslaught"
  silence_me
  # Bounded, not a bare wait_until -- an unexpected/missing response
  # (disconnect, unrecognized wording, or a future format change that
  # never emits the Codices line) must not hang the main loop forever.
  deadline = Time.now + 5
  sleep 0.1 until done || Time.now >= deadline
rescue StandardError => e
  echo "Creaturewindow onslaught refresh error: #{e.message}"
ensure
  DownstreamHook.remove(hook_id) rescue nil
end

# [header, detail] text for *cwonslaught timer -- shared by *cwcustom1's
# own layout and the normal (non-custom1) panel, so both render the exact
# same thing. [nil, nil] whenever the toggle is off, or on but @cw_onslaught_*
# hasn't been polled yet (nil until the first refresh_onslaught! -- see
# ONSLAUGHT_POLL_SECONDS in the main loop, which now polls regardless of
# *cwcustom1, only gated on this same toggle).
#
# No explicit timezone conversion needed for the "next onslaught" time
# despite the game's own message being Elanthian/Eastern-flavored text
# ("Day of the Huntress, Phoenatos 28th at 18:43 elven time") -- that
# absolute clock string is never parsed. refresh_onslaught! only reads the
# RELATIVE countdown in the same sentence ("... from now)") and adds those
# seconds to Time.now, which is already this system's local time regardless
# of what zone the server itself runs on, the same way a stopwatch reads
# correctly no matter what timezone you're in. Per the user, displayed as
# 12-hour clock time, not military.
def CreatureWindow.onslaught_texts
  return [nil, nil] unless CreatureWindow.onslaught_timer_enabled

  if @cw_onslaught_active
    header = "#{@cw_onslaught_location} Onslaught"
    detail = nil
    if @cw_onslaught_remaining
      hours = @cw_onslaught_remaining / 3600
      minutes = (@cw_onslaught_remaining % 3600) / 60
      detail = hours > 0 ? "Active for #{hours}h #{minutes}m" : "Active for #{minutes}m"
    end
    [header, detail]
  elsif @cw_onslaught_active == false
    [ "Next Onslaught", @cw_onslaught_next_at ? @cw_onslaught_next_at.strftime("%-I:%M %p on %a %-m/%-d") : nil ]
  else
    [nil, nil]
  end
end

def CreatureWindow.parse_bounty_from_checkbounty
  bounty_text = checkbounty

  # Clear everything first
  @cw_bounty_task_type = nil
  @cw_bounty_total = nil
  @cw_bounty_remaining = nil
  @cw_bounty_location = nil
  @cw_bounty_gem = nil
  @cw_bounty_skin = nil
  @cw_bounty_heirloom = nil
  @cw_bounty_target_creature = nil
  @cw_bounty_herb = nil
  @cw_bounty_kills_total = nil
  @cw_bounty_kills_remaining = nil
  @cw_bounty_turnin_npc = nil

  if bounty_text =~ /You are not currently assigned a task/i
    @cw_bounty_task_type = :none

  elsif bounty_text =~ /You have located (?:an? |a pair of |some )(.+?) and should bring/i
    @cw_bounty_task_type = :completeheirloom
    @cw_bounty_heirloom = bounty_text.match(/You have located (?:an? |a pair of |some )(.+?) and should bring/i)[1]

  elsif bounty_text =~ /report back to/i
    @cw_bounty_task_type = :completeguard
    @cw_bounty_turnin_npc = bounty_text.match(/report back to (.+?)\./i)&.[](1)

  elsif bounty_text =~ /made contact with the child you are to rescue/i &&
        bounty_text =~ /must get (?:him|her) back alive/i
    @cw_bounty_task_type = :completerescue
    @cw_bounty_turnin_npc = if bounty_text =~ /Icemule Trace gate guards?.*?(?:half(?:l|)ing )?Belle/i
                              "Icemule gate guard or Belle (Pinefar)"
                            else
                              "gate guard or Belle"
                            end

  elsif bounty_text =~ /child you were tasked to rescue is gone/i &&
        bounty_text =~ /task is failed/i
    @cw_bounty_task_type = :rescuefailed

  elsif bounty_text =~ /Guild to receive your reward/i
    @cw_bounty_task_type = :completeguild
  elsif bounty_text =~ /(visit|head|go|return)\s+(?:to\s+)?the Adventurer'?s Guild/i ||
        bounty_text =~ /talk to (?:the )?Guild Taskmaster/i
    @cw_bounty_task_type = :guildvisit

  elsif bounty_text =~ /task here from the town of (.+?)\.  It appears they have a bandit problem/i
    @cw_bounty_task_type = :bandit
    @cw_bounty_remaining = "Talk to guard for specifics."
    @cw_bounty_location = bounty_text.match(/task here from the town of (.+?)\.  It appears they have a bandit problem/i)[1]

  elsif bounty_text =~ /You have been tasked to suppress bandit activity (?:on|in the|in) (.+?) (?:near|between)/i && bounty_text =~ /You need to kill (\d+)/i
    @cw_bounty_task_type = :banditspecifics
    @cw_bounty_location = bounty_text.match(/You have been tasked to suppress bandit activity (?:on|in the|in) (.+?) (?:near|between)/i)[1]
    @cw_bounty_remaining = bounty_text.match(/You need to kill (\d+)/i)[1].to_i
  # ###################escort
  elsif bounty_text =~ /protective escort/i && bounty_text =~ /safety to (.+?) as/i && bounty_text =~ /(?:inside the |area just |south end )(.+?) and wait/i
    @cw_bounty_task_type = :escort
    @cw_bounty_escort = bounty_text.match(/(?:inside the |area just |south end )(.+?) and wait/i)[1]
    @cw_bounty_location = bounty_text.match(/safety to (.+?) as/i)[1]

  elsif bounty_text =~ /(?:town|outpost) of ([^\.]+)\.\s+The local gem dealer/i
    @cw_bounty_task_type = :gem
    @cw_bounty_remaining = "Talk to gem dealer for specifics."
    @cw_bounty_location = bounty_text.match(/(?:town|outpost) of ([^\.]+)\.\s+The local gem dealer/i)[1]
  # ###################GEM
  elsif bounty_text =~ /The gem dealer in (.+?),/i && bounty_text =~ /The gem dealer in .*? requesting (.+?)\./i && bounty_text =~ /You have been tasked to retrieve (\d+) (?:more )?of them/i
    @cw_bounty_task_type = :gemspecifics
    @cw_bounty_gem = bounty_text.match(/The gem dealer in .*? requesting (.+?)\./i)[1]
    @cw_bounty_remaining = bounty_text.match(/You have been tasked to retrieve (\d+) (?:more )?of them/i)[1].to_i
    @cw_bounty_location = bounty_text.match(/The gem dealer in (.+?),/i)[1]

  elsif bounty_text =~ /task here from the (?:town|outpost) of (.+?)\.  The local .*(?:alchemist|healer|herbalist)/i
    @cw_bounty_task_type = :herb
    @cw_bounty_remaining = "Talk to healer for specifics."
    @cw_bounty_location = bounty_text.match(/task here from the (?:town|outpost) of (.+?)\.  The local .*(?:alchemist|healer)/i)[1]
  # ###################FORAGE
  elsif bounty_text =~ /working on a concoction that requires (?:an?|a handful of|some)\s+(.+?)(?:\s+found\s+in|\.)/i &&
        bounty_text =~ /retrieve (\d+)\s+(?:more\s+)?sample(?:s)?/i
    @cw_bounty_task_type = :herbspecifics
    @cw_bounty_herb = bounty_text.match(/working on a concoction that requires (?:an?|a handful of|some)\s+(.+?)(?:\s+found\s+in|\.)/i)[1]
    @cw_bounty_remaining = bounty_text.match(/retrieve (\d+)\s+(?:more\s+)?sample(?:s)?/i)[1].to_i
    @cw_bounty_location = bounty_text.match(/found in (?:the )?(.+?) near/i)&.[](1) ||
                          bounty_text.match(/only grows in (?:the )?(.+?) near/i)&.[](1) ||
                          @cw_bounty_location
  elsif bounty_text =~ /concoction that requires (?:an?|some) (.+?) found/i && bounty_text =~ /found (?:in|on the) (?:the )?(.+?) near/i && bounty_text =~ /You have been tasked to retrieve (\d+) (?:more )?sample(?:s)?/i
    @cw_bounty_task_type = :herbspecifics
    @cw_bounty_herb = bounty_text.match(/concoction that requires (?:an?|some) (.+?) found/i)[1]
    @cw_bounty_remaining = bounty_text.match(/You have been tasked to retrieve (\d+) (?:more )?sample(?:s)?/i)[1].to_i
    @cw_bounty_location = bounty_text.match(/found (?:in|on the) (?:the )?(.+?) near/i)[1]

  elsif bounty_text =~ /The local furrier .* has an order to fill and wants our help/i && bounty_text =~ /of (.+?)\.  The local furrier/i
    @cw_bounty_task_type = :skin
    @cw_bounty_remaining = "Talk to furrier for specifics."
    @cw_bounty_location = bounty_text.match(/of (.+?)\.  The local furrier/i)[1]
  # ###################SKINNING
  elsif bounty_text =~ /You have been tasked to retrieve (\d+) .* of at/i && bounty_text =~ /retrieve \d+ (.+?) of at least/i && bounty_text =~ /quality\ for.*?(?:in|on\ the)\s+(.+?)\.\s+You/i
    @cw_bounty_task_type = :skinspecifics
    @cw_bounty_skin = bounty_text.match(/retrieve \d+ (.+?) of at least/i)[1]
    @cw_bounty_remaining = bounty_text.match(/You have been tasked to retrieve (\d+) .*? (?:more )?of at/i)[1].to_i
    @cw_bounty_location = bounty_text.match(/quality\s+for.*?(?:in|on\ the)\s+(.+?)\.\s+You/i)[1]
  # ###################CREATURE
  elsif bounty_text =~ /It appears they have a creature problem/i && bounty_text =~ /(?:town|outpost) of ([^\.]+)\.\s+It/i
    @cw_bounty_task_type = :creature
    @cw_bounty_remaining = "Talk to guard for specifics."
    @cw_bounty_location = bounty_text.match(/(?:town|outpost) of ([^\.]+)\.\s+It/i)[1]
  # ###################DANGEROUS
  elsif bounty_text =~ /hunt down and kill a particularly dangerous (.+?) that has/i && bounty_text =~ /(?:activity|territory) (?:in|on the) (?:the )?(.+?)(?: near)?\./i
    @cw_bounty_task_type = :dangerous
    @cw_bounty_target_creature = bounty_text.match(/hunt down and kill a particularly dangerous (.+?) that has/i)[1]
    @cw_bounty_location = bounty_text.match(/(?:activity|territory) (?:in|on the) (?:the )?(.+?)(?: near)?\./i)[1]
    @cw_bounty_kills_total = nil
    @cw_bounty_kills_remaining = nil
  # ###################KILL
  elsif bounty_text =~ /(?:tasked to|by) (?:.* )?(?:suppressing|suppress) (.+?) activity/i && bounty_text =~ /You need to kill (\d+)/i && bounty_text =~ /(?:activity|territory) (?:in|on the) (?:the )?(.+?)(?: near)?\./i
    @cw_bounty_task_type = :kill
    @cw_bounty_target_creature = bounty_text.match(/(?:tasked to|by) (?:.* )?(?:suppressing|suppress) (.+?) activity/i)[1]
    @cw_bounty_remaining = bounty_text.match(/You need to kill (\d+)/i)[1].to_i
    @cw_bounty_location = bounty_text.match(/(?:activity|territory) (?:in|on the) (?:the )?(.+?)(?: near)?\./i)[1]

  elsif bounty_text =~ /It appears (?:that a local resident|they need your help in tracking down some king of lost heirloom)/i && bounty_text =~ /(?:town|outpost) of ([^\.]+)\.\s+It/i
    @cw_bounty_task_type = :resident
    @cw_bounty_remaining = "Talk to guard for specifics."
    @cw_bounty_location = bounty_text.match(/(?:town|outpost) of ([^\.]+)\.\s+It/i)[1]
  # ###################RESCUE
  elsif bounty_text =~ /rescue/i && bounty_text =~ /the child fleeing from an? (.+?) in/i && bounty_text =~ /(?:in|on the) (?:the )?(.+?) near/i
    @cw_bounty_task_type = :rescue
    @cw_bounty_target_creature = bounty_text.match(/the child fleeing from an? (.+?) in/i)[1]
    @cw_bounty_location = bounty_text.match(/(?:in|on the) (?:the )?(.+?) near/i)[1]

  elsif bounty_text =~ /(?:town|outpost) of (.+?)\.  It appears they need your help in tracking down some kind of lost heirloom/i
    @cw_bounty_task_type = :heirloom
    @cw_bounty_remaining = "Talk to guard for specifics."
    @cw_bounty_location = bounty_text.match(/(?:town|outpost) of (.+?)\.  It appears they need your help in tracking down some kind of lost heirloom/i)[1]
  # ###################HEIRLOOM KILL
  elsif bounty_text =~ /tasked to recover (?:an|a pair of|a|some) (.+?) that/i &&
        bounty_text =~ /attacked by an? (.+?) (?:in the |in |on the )(.+?) (?: near)?/i &&
        bounty_text =~ /hunt down/i
    @cw_bounty_task_type = :heirloomkill
    @cw_bounty_heirloom = bounty_text.match(/tasked to recover (?:an|a pair of|a|some) (.+?) that/i)[1]
    creature_match = bounty_text.match(/attacked by an? (.+?) (?:in the |in |on the )(.+?) (?: near)?/i)
    @cw_bounty_target_creature = creature_match[1]
    @cw_bounty_location = creature_match[2]
  # ###################HEIRLOOM SEARCH
  elsif bounty_text =~ /tasked to recover (?:an|a pair of|a|some) (.+?) that/i &&
        bounty_text =~ /attacked by an? (.+?) (?:in the |in |on the )(.+?) (?: near)?/i &&
        bounty_text =~ /search/i
    @cw_bounty_task_type = :heirloomsearch
    @cw_bounty_heirloom = bounty_text.match(/tasked to recover (?:an|a pair of|a|some) (.+?) that/i)[1]
    creature_match = bounty_text.match(/attacked by an? (.+?) (?:in the |in |on the )(.+?) (?: near)?/i)
    @cw_bounty_target_creature = creature_match[1]
    @cw_bounty_location = creature_match[2]
  end
end

def CreatureWindow.bounty_task_line
  case @cw_bounty_task_type
  when :bandit
    "#{@cw_bounty_location} - Bandit Bounty"
  when :banditspecifics
    "#{@cw_bounty_location} - Bandit Bounty"
  when :escort
    "Escort - #{@cw_bounty_location}"
  when :gem
    "#{@cw_bounty_location} - Gem Bounty"
  when :gemspecifics
    "#{@cw_bounty_location} - Gem Bounty"
  when :herb
    "#{@cw_bounty_location} - Foraging Bounty"
  when :herbspecifics
    "#{@cw_bounty_location} - Foraging Bounty"
  when :skin
    "#{@cw_bounty_location} - Skinning Bounty"
  when :skinspecifics
    "#{@cw_bounty_location} - Skinning Bounty"
  when :creature
    "#{@cw_bounty_location} - Creature Bounty"
  when :kill
    "#{@cw_bounty_location} - Culling Bounty"
  when :dangerous
    "#{@cw_bounty_location} - Dangerous Bounty"
  when :resident
    "#{@cw_bounty_location} - Resident Bounty"
  when :rescue
    "#{@cw_bounty_location} - Rescue Bounty"
  when :heirloom
    "#{@cw_bounty_location} - Heirloom Bounty"
  when :heirloomkill
    "Find - #{@cw_bounty_heirloom}"
  when :heirloomsearch
    "Find - #{@cw_bounty_heirloom}"
  when :completeheirloom
    "Found! - #{@cw_bounty_heirloom}"
  when :completeguard
    nil
  when :completerescue
    "Rescue Complete!"
  when :rescuefailed
    "Rescue Failed"
  when :completeguild
    nil
  when :guildvisit
    "Guild Bounty"
  else
    "No Bounty"
  end
end

def CreatureWindow.bounty_status_line
  case @cw_bounty_task_type
  when :bandit
    "#{@cw_bounty_remaining}"
  when :banditspecifics
    "Kill #{@cw_bounty_remaining} - Bandit"
  when :escort
    "Start - #{@cw_bounty_escort}"
  when :gem
    "#{@cw_bounty_remaining}"
  when :gemspecifics
    "Find #{@cw_bounty_remaining} - #{@cw_bounty_gem}"
  when :herb
    "#{@cw_bounty_remaining}"
  when :herbspecifics
    "Find #{@cw_bounty_remaining} - #{@cw_bounty_herb}"
  when :skin
    "#{@cw_bounty_remaining}"
  when :skinspecifics
    "Find #{@cw_bounty_remaining} - #{@cw_bounty_skin}"
  when :creature
    "#{@cw_bounty_remaining}"
  when :kill
    "Kill #{@cw_bounty_remaining} - #{@cw_bounty_target_creature}"
  when :dangerous
    "Kill - #{@cw_bounty_target_creature}"
  when :resident
    "#{@cw_bounty_remaining}"
  when :rescue
    "Kill - #{@cw_bounty_target_creature}"
  when :heirloom
    "#{@cw_bounty_remaining}"
  when :heirloomkill
    "Kill - #{@cw_bounty_target_creature}"
  when :heirloomsearch
    "Search Near - #{@cw_bounty_target_creature}"
  when :completeheirloom
    "Return it to the guard!"
  when :completeguard
    if @cw_bounty_turnin_npc && !@cw_bounty_turnin_npc.empty?
      "Report to #{@cw_bounty_turnin_npc}"
    else
      "Report to the guard!"
    end
  when :completerescue
    if @cw_bounty_turnin_npc && !@cw_bounty_turnin_npc.empty?
      "Return child alive to #{@cw_bounty_turnin_npc}"
    else
      "Return child alive to the guard!"
    end
  when :rescuefailed
    "Report failure to the guild!"
  when :completeguild
    "Report to the guild!"
  when :guildvisit
    "Visit the Adventurer's Guild"
  else
    ""
  end
end

def CreatureWindow.bounty_state_signature
  [
    @cw_bounty_task_type,
    @cw_bounty_total,
    @cw_bounty_remaining,
    @cw_bounty_location,
    @cw_bounty_gem,
    @cw_bounty_skin,
    @cw_bounty_heirloom,
    @cw_bounty_target_creature,
    @cw_bounty_herb,
    @cw_bounty_turnin_npc
  ]
end

def CreatureWindow.refresh_bounty_ui
  CreatureWindow.parse_bounty_from_checkbounty
  CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push("update_window")
  @cw_last_bounty_check = Time.now
end

def CreatureWindow.ask_bounty_and_sync(npc, use_put: false, timeout: 1.5, interval: 0.15)
  return false unless npc

  before = CreatureWindow.bounty_state_signature
  ask_cmd = "ask ##{npc.id} about bounty"
  use_put ? put(ask_cmd) : fput(ask_cmd)

  changed = false
  deadline = Time.now + timeout
  loop do
    CreatureWindow.refresh_bounty_ui
    if CreatureWindow.bounty_state_signature != before
      changed = true
      break
    end
    break if Time.now >= deadline
    sleep interval
  end

  changed
end

def CreatureWindow.bounty_action_line
  if @cw_bounty_task_type == :none
    return "Guild Run Active..." if @cw_guild_workflow_running
    return "Get New Bounty (AdvGuild)"
  end

  if [:herb, :herbspecifics].include?(@cw_bounty_task_type)
    return "Herb Run Active..." if @cw_herb_workflow_running
    return "Forage Herbs (zzherb) and Turn In"
  end

  if [:gem, :gemspecifics].include?(@cw_bounty_task_type)
    return "Gem Run Active..." if @cw_gem_workflow_running
    return "Gem Bounty Workflow"
  end

  if [:guildvisit, :completeguild, :rescuefailed].include?(@cw_bounty_task_type)
    return "Guild Run Active..." if @cw_guild_workflow_running
    return "Go to AdvGuild and Ask About Bounty"
  end

  if @cw_bounty_task_type == :skin
    return "Furrier Run Active..." if @cw_furrier_workflow_running
    return "Go to Furrier and Ask About Bounty"
  end

  if @cw_bounty_task_type == :skinspecifics
    return "Skin Run Active..." if @cw_skin_workflow_running
    summary = CreatureWindow.skin_inventory_breakdown
    required = @cw_bounty_remaining.to_i
    required = 1 if required < 1
    return "Turn In Skins (#{summary[:singles]} singles, #{summary[:bundles]} bundles / need #{required})"
  end

  if [:bandit, :creature, :resident, :heirloom, :completeguard, :completeheirloom, :completerescue].include?(@cw_bounty_task_type)
    return "Guard Run Active..." if @cw_guard_workflow_running
    return "Go to AdvGuard and Ask About Bounty"
  end

  nil
end

def CreatureWindow.bounty_action_cmd
  return "*cwguild" if @cw_bounty_task_type == :none
  return "*cwherb" if [:herb, :herbspecifics].include?(@cw_bounty_task_type)
  return "*cwgem" if [:gem, :gemspecifics].include?(@cw_bounty_task_type)
  return "*cwguild" if [:guildvisit, :completeguild, :rescuefailed].include?(@cw_bounty_task_type)
  return "*cwfurrier" if @cw_bounty_task_type == :skin
  return "*cwskin" if @cw_bounty_task_type == :skinspecifics
  return "*cwguard" if [:bandit, :creature, :resident, :heirloom, :completeguard, :completeheirloom, :completerescue].include?(@cw_bounty_task_type)

  nil
end

def CreatureWindow.bounty_complete?
  [:completeguard, :completeguild, :completeheirloom, :completerescue].include?(@cw_bounty_task_type)
end

def CreatureWindow.npc_is_invalid_turnin_target?(npc)
  return true unless npc

  status = npc.respond_to?(:status) ? npc.status.to_s.downcase : ""
  type = npc.respond_to?(:type) ? npc.type.to_s.downcase : ""
  name = npc.name.to_s.downcase

  return true if status =~ /dead|gone/
  return true if type =~ /companion|familiar|pet/
  return true if name =~ /\bfamiliar\b/
  return true if name =~ /\banimated\b/ && name !~ /animated slush/

  false
end

def CreatureWindow.stop_active_nonhidden_scripts_for_turnin
  Script.running
        .find_all { |scr| scr && CreatureWindow::BOUNTY_WORKFLOW_STOP_SCRIPTS.include?(scr.name.to_s.downcase) }
        .each { |scr| scr.kill }
end

def CreatureWindow.collect_all_inv_items(items = GameObj.inv, depth: 0, max_depth: 3)
  return [] if depth > max_depth

  result = []
  items.each do |item|
    next unless item

    result << item
    if item.respond_to?(:contents) && item.contents
      result.concat(collect_all_inv_items(item.contents, depth: depth + 1, max_depth: max_depth))
    end
  end
  result
end

def CreatureWindow.heirloom_item_for_turnin
  heirloom_name = @cw_bounty_heirloom.to_s.strip
  return nil if heirloom_name.empty?

  CreatureWindow.collect_all_inv_items.find { |i| CreatureWindow.item_matches_bounty_name?(i.name.to_s, heirloom_name) }
end

def CreatureWindow.get_heirloom_for_turnin
  item = CreatureWindow.heirloom_item_for_turnin
  return unless item

  fput "get ##{item.id}"
end

def CreatureWindow.find_guild_taskmaster
  GameObj.npcs.find { |n| n && !CreatureWindow.npc_is_invalid_turnin_target?(n) && n.name.to_s =~ /Guild Taskmaster|taskmaster/i }
end

def CreatureWindow.prepare_turnin_hands
  put "stow all"
rescue StandardError
  nil
end

def CreatureWindow.run_guild_bounty_workflow
  return if @cw_guild_workflow_running

  @cw_guild_workflow_running = true
  begin
    CreatureWindow.stop_active_nonhidden_scripts_for_turnin

    Script.run("go2", "advguild")
    sleep 0.2 while running?("go2")
    CreatureWindow.prepare_turnin_hands

    npc = CreatureWindow.find_origin_turnin_npc
    npc ||= CreatureWindow.find_guild_taskmaster
    if npc
      CreatureWindow.ask_bounty_and_sync(npc)
    else
      respond "Creaturewindow: could not find a valid guild bounty NPC here."
    end
  rescue StandardError => e
    respond "Creaturewindow guild workflow error: #{e.class} - #{e.message}"
  ensure
    @cw_guild_workflow_running = false
    CreatureWindow.refresh_bounty_ui
  end
end

def CreatureWindow.find_advguard_npc
  if @cw_bounty_turnin_npc && !@cw_bounty_turnin_npc.to_s.empty?
    npc = GameObj.npcs.find do |n|
      n && !CreatureWindow.npc_is_invalid_turnin_target?(n) && n.name.to_s.downcase.include?(@cw_bounty_turnin_npc.to_s.downcase)
    end
    return npc if npc
  end

  npc = GameObj.npcs.find do |n|
    n && !CreatureWindow.npc_is_invalid_turnin_target?(n) &&
      n.name.to_s =~ /(?:^|\s)(?:town guard|gate guard|Guard Corporal Rex|guard corporal rex|Guard Private Witlass|guard private witlass|Corporal Sleetwood|corporal sleetwood|sergeant|city guardsman|guardsmen|guardsman|sentry|tavernkeeper)\b/i
  end
  npc ||= GameObj.npcs.find { |n| n && !CreatureWindow.npc_is_invalid_turnin_target?(n) && n.name.to_s =~ /Guild Taskmaster|taskmaster/i }
  npc
end

def CreatureWindow.hinterwilds_context?
  return true if @cw_bounty_location.to_s =~ /hinterwilds/i
  return true if checkbounty.to_s =~ /hinterwilds/i
  return true if checkarea.to_s =~ /hinterwilds/i
  return true if Room.current.title.to_s =~ /hinterwilds/i
  return true if @cw_last_location_probe.to_s =~ /hinterwilds/i

  false
rescue StandardError
  false
end

def CreatureWindow.refresh_location_probe_for_guard
  line = dothistimeout("location", 3, /current location is/i)
  @cw_last_location_probe = line.to_s
  line
rescue StandardError
  nil
end

def CreatureWindow.guard_go2_tag
  CreatureWindow.refresh_location_probe_for_guard
  CreatureWindow.hinterwilds_context? ? "advguard3" : "advguard"
end

def CreatureWindow.find_current_turnin_npc
  GameObj.npcs.find do |n|
    n && !CreatureWindow.npc_is_invalid_turnin_target?(n) &&
      n.name.to_s =~ CreatureWindow::BOUNTY_TURNIN_NPC_REGEX
  end
end

def CreatureWindow.run_guard_bounty_workflow
  return if @cw_guard_workflow_running

  @cw_guard_workflow_running = true
  begin
    CreatureWindow.stop_active_nonhidden_scripts_for_turnin

    Script.run("go2", CreatureWindow.guard_go2_tag)
    sleep 0.2 while running?("go2")
    CreatureWindow.prepare_turnin_hands

    CreatureWindow.get_heirloom_for_turnin if @cw_bounty_task_type == :completeheirloom

    npc = CreatureWindow.find_advguard_npc
    npc ||= CreatureWindow.find_current_turnin_npc
    if npc
      CreatureWindow.ask_bounty_and_sync(npc)
    else
      respond "Creaturewindow: could not find a valid bounty NPC here."
    end
  rescue StandardError => e
    respond "Creaturewindow guard workflow error: #{e.class} - #{e.message}"
  ensure
    @cw_guard_workflow_running = false
    CreatureWindow.refresh_bounty_ui
  end
end

def CreatureWindow.find_furrier_npc
  GameObj.npcs.find do |n|
    n && !CreatureWindow.npc_is_invalid_turnin_target?(n) &&
      n.name.to_s =~ /furrier|fur trader|Bramblefist|Delosa|Dagresar|dwarven clerk|pelt.*clerk|hide.*clerk/i
  end
end

def CreatureWindow.find_healer_bounty_npc
  GameObj.npcs.find do |n|
    n && !CreatureWindow.npc_is_invalid_turnin_target?(n) &&
      n.name.to_s =~ /alchemist|healer|herbalist|Sparkfinger|Maraene|Bumbleberry/i
  end
end

def CreatureWindow.run_furrier_bounty_workflow
  return if @cw_furrier_workflow_running

  @cw_furrier_workflow_running = true
  begin
    CreatureWindow.stop_active_nonhidden_scripts_for_turnin

    Script.run("go2", "furrier")
    sleep 0.2 while running?("go2")
    CreatureWindow.prepare_turnin_hands

    npc = CreatureWindow.find_furrier_npc
    npc ||= CreatureWindow.find_current_turnin_npc
    if npc
      CreatureWindow.ask_bounty_and_sync(npc)
    else
      respond "Creaturewindow: could not find a valid furrier NPC here."
    end
  rescue StandardError => e
    respond "Creaturewindow furrier workflow error: #{e.class} - #{e.message}"
  ensure
    @cw_furrier_workflow_running = false
    CreatureWindow.refresh_bounty_ui
  end
end

def CreatureWindow.run_skin_bounty_workflow
  return if @cw_skin_workflow_running

  unless @cw_bounty_task_type == :skinspecifics
    respond "Creaturewindow: no active skin-specific bounty."
    return
  end

  @cw_skin_workflow_running = true
  begin
    CreatureWindow.stop_active_nonhidden_scripts_for_turnin

    Script.run("go2", "furrier")
    sleep 0.2 while running?("go2")
    CreatureWindow.prepare_turnin_hands

    npc = CreatureWindow.find_furrier_npc
    npc ||= CreatureWindow.find_current_turnin_npc
    unless npc
      respond "Creaturewindow: could not find a valid furrier NPC here."
      return
    end

    CreatureWindow.sell_skins_to_npc(npc)
  rescue StandardError => e
    respond "Creaturewindow skin workflow error: #{e.class} - #{e.message}"
  ensure
    @cw_skin_workflow_running = false
    CreatureWindow.parse_bounty_from_checkbounty
    CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push("update_window")
  end
end

def CreatureWindow.capture_bounty_origin_context
  @cw_bounty_origin_room_id ||= Room.current.id
  npc = GameObj.npcs.find do |n|
    n && !CreatureWindow.npc_is_invalid_turnin_target?(n) && n.name =~ CreatureWindow::BOUNTY_TURNIN_NPC_REGEX
  end
  return unless npc

  @cw_bounty_origin_npc_id = npc.id
  @cw_bounty_origin_npc_noun = npc.noun
end

def CreatureWindow.capture_herb_origin_context
  @cw_bounty_origin_room_id ||= Room.current.id
  npc = CreatureWindow.find_healer_bounty_npc
  return unless npc

  @cw_bounty_origin_npc_id = npc.id
  @cw_bounty_origin_npc_noun = npc.noun
end

def CreatureWindow.capture_gem_origin_context
  @cw_bounty_origin_room_id ||= Room.current.id
  npc = GameObj.npcs.find do |n|
    n && !CreatureWindow.npc_is_invalid_turnin_target?(n) && n.name =~ CreatureWindow::GEM_TURNIN_NPC_REGEX
  end
  return unless npc

  @cw_bounty_origin_npc_id = npc.id
  @cw_bounty_origin_npc_noun = npc.noun
end

def CreatureWindow.find_origin_turnin_npc
  npc = nil
  npc = GameObj.npcs.find { |n| n && !CreatureWindow.npc_is_invalid_turnin_target?(n) && n.id == @cw_bounty_origin_npc_id } if @cw_bounty_origin_npc_id
  npc ||= GameObj.npcs.find { |n| n && !CreatureWindow.npc_is_invalid_turnin_target?(n) && n.noun.to_s.casecmp(@cw_bounty_origin_npc_noun.to_s).zero? } if @cw_bounty_origin_npc_noun
  npc ||= GameObj.npcs.find { |n| n && !CreatureWindow.npc_is_invalid_turnin_target?(n) && n.name =~ CreatureWindow::BOUNTY_TURNIN_NPC_REGEX }
  npc
end

def CreatureWindow.find_origin_healer_npc
  npc = nil
  if @cw_bounty_origin_npc_id
    found_by_id = GameObj.npcs.find { |n| n && !CreatureWindow.npc_is_invalid_turnin_target?(n) && n.id == @cw_bounty_origin_npc_id }
    npc = found_by_id if found_by_id && found_by_id.name.to_s =~ /alchemist|healer|herbalist|Sparkfinger|Maraene|Bumbleberry/i
  end
  if npc.nil? && @cw_bounty_origin_npc_noun
    found_by_noun = GameObj.npcs.find { |n| n && !CreatureWindow.npc_is_invalid_turnin_target?(n) && n.noun.to_s.casecmp(@cw_bounty_origin_npc_noun.to_s).zero? }
    npc = found_by_noun if found_by_noun && found_by_noun.name.to_s =~ /alchemist|healer|herbalist|Sparkfinger|Maraene|Bumbleberry/i
  end
  npc ||= CreatureWindow.find_healer_bounty_npc
  npc
end

def CreatureWindow.current_herb_name
  herb = @cw_bounty_herb.to_s.dup
  herb.sub!(/\A(?:some|an?|a handful of)\s+/i, "")
  herb.sub!(/\s+found\s+in\s+.+\z/i, "")
  herb.sub!(/\s+that\s+only\s+grows\s+in\s+.+\z/i, "")
  herb.strip
end

def CreatureWindow.current_zzherb_name
  CreatureWindow.current_herb_name
end

def CreatureWindow.current_herb_noun
  herb_name = CreatureWindow.current_herb_name
  return "" if herb_name.empty?

  # forage.lic expects the base noun as a separate arg.
  herb_name.split(/\s+/).last.to_s.gsub(/[^a-zA-Z'-]/, "").downcase
end

def CreatureWindow.herb_items_for_turnin
  herb_name = CreatureWindow.current_herb_name.downcase
  return [] if herb_name.empty?

  CreatureWindow.collect_all_inv_items.select { |i| i.name.to_s.downcase.include?(herb_name) }
end

def CreatureWindow.held_herb_for_turnin
  herb_name = CreatureWindow.current_herb_name.downcase
  return nil if herb_name.empty?

  [GameObj.left_hand, GameObj.right_hand].compact.find { |i| i.name.to_s.downcase.include?(herb_name) }
end

def CreatureWindow.herb_count_on_hand
  CreatureWindow.herb_items_for_turnin.inject(0) { |sum, item| sum + CreatureWindow.item_stack_count(item) }
end

def CreatureWindow.hand_in_herbs_to_npc(npc)
  return unless npc

  loop do
    held_herb = CreatureWindow.held_herb_for_turnin
    unless held_herb
      herb_item = CreatureWindow.herb_items_for_turnin.first
      break unless herb_item

      result = dothistimeout("get ##{herb_item.id}", 4, /You remove|You pick up|You need a free hand|Get what|What were you referring to/i)
      if result.to_s =~ /need a free hand/i
        CreatureWindow.prepare_turnin_hands
        result = dothistimeout("get ##{herb_item.id}", 4, /You remove|You pick up|You need a free hand|Get what|What were you referring to/i)
      end
      break if result.to_s =~ /Get what|What were you referring to/i

      held_herb = CreatureWindow.held_herb_for_turnin || CreatureWindow.find_item_in_hands_by_id(herb_item.id)
      break unless held_herb
    end

    give_result = dothistimeout(
      "give ##{held_herb.id} to ##{npc.id}",
      6,
      /I'll need \d+ more samples|finish my concoction|This looks perfect|What is it you're trying to give|moves out of your reach|You hand|accepts/i
    )
    break if give_result.to_s =~ /What is it you're trying to give|moves out of your reach/i
  end

  CreatureWindow.ask_bounty_and_sync(npc)
end

def CreatureWindow.go2_healer_room_for_turnin
  go2_target = CreatureWindow.hinterwilds_context? ? "advguard3" : "healer"
  Script.run("go2", go2_target)
  sleep 0.2 while running?("go2")
  CreatureWindow.prepare_turnin_hands
end

def CreatureWindow.find_origin_gem_npc
  npc = nil
  if @cw_bounty_origin_npc_id
    found_by_id = GameObj.npcs.find { |n| n && !CreatureWindow.npc_is_invalid_turnin_target?(n) && n.id == @cw_bounty_origin_npc_id }
    npc = found_by_id if found_by_id && found_by_id.name =~ CreatureWindow::GEM_TURNIN_NPC_REGEX
  end
  npc ||= GameObj.npcs.find { |n| n && !CreatureWindow.npc_is_invalid_turnin_target?(n) && n.name =~ CreatureWindow::GEM_TURNIN_NPC_REGEX }
  npc ||= GameObj.npcs.find { |n| n && !CreatureWindow.npc_is_invalid_turnin_target?(n) && n.name =~ CreatureWindow::BOUNTY_TURNIN_NPC_REGEX }
  npc
end

def CreatureWindow.current_gem_name
  @cw_bounty_gem.to_s.strip
end

def CreatureWindow.blocked_gemshop_room?
  current_uid_values = []
  if Room.current.respond_to?(:uid)
    current_uid_values = Array(Room.current.uid).compact.map { |u| u.to_s.sub(/\Au/i, "") }
  end

  return true if CreatureWindow::BLOCKED_GEMSHOP_ROOM_IDS.include?(Room.current.id.to_i)
  return true if CreatureWindow::BLOCKED_GEMSHOP_UIDS.any? { |uid| current_uid_values.include?(uid.to_s.sub(/\Au/i, "")) }
  return true if Room.current.title.to_s =~ CreatureWindow::BLOCKED_GEMSHOP_TITLES

  false
end

def CreatureWindow.goto_target_gemshop
  town = @cw_bounty_location.to_s.strip
  preferred = CreatureWindow::GEMSHOP_UID_BY_TOWN[town]

  if preferred
    Script.run("go2", preferred)
    sleep 0.2 while running?("go2")
    CreatureWindow.prepare_turnin_hands
    return
  end

  Script.run("go2", "gemshop")
  sleep 0.2 while running?("go2")
  CreatureWindow.prepare_turnin_hands
end

def CreatureWindow.normalize_bounty_item_name(name)
  name.to_s
      .downcase
      .gsub(/[^\w\s'-]/, " ")
      .gsub(/\A(?:a|an|some)\s+/, "")
      .gsub(/\A(?:piece|pieces|handful|handfuls|bundle|bundles)\s+of\s+/, "")
      .gsub(/\s+/, " ")
      .strip
end

def CreatureWindow.item_text_for_bounty_match(item)
  parts = []
  parts << item.name.to_s if item.respond_to?(:name)
  parts << item.noun.to_s if item.respond_to?(:noun)
  parts << item.after_name.to_s if item.respond_to?(:after_name)
  parts << item.full_name.to_s if item.respond_to?(:full_name)
  parts.compact.join(" ")
rescue StandardError
  item.to_s
end

def CreatureWindow.item_matches_bounty_name?(item_name, bounty_name)
  normalized_item = CreatureWindow.normalize_bounty_item_name(item_name)
  normalized_bounty = CreatureWindow.normalize_bounty_item_name(bounty_name)
  return false if normalized_item.empty? || normalized_bounty.empty?
  return true if normalized_item.include?(normalized_bounty) || normalized_bounty.include?(normalized_item)

  # Skin/material bounty descriptions often include a dropped adjective in inventory
  # (e.g. "niveous warg pelts" bounty vs "bundle of warg pelts" item).
  if (m = normalized_bounty.match(/\A\w+\s+(.+\b(?:pelt|pelts|skin|skins|scale|scales|plume|plumes|mane|manes|trunk|trunks|hide|hides)\b)\z/))
    return true if normalized_item.include?(m[1])
  end

  bounty_tokens = normalized_bounty.split(/\s+/)
  bounty_tokens.all? { |token| normalized_item.include?(token) }
end

def CreatureWindow.item_stack_count(item)
  if item.respond_to?(:quantity)
    qty = item.quantity.to_i
    return qty if qty > 0
  end
  if item.respond_to?(:count)
    qty = item.count.to_i
    return qty if qty > 0
  end
  if item.respond_to?(:stack_size)
    qty = item.stack_size.to_i
    return qty if qty > 0
  end
  if item.name.to_s =~ /\((\d+)\)\s*\z/
    qty = Regexp.last_match(1).to_i
    return qty if qty > 0
  end

  1
end

def CreatureWindow.gem_items_for_turnin
  gem_name = CreatureWindow.current_gem_name
  return [] if gem_name.empty?

  CreatureWindow.collect_all_inv_items.select do |i|
    CreatureWindow.item_matches_bounty_name?(CreatureWindow.item_text_for_bounty_match(i), gem_name)
  end
end

def CreatureWindow.gem_item_container?(item)
  item_name = item.name.to_s
  item_noun = item.noun.to_s
  item_after = item.respond_to?(:after_name) ? item.after_name.to_s : ""
  combined = "#{item_name} #{item_noun}".downcase

  (combined =~ /\b(?:bottle|jar|vial|flask)\b/i) ||
    item_after.downcase.include?("containing")
end

def CreatureWindow.gem_count_on_hand
  CreatureWindow.gem_items_for_turnin.inject(0) { |sum, item| sum + CreatureWindow.item_stack_count(item) }
end

def CreatureWindow.loose_gem_in_hands(excluding_id: nil)
  gem_name = CreatureWindow.current_gem_name
  hands = [GameObj.left_hand, GameObj.right_hand].compact
  hands.find do |item|
    next false if excluding_id && item.id == excluding_id

    CreatureWindow.item_matches_bounty_name?(CreatureWindow.item_text_for_bounty_match(item), gem_name)
  end
end

def CreatureWindow.find_item_in_hands_by_id(item_id)
  [GameObj.left_hand, GameObj.right_hand].compact.find { |item| item.id == item_id }
end

def CreatureWindow.shake_gem_container_for_turnin(container_item)
  return nil unless container_item

  fput "get ##{container_item.id}" unless CreatureWindow.find_item_in_hands_by_id(container_item.id)
  shake_result = dothistimeout(
    "shake ##{container_item.id}",
    4,
    /You give your .* a hard shake, causing|few times before you realize|You shake .* but nothing happens|You can't seem to get anything more out of/i
  )

  if shake_result =~ /You give your .* a hard shake, causing/i
    sleep 0.1
    return CreatureWindow.loose_gem_in_hands(excluding_id: container_item.id)
  end

  nil
end

def CreatureWindow.current_skin_name
  @cw_bounty_skin.to_s.strip
end

def CreatureWindow.skin_items_for_turnin
  skin_name = CreatureWindow.current_skin_name
  return [] if skin_name.empty?

  CreatureWindow.collect_all_inv_items.select { |i| CreatureWindow.item_matches_bounty_name?(i.name.to_s, skin_name) }
end

def CreatureWindow.skin_count_on_hand
  CreatureWindow.skin_items_for_turnin.inject(0) { |sum, item| sum + CreatureWindow.item_stack_count(item) }
end

def CreatureWindow.skin_inventory_breakdown
  singles = 0
  bundles = 0

  CreatureWindow.skin_items_for_turnin.each do |item|
    count = CreatureWindow.item_stack_count(item)
    if item.name.to_s =~ /bundle of/i
      bundles += count
    else
      singles += count
    end
  end

  { singles: singles, bundles: bundles }
end

def CreatureWindow.sell_skins_to_npc(npc)
  return unless npc

  target_count = @cw_bounty_remaining.to_i
  target_count = 1 if target_count < 1
  skin_ids = CreatureWindow.skin_items_for_turnin.take(target_count).map(&:id)

  skin_ids.each do |skin_id|
    fput "get ##{skin_id}"
    fput "sell ##{skin_id}"
  end

  CreatureWindow.ask_bounty_and_sync(npc, use_put: true)
end

def CreatureWindow.sell_gems_to_npc(npc)
  return unless npc

  target_count = @cw_bounty_remaining.to_i
  target_count = 1 if target_count < 1

  sold_count = 0
  active_container_id = nil
  loop do
    break if sold_count >= target_count

    gem_item = active_container_id ? CreatureWindow.find_item_in_hands_by_id(active_container_id) : nil
    gem_item ||= CreatureWindow.gem_items_for_turnin.first
    break unless gem_item

    if CreatureWindow.gem_item_container?(gem_item)
      active_container_id = gem_item.id
      loose_gem = CreatureWindow.shake_gem_container_for_turnin(gem_item)
      break unless loose_gem

      fput "sell ##{loose_gem.id}"
      sold_count += 1
    else
      active_container_id = nil
      stack_count = CreatureWindow.item_stack_count(gem_item)
      fput "get ##{gem_item.id}"
      fput "sell ##{gem_item.id}"
      sold_count += [stack_count, 1].max
    end
  end

  CreatureWindow.ask_bounty_and_sync(npc, use_put: true)
end

def CreatureWindow.run_herb_bounty_workflow
  return if @cw_herb_workflow_running

  unless [:herb, :herbspecifics].include?(@cw_bounty_task_type)
    respond "Creaturewindow: no active herb-specific bounty."
    return
  end

  @cw_herb_workflow_running = true
  begin
    CreatureWindow.stop_active_nonhidden_scripts_for_turnin

    needs_specifics = (@cw_bounty_task_type == :herb)
    needs_specifics ||= @cw_bounty_remaining.to_i < 1
    needs_specifics ||= CreatureWindow.current_zzherb_name.empty?
    needs_specifics ||= @cw_bounty_origin_npc_id.nil?
    needs_specifics ||= @cw_bounty_origin_room_id.nil?

    if needs_specifics
      CreatureWindow.go2_healer_room_for_turnin
      healer_npc = CreatureWindow.find_healer_bounty_npc
      unless healer_npc
        respond "Creaturewindow: could not find healer/alchemist for herb specifics."
        return
      end

      ask_result = dothistimeout("ask ##{healer_npc.id} about bounty", 8, /concoction that requires|retrieve \d+ samples|You have been tasked to retrieve/i)
      sleep 0.2 if ask_result.nil?

      # Give checkbounty a short window to reflect freshly asked specifics.
      8.times do
        CreatureWindow.refresh_bounty_ui
        break if @cw_bounty_task_type == :herbspecifics
        sleep 0.2
      end
      @cw_bounty_origin_room_id = Room.current.id
      @cw_bounty_origin_npc_id = healer_npc.id
      @cw_bounty_origin_npc_noun = healer_npc.noun
    else
      CreatureWindow.capture_herb_origin_context
    end

    unless @cw_bounty_task_type == :herbspecifics
      respond "Creaturewindow: could not fetch herb specifics from healer/alchemist."
      return
    end

    origin_room = @cw_bounty_origin_room_id || Room.current.id
    zzherb_name = CreatureWindow.current_zzherb_name
    needed_count = @cw_bounty_remaining.to_i
    needed_count = 1 if needed_count < 1
    on_hand_count = CreatureWindow.herb_count_on_hand
    find_count = [needed_count - on_hand_count, 0].max

    if running?("zzherb")
      respond "Creaturewindow: waiting for current zzherb run to finish..."
      sleep 0.2 while running?("zzherb")
    end

    unless File.exist?(File.join($script_dir, "zzherb.lic"))
      respond "Creaturewindow: zzherb.lic not found."
      return
    end

    if zzherb_name.empty?
      respond "Creaturewindow: no herb name parsed from bounty."
    elsif find_count > 0
      # zzherb accepts one arg string: "<herbname> <qty> [location optional]"
      Script.run("zzherb", %{#{zzherb_name} #{find_count}})
      sleep 0.2 while running?("zzherb")

      # Fallback for herb tags that require a determiner in Room.tags.
      if CreatureWindow.herb_count_on_hand < needed_count
        alt_name = "some #{zzherb_name}"
        Script.run("zzherb", %{#{alt_name} #{find_count}})
        sleep 0.2 while running?("zzherb")
      end

      # Additional fallback for herbs where scripts key off the base noun.
      if CreatureWindow.herb_count_on_hand < needed_count
        noun_name = CreatureWindow.current_herb_noun
        unless noun_name.empty?
          Script.run("zzherb", %{#{noun_name} #{find_count}})
          sleep 0.2 while running?("zzherb")
        end
      end
    end

    sleep 0.2 while running?("zzherb")

    if Room.current.id != origin_room
      Script.run("go2", origin_room.to_s)
      sleep 0.2 while running?("go2")
      CreatureWindow.prepare_turnin_hands
    end

    npc = CreatureWindow.find_origin_healer_npc
    if npc
      CreatureWindow.hand_in_herbs_to_npc(npc)
    else
      respond "Creaturewindow: turn-in NPC not found in origin room, heading to healer room."
      CreatureWindow.go2_healer_room_for_turnin
      healer_npc = CreatureWindow.find_origin_healer_npc
      if healer_npc
        CreatureWindow.hand_in_herbs_to_npc(healer_npc)
      else
        respond "Creaturewindow: could not find turn-in NPC in healer room."
      end
    end
  rescue StandardError => e
    respond "Creaturewindow herb workflow error: #{e.class} - #{e.message}"
  ensure
    @cw_herb_workflow_running = false
    CreatureWindow.parse_bounty_from_checkbounty
    CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push("update_window")
  end
end

def CreatureWindow.run_gem_bounty_workflow
  return if @cw_gem_workflow_running

  unless [:gem, :gemspecifics].include?(@cw_bounty_task_type)
    respond "Creaturewindow: no active gem bounty."
    return
  end

  @cw_gem_workflow_running = true
  begin
    CreatureWindow.stop_active_nonhidden_scripts_for_turnin

    CreatureWindow.capture_gem_origin_context

    CreatureWindow.goto_target_gemshop
    if CreatureWindow.blocked_gemshop_room?
      respond "Creaturewindow: blocked gemshop detected; aborting gem workflow."
      return
    end

    npc = CreatureWindow.find_origin_gem_npc
    unless npc
      respond "Creaturewindow: could not find gem dealer in gemshop."
      return
    end

    CreatureWindow.ask_bounty_and_sync(npc)

    unless @cw_bounty_task_type == :gemspecifics
      respond "Creaturewindow: could not fetch gem specifics from gem dealer."
      return
    end

    required = @cw_bounty_remaining.to_i
    required = 1 if required < 1
    on_hand = CreatureWindow.gem_count_on_hand

    if on_hand < required
      if running?("eloot")
        respond "Creaturewindow: waiting for current eloot run to finish..."
        sleep 0.2 while running?("eloot")
      end

      unless File.exist?(File.join($script_dir, "eloot.lic"))
        respond "Creaturewindow: eloot.lic not found."
        return
      end

      Script.run("eloot", "bounty")
      sleep 0.2 while running?("eloot")

      # eloot can move you; return to the correct gemshop before selling.
      CreatureWindow.goto_target_gemshop
      if CreatureWindow.blocked_gemshop_room?
        respond "Creaturewindow: blocked gemshop detected after eloot; aborting."
        return
      end
      npc = CreatureWindow.find_origin_gem_npc
      unless npc
        respond "Creaturewindow: could not find gem dealer after eloot run."
        return
      end
    else
      respond "Creaturewindow: found #{on_hand} matching gems on hand; skipping eloot bounty."
    end

    CreatureWindow.sell_gems_to_npc(npc)
  rescue StandardError => e
    respond "Creaturewindow gem workflow error: #{e.class} - #{e.message}"
  ensure
    @cw_gem_workflow_running = false
    CreatureWindow.refresh_bounty_ui
  end
end

def CreatureWindow.completed_amount
  return 0 unless @cw_bounty_total
  @cw_bounty_total - (@cw_bounty_remaining || 0)
end

# *cwcustom1 -- a fixed, special-purpose layout replacing the entire
# panel (not layered on top of the normal one), per the user. Three real
# side-by-side columns -- Creatures (narrow, ~1/4 width) | Bounty | Gem
# Onslaught -- not one shared text column:
#   Row 1: Creature count | Bounty Status (bounty_status_line -- the
#          field that actually carries specifics, e.g. "Find 8 - a small
#          gold nugget", once known)                        | Onslaught
#          header ("Next Onslaught" or "<Location> Onslaught"), with a
#          fixed right-edge slot for the Empyrean kill counter (alien
#          emoji + bare count -- see EMPYREAN_KILL_NAMES/
#          track_empyrean_kills, counts only those specific Hive Onslaught
#          creatures, regardless of room claim, never reset by inactivity)
#   Row 2: Dead count     | complete-task button (bounty_action_line/
#          bounty_action_cmd, clickable), same column as the status line
#          above it                                          | Onslaught
#          detail (local start time, 12-hour, or hours/minutes left with
#          seconds skipped) -- see onslaught_texts/refresh_onslaught!,
#          polled every ONSLAUGHT_POLL_SECONDS whenever *cwonslaught timer
#          is on (off by default), independent of whether this layout is
#          active -- the normal, non-custom1 panel shows the exact same
#          text via the same onslaught_texts call -- plus a fixed
#          right-edge slot, directly under row 1's alien counter, for the
#          flying-saucer "kills since last captain" counter
#          (EMPYREAN_SINCE_CAPTAIN_ICON) -- resets to 0 whenever a
#          battle-worn Empyrean captain's encounter ends (see
#          CAPTAIN_FLEE_PATTERN/CAPTAIN_DEFEATED_PATTERN/
#          reset_empyrean_since_captain_count!), counts back up again for
#          the next corridor-fighting phase
#   Row 3: Hazard count   | (blank)                          | (blank)
#   Row 4: hazard names, comma-separated, plain text, spanning the full
#          panel width (not confined to one of the three columns)
#   then the creature grid, hard-coded 3 columns, filled COLUMN-major
#   (down column 1 first, then column 2, then column 3) instead of the
#   row-major order every other layout in this script uses.
#   bounty_task_line ("Icemule Trace - Gem Bounty" etc.) is not shown at
#   all in this layout -- it's redundant with the count/icon on this same
#   row and never reflects specifics the way bounty_status_line does.
# Dead creatures are counted (the Row 2 count) AND stay in the creature
# list itself, in their same stable arrival-order slot, rather than
# disappearing once they die. Ignores every other display_*/
# hazard_display_mode/header_mode/grid_cols/grid_rows/grid_flow setting
# while active -- this
# is its own complete template, not a variation on the normal one.
def CreatureWindow.build_custom_layout1(targets, hazards, dead_creatures)
  out = String.new
  row_height = CreatureWindow::CREATURE_ROW_HEIGHT
  # Three real side-by-side columns per the user: Creatures/Bounty/
  # Onslaught. Creatures only ever holds short icon+number text, so it
  # gets about a quarter of the width the other two columns get.
  creature_col_left = 0
  creature_col_width = 90
  bounty_col_left = creature_col_width + 4
  bounty_col_width = ((CreatureWindow::BOUNTY_ROW_WIDTH - bounty_col_left) / 2.0).floor
  onslaught_col_left = bounty_col_left + bounty_col_width
  onslaught_col_width = CreatureWindow::BOUNTY_ROW_WIDTH - onslaught_col_left
  # Empyrean kill counter (alien emoji + bare count) gets a fixed slot at
  # the right edge of row 1, per the user -- the onslaught header text
  # gives up that much width so the two never overlap.
  empyrean_col_width = 40
  empyrean_col_left = onslaught_col_left + onslaught_col_width - empyrean_col_width
  onslaught_header_width = onslaught_col_width - empyrean_col_width - 4
  top = 0

  # bounty_status_line (not bounty_task_line) -- per the user, status
  # carries the actually-useful detail (e.g. "Find 8 - a small gold
  # nugget" once gem/herb/skin specifics are known); bounty_task_line/
  # bounty_action_line both stay generic ("Icemule Trace - Gem Bounty"/
  # "Gem Bounty Workflow") whether specifics are known or not, which is
  # why *cwcustom1 never looked like it updated -- it never had a slot
  # for the one field that actually changes. The complete-task button
  # (bounty_action_line) sits underneath it, same column.
  bounty_active = CreatureWindow.display_bounty && @cw_bounty_task_type != :none
  bounty_status_text = bounty_active && (line = CreatureWindow.bounty_status_line) && !line.empty? ? line : nil
  hazard_names_text = hazards.any? ? hazards.map { |hazard| hazard.name }.join(", ") : nil

  # NOT gated on bounty_active (task_type != :none) -- matches the normal
  # panel's own bounty_action_text gating exactly. bounty_action_line
  # returns "Get New Bounty (AdvGuild)" specifically when task_type IS
  # :none, so gating on bounty_active hid the get-a-new-bounty button
  # entirely whenever no task was active -- confirmed missing live.
  bounty_action_text = nil
  bounty_action_cmd = ''
  if CreatureWindow.display_bounty && (line = CreatureWindow.bounty_action_line)
    bounty_action_cmd = CreatureWindow.bounty_action_cmd
    bounty_action_text = CreatureWindow.bounty_complete? ? "Task Complete - Go to AdvGuard and Ask About Bounty" : line
  end

  # Gem Onslaught status -- see onslaught_texts (shared with the normal,
  # non-custom1 panel below).
  onslaught_header_text, onslaught_detail_text = CreatureWindow.onslaught_texts

  # *cwonslaught counter -- separate from the timer above. Kill tracking
  # itself (track_empyrean_kills) always runs regardless of this toggle, so
  # the count keeps accumulating in the background even while hidden.
  empyrean_count_text = CreatureWindow.onslaught_counter_enabled ? "#{CreatureWindow.empyrean_icon}#{@cw_empyrean_kill_count.to_i}" : nil

  out << "<label id='c1_creature_count' value='#{CreatureWindow.combined_header_value(targets.size, :creatures)}' justify='left' left='#{creature_col_left}' top='#{top}' width='#{creature_col_width}' height='#{row_height}' />"
  out << "<label id='c1_bounty_status' value='#{bounty_status_text ? CreatureWindow.sanitize_xml(bounty_status_text) : ''}' justify='left' left='#{bounty_col_left}' top='#{top}' width='#{bounty_col_width}' height='#{row_height}' wrap='true' />"
  out << "<label id='c1_onslaught_header' value='#{onslaught_header_text ? CreatureWindow.sanitize_xml(onslaught_header_text) : ''}' justify='left' left='#{onslaught_col_left}' top='#{top}' width='#{onslaught_header_width}' height='#{row_height}' />"
  out << "<label id='c1_empyrean_count' value='#{empyrean_count_text || ''}' justify='right' left='#{empyrean_col_left}' top='#{top}' width='#{empyrean_col_width}' height='#{row_height}' />"
  top += row_height

  # Flying-saucer "kills since last captain" counter (see
  # EMPYREAN_SINCE_CAPTAIN_ICON) sits directly under the permanent alien
  # counter above, per the user -- same right-edge slot, one row down.
  # onslaught_detail_text gives up the same width the header text did in
  # row 1, so the two never overlap.
  since_captain_text = CreatureWindow.onslaught_counter_enabled ? "#{CreatureWindow.empyrean_since_captain_icon}#{@cw_empyrean_since_captain_kill_count.to_i}" : nil
  out << "<label id='c1_dead_count' value='#{CreatureWindow.combined_header_value(dead_creatures.size, :dead)}' justify='left' left='#{creature_col_left}' top='#{top}' width='#{creature_col_width}' height='#{row_height}' />"
  out << "<link id='c1_bounty_action' value='#{bounty_action_text ? CreatureWindow.sanitize_xml(bounty_action_text) : ''}' cmd='#{bounty_action_cmd}' echo='Starting bounty workflow...' justify='left' left='#{bounty_col_left}' top='#{top}' width='#{bounty_col_width}' height='#{row_height}' />"
  out << "<label id='c1_onslaught_detail' value='#{onslaught_detail_text ? CreatureWindow.sanitize_xml(onslaught_detail_text) : ''}' justify='left' left='#{onslaught_col_left}' top='#{top}' width='#{onslaught_header_width}' height='#{row_height}' />"
  out << "<label id='c1_empyrean_since_captain' value='#{since_captain_text || ''}' justify='right' left='#{empyrean_col_left}' top='#{top}' width='#{empyrean_col_width}' height='#{row_height}' />"
  top += row_height

  out << "<label id='c1_hazard_count' value='#{CreatureWindow.combined_header_value(hazards.size, :hazards)}' justify='left' left='#{creature_col_left}' top='#{top}' width='#{creature_col_width}' height='#{row_height}' />"
  top += row_height

  out << "<label id='c1_hazard_list' value='#{hazard_names_text ? CreatureWindow.sanitize_xml(hazard_names_text) : ''}' justify='left' left='0' top='#{top}' width='#{CreatureWindow::BOUNTY_ROW_WIDTH}' height='#{row_height}' wrap='true' />"
  top += row_height # no extra spacer -- creature grid starts right after this, per the user

  cols = 3
  # Evenly split across the full panel width (matching BOUNTY_ROW_WIDTH,
  # not the general grid's CREATURE_COLUMN_WIDTH, which at 140 x 3 only
  # covers 420 of 460 and left the columns looking off-center) for
  # symmetric spacing across all 3 columns, per the user.
  col_width = CreatureWindow::BOUNTY_ROW_WIDTH / 3.0
  # Fixed 8 rows before spilling into the next column, per the user --
  # NOT the normal column-count filling rule (ceil(count/cols)), which
  # would instead spread creatures thin across all 3 columns whenever
  # there are fewer than 24 of them.
  rows_per_column = 8
  curr_target_id = CreatureWindow.current_target_id_for_display
  # Dead creatures stay in the list (per the user) instead of dropping out
  # the moment they die -- combined with the living targets and sorted by
  # the same arrival-order sequence number assign_sequence_numbers! (see
  # refresh_creature_windows) already assigns both groups together, so
  # each creature keeps its same slot in the list whether it's alive or
  # dead, rather than disappearing or jumping to some new position.
  all_creatures = (targets + dead_creatures).sort_by { |c| CreatureWindow.sequence_number_for(c.id) || Float::INFINITY }
  all_creatures.each_with_index do |creature, idx|
    column = idx / rows_per_column
    row = idx % rows_per_column
    left = (column * col_width).round
    creature_top = top + row * row_height

    if creature.status.to_s.downcase == 'dead'
      noun = CreatureWindow.with_sequence_number(creature.noun.to_s, creature.id)
      display = CreatureWindow.saga_dead_label(CreatureWindow.sanitize_xml(noun))
      cmd = "loot ##{creature.id}"
      echo_text = "loot ##{creature.id}"
    else
      status = CreatureWindow.creature_status_fix(creature.status, creature.name, creature.id)
      label_value = CreatureWindow.saga_wrap_status(creature.noun, status)
      display = CreatureWindow.finalize_creature_label(label_value, creature.id == curr_target_id)
      cmd = "target ##{creature.id}"
      echo_text = "Targeting #{CreatureWindow.sanitize_xml(creature.name)}"
    end

    out << "<link id='c1_creature_#{idx}' value='#{display}' cmd='#{cmd}' echo='#{echo_text}' justify='bottom' left='#{left}' top='#{creature_top}' width='#{col_width.round}' height='#{row_height}' />"
  end

  out
end

def CreatureWindow.push_creatures_to_window(targets)
  curr_target_id = CreatureWindow.current_target_id_for_display
  output = "<dialogData id='CreatureWindow' clear='t' >"

  # *cwcustom1 replaces the entire panel with its own fixed template --
  # see build_custom_layout1 -- and ignores every other display toggle
  # below (TTK/KPM, normal bounty layout, *cwheaders, hazard_display_mode
  # positioning, column count), so it short-circuits here before any of
  # that runs.
  if CreatureWindow.custom_layout1
    hazards = CreatureWindow.current_hazards
    dead_creatures = CreatureWindow.dead_creatures_now
    output += CreatureWindow.build_custom_layout1(targets, hazards, dead_creatures)
    output += "</dialogData>"
    _respond(output)
    return
  end

  current_top = 0
  row_height = CreatureWindow::CREATURE_ROW_HEIGHT

  # Avg TTK/Last TTK/Kills-per-Min/last-kill-name all always emit their
  # fixed ID (blank when hidden) for the same reason the bounty rows do
  # (see the comment above the bounty block below): this dialog's
  # clear='t' does not purge a previously-rendered element that's simply
  # left out of a later update, so a toggle-off would otherwise freeze
  # the last-shown value on screen forever instead of hiding it.
  avg_ttk_display = CreatureWindow.display_avg_ttk ? CreatureWindow.calculate_avg_ttk : nil
  output += "<label id='ttk' value='#{avg_ttk_display ? "Avg TTK: #{avg_ttk_display}" : ''}' justify='left' left='0' top='#{current_top}' />"
  current_top += row_height if avg_ttk_display

  last_ttk_display = CreatureWindow.display_last_ttk ? (@cw_last_kill_time ? format("%.2f sec", @cw_last_kill_time) : "N/A") : nil
  output += "<label id='last_ttk' value='#{last_ttk_display ? "Last TTK: #{last_ttk_display}" : ''}' justify='left' left='0' top='#{current_top}' />"
  current_top += row_height if last_ttk_display

  last_kill_name_display = (CreatureWindow.display_last_ttk && @cw_last_kill_name) ? @cw_last_kill_name : nil
  output += "<label id='last_kill_name' value='#{last_kill_name_display ? "(#{last_kill_name_display})" : ''}' justify='left' left='0' top='#{current_top}' />"
  current_top += row_height if last_kill_name_display

  kpm_display = CreatureWindow.display_kpm ? CreatureWindow.calculate_owned_room_kpm : nil
  output += "<label id='kpm' value='#{kpm_display ? "Kills/Min: #{kpm_display}" : ''}' justify='left' left='0' top='#{current_top}' />"
  current_top += row_height if kpm_display

  # *cwonslaught timer/counter -- independent of *cwcustom1 (per the user,
  # "let anyone use it"), so both also render here on the normal panel, all
  # on one line: alien counter, then flying-saucer counter, then the
  # onslaught timer text, per the user. .rjust reserves a fixed 4/3-digit
  # gap after each icon (alien kills can run higher over a whole event than
  # the since-last-captain count) so the icon that follows doesn't drift as
  # the numbers grow. onslaught_texts already returns [nil, nil] when the
  # timer toggle is off.
  # &#160; (nbsp) x3, not plain spaces -- gives clear breathing room between
  # the alien count, the saucer count, and the onslaught text on this one
  # shared line, per the user ("a bit more space").
  onslaught_line_gap = "&#160;&#160;&#160;"
  counter_segment = nil
  if CreatureWindow.onslaught_counter_enabled
    alien_count = @cw_empyrean_kill_count.to_i.to_s.rjust(4)
    saucer_count = @cw_empyrean_since_captain_kill_count.to_i.to_s.rjust(3)
    counter_segment = "#{CreatureWindow.empyrean_icon}#{alien_count}#{onslaught_line_gap}#{CreatureWindow.empyrean_since_captain_icon}#{saucer_count}"
  end

  onslaught_header_text, onslaught_detail_text = CreatureWindow.onslaught_texts
  # Sanitized BEFORE joining with counter_segment, not after -- counter_segment
  # carries raw XML numeric entities (&#x1F47D; etc.), and running the whole
  # combined string through sanitize_xml afterward would escape their '&'
  # into '&amp;', corrupting them into literal "&#x1F47D;" text instead of
  # rendering as the emoji (same ordering bug class documented for
  # verbwindow.lic's target-emoji labels -- entities must be appended AFTER
  # sanitizing, never sanitized themselves).
  onslaught_segment = onslaught_header_text ? CreatureWindow.sanitize_xml([onslaught_header_text, onslaught_detail_text].compact.join(" - ")) : nil

  onslaught_line_display = [counter_segment, onslaught_segment].compact.join(onslaught_line_gap)
  onslaught_line_display = nil if onslaught_line_display.empty?
  output += "<label id='onslaught' value='#{onslaught_line_display || ''}' justify='left' left='0' top='#{current_top}' />"
  current_top += row_height if onslaught_line_display

  # Blank forever -- these two used to be their own separate lines (now
  # folded into id='onslaught' above). clear='t' doesn't purge an omitted
  # element, so a leftover 'empyrean_count'/'empyrean_since_captain' from
  # before this change would otherwise stay frozen on screen indefinitely.
  output += "<label id='empyrean_count' value='' justify='left' left='0' top='#{current_top}' />"
  output += "<label id='empyrean_since_captain' value='' justify='left' left='0' top='#{current_top}' />"

  col_width = CreatureWindow::CREATURE_COLUMN_WIDTH
  creature_row_height = row_height
  hazard_col_width = CreatureWindow::HAZARD_COLUMN_WIDTH
  bounty_row_width = CreatureWindow::BOUNTY_ROW_WIDTH
  hazards = CreatureWindow.current_hazards
  # Computed early (not just right before the dead-creature grid further
  # down) so the count is available for the combined header row too.
  dead_creatures = CreatureWindow.dead_creatures_now

  # `cols` here is only the reference column count used for the hazard
  # grid and the header-row width math below -- the actual creature/dead
  # grids compute (and may reorder for) their own list via flow_grid.
  _, cols = CreatureWindow.flow_grid(targets)
  cols = [cols, 1].max

  # *cwheaders ("text"/"emoji"/"off") -- "emoji" always combines
  # Creatures/Hazards/Dead Creatures onto one compact icon+bare-count row;
  # "text" always shows full per-section labels; "off" hides them entirely.
  header_mode = CreatureWindow.header_mode
  combine_headers = header_mode == "emoji"
  hazard_count_text = (header_mode == "text" && CreatureWindow.hazards_enabled? && hazards.any?) ? "Hazards: #{hazards.size}" : nil
  creature_count_text = header_mode == "text" ? "Creatures: #{targets.size}#{CreatureWindow.claim_status_text}" : nil
  dead_count_text = header_mode == "text" ? "Dead Creatures: #{dead_creatures.size}" : nil
  header_value = lambda do |text|
    text ? CreatureWindow.sanitize_xml(text) : ''
  end

  # Combined-row format ("emoji" header mode) -- icon + bare count, no
  # label text or colon, Creatures/Hazards/Dead Creatures in that order,
  # and Hazards always shows (not gated on hazards_enabled?/hazards.any?
  # the way its own detail section is) so the row always has all three
  # segments.
  combined_creature_count = combine_headers ? targets.size : nil
  combined_hazard_count = combine_headers ? hazards.size : nil
  combined_dead_count = combine_headers ? dead_creatures.size : nil
  combined_value = lambda do |count, icon_kind|
    count ? CreatureWindow.combined_header_value(count, icon_kind) : ''
  end

  add_hazards_section = lambda do
    next unless CreatureWindow.hazards_enabled? && hazards.any?

    # Always emits id='hazard_count' when not already shown up in the
    # combined row (blank when headers are off) -- see the comment above
    # the Avg TTK block for why omitting it outright would leave stale
    # text frozen on screen instead of hiding it.
    unless combine_headers
      output += "<label id='hazard_count' value='#{header_value.call(hazard_count_text)}' justify='left' left='0' top='#{current_top}' />"
      current_top += row_height if hazard_count_text
    end

    top_offset = current_top / row_height
    hazards.each_slice(cols).with_index do |group, row|
      group.each_with_index do |hazard, col|
        left = col * hazard_col_width
        top = row_height * (row + top_offset)
        label = CreatureWindow.sanitize_xml(hazard.name)
        cmd = CreatureWindow.hazard_dialog_command(hazard)

        if cmd
          output += "<link id='hazard_#{row}_#{col}' value='#{label}' cmd=\"#{cmd}\" echo='#{label}' justify='left' left='#{left}' top='#{top}' width='#{hazard_col_width}' height='#{row_height}' />"
        else
          output += "<label id='hazard_#{row}_#{col}' value='#{label}' justify='left' left='#{left}' top='#{top}' width='#{hazard_col_width}' height='#{row_height}' />"
        end
      end
    end

    current_top = row_height * ((hazards.size.to_f / cols).ceil + top_offset) + row_height
  end

  # Bounty info -- always emits these three fixed IDs (blank when hidden)
  # rather than omitting them when off. Confirmed live: this dialog's
  # clear='t' does NOT purge a previously-rendered element that's simply
  # left out of a later update -- turning *cwbty off stopped the bounty
  # rows from updating but left their last-known text frozen on screen
  # indefinitely instead of disappearing. Explicitly blanking the same ID
  # forces the client to actually clear it.
  bounty_type_text = (line = CreatureWindow.bounty_task_line) if CreatureWindow.display_bounty && @cw_bounty_task_type != :none
  output += "<label id='bounty_type' value='#{bounty_type_text ? CreatureWindow.sanitize_xml(bounty_type_text) : ''}' justify='left' left='0' top='#{current_top}' width='#{bounty_row_width}' height='#{row_height}' />"
  current_top += row_height if bounty_type_text

  bounty_status_text = nil
  if CreatureWindow.display_bounty && @cw_bounty_task_type != :none && (line = CreatureWindow.bounty_status_line) && !line.empty?
    bounty_status_text = line
  end
  output += "<label id='bounty_status' value='#{bounty_status_text ? CreatureWindow.sanitize_xml(bounty_status_text) : ''}' justify='left' left='0' top='#{current_top}' width='#{bounty_row_width}' height='#{row_height}' />"
  current_top += row_height if bounty_status_text

  bounty_action_text = nil
  bounty_action_cmd = ''
  if CreatureWindow.display_bounty && (line = CreatureWindow.bounty_action_line)
    bounty_action_cmd = CreatureWindow.bounty_action_cmd
    bounty_action_text = CreatureWindow.bounty_complete? ? "Task Complete - Go to AdvGuard and Ask About Bounty" : line
  end
  output += "<link id='bounty_action' value='#{bounty_action_text ? CreatureWindow.sanitize_xml(bounty_action_text) : ''}' cmd='#{bounty_action_cmd}' echo='Starting bounty workflow...' justify='left' left='0' top='#{current_top}' width='#{bounty_row_width}' height='#{row_height}' />"
  current_top += row_height if bounty_action_text

  # Combined Creatures/Hazards/Dead Creatures row (3+ columns) -- per the
  # user, falls under the bounty display rather than above it.
  if combine_headers
    segment_width = (col_width * cols) / 3.0
    output += "<label id='total' value='#{combined_value.call(combined_creature_count, :creatures)}' justify='left' left='0' top='#{current_top}' width='#{segment_width}' height='#{row_height}' />"
    output += "<label id='hazard_count' value='#{combined_value.call(combined_hazard_count, :hazards)}' justify='left' left='#{segment_width.round}' top='#{current_top}' width='#{segment_width}' height='#{row_height}' />"
    output += "<label id='deadcount' value='#{combined_value.call(combined_dead_count, :dead)}' justify='left' left='#{(segment_width * 2).round}' top='#{current_top}' width='#{segment_width}' height='#{row_height}' />"
    current_top += row_height if combined_creature_count
  end

  add_hazards_section.call if CreatureWindow.hazard_display_mode == "above"

  # Creature count -- id='total' already shown in the combined row above
  # when combine_headers; otherwise emitted here on its own row (blank
  # when headers are off -- see the comment above the Avg TTK block).
  unless combine_headers
    output += "<label id='total' value='#{header_value.call(creature_count_text)}' justify='left' left='0' top='#{current_top}' />"
    current_top += row_height if creature_count_text
  end

  if CreatureWindow.target_next_inline?
    # Keep the current target inline with the others, in arrival order,
    # tagged with its sequence number and wrapped in asterisks -- instead of
    # floating it to a separate row at the top.
    if (target_creature = targets.find { |t| t.id == curr_target_id })
      unless @cw_creature_targeted[target_creature.id]
        @cw_creature_timestamps[target_creature.id] = Time.now
        @cw_creature_targeted[target_creature.id] = true
      end
    end

    ordered_creatures = targets.sort_by { |t| CreatureWindow.sequence_number_for(t.id) || Float::INFINITY }
    # *cwdead: merge dead creatures into the same grid (in arrival order)
    # instead of listing them separately below.
    if CreatureWindow.dead_inline
      ordered_creatures = (ordered_creatures + dead_creatures).sort_by { |t| CreatureWindow.sequence_number_for(t.id) || Float::INFINITY }
    end

    render_list, render_cols = CreatureWindow.flow_grid(ordered_creatures)
    render_list.each_slice(render_cols).with_index do |group, row|
      group.each_with_index do |creature, col|
        label_id = "creature_#{row}_#{col}"
        left = col * col_width
        top = current_top + row * creature_row_height
        output += CreatureWindow.creature_cell_xml(label_id, creature, left, top, col_width, creature_row_height, creature.id == curr_target_id)
      end
    end

    grid_rows = render_cols.zero? ? 0 : (render_list.size.to_f / render_cols).ceil
    current_top += grid_rows * creature_row_height

    # Target-next inline mode has no dedicated row for the current target
    # (it stays in place within the grid), so the HP readout is placed below
    # the whole grid (to avoid overlapping the next grid row) but horizontally
    # aligned under the target's own column, not centered under the grid.
    if target_creature
      target_index = render_list.index { |t| t.id == target_creature.id }
      target_col = target_index ? target_index % render_cols : 0
      hp_left = target_col * col_width
      output, current_top = CreatureWindow.append_target_hp_rows(output, target_creature, hp_left, current_top, col_width, row_height)
      output, current_top = CreatureWindow.append_target_ucs_row(output, target_creature, hp_left, current_top, col_width, row_height)
    end

    current_top += row_height # Add a little extra space before the dead-creature list
  else
    # Separate and render current target first
    target_creature = targets.find { |t| t.id == curr_target_id }
    other_creatures = targets.reject { |t| t.id == curr_target_id }
    # *cwdead: merge dead creatures into the same grid (in arrival order)
    # instead of listing them separately below.
    if CreatureWindow.dead_inline
      other_creatures = (other_creatures + dead_creatures).sort_by { |t| CreatureWindow.sequence_number_for(t.id) || Float::INFINITY }
    end

    if target_creature
      status = CreatureWindow.creature_status_fix(target_creature.status, target_creature.name, target_creature.id)
      label_value = CreatureWindow.saga_wrap_status(target_creature.noun, status)

      unless @cw_creature_targeted[target_creature.id]
        @cw_creature_timestamps[target_creature.id] = Time.now
        @cw_creature_targeted[target_creature.id] = true
      end

      cmd = "target ##{target_creature.id}"
      display = CreatureWindow.finalize_creature_label(label_value, true)
      output += "<link id='target_creature' value='#{display}' cmd='#{cmd}' echo='Targeting #{CreatureWindow.sanitize_xml(target_creature.name)}' justify='bottom' left='0' top='#{current_top}' width='#{col_width}' height='#{creature_row_height}' />"
      current_top += creature_row_height

      output, current_top = CreatureWindow.append_target_hp_rows(output, target_creature, 0, current_top, col_width, row_height)
      output, current_top = CreatureWindow.append_target_ucs_row(output, target_creature, 0, current_top, col_width, row_height)

      current_top += row_height # Add a little extra space after target (and hp, if shown) for clarity
    end

    # Creature grid
    render_list, render_cols = CreatureWindow.flow_grid(other_creatures)
    render_list.each_slice(render_cols).with_index do |group, row|
      group.each_with_index do |creature, col|
        label_id = "creature_#{row}_#{col}"
        left = col * col_width
        top = current_top + row * creature_row_height
        output += CreatureWindow.creature_cell_xml(label_id, creature, left, top, col_width, creature_row_height, false)
      end
    end
    # After rendering all creatures, bump spacing by one row before starting dead creature block
    grid_rows = render_cols.zero? ? 0 : (render_list.size.to_f / render_cols).ceil
    current_top += grid_rows * creature_row_height + row_height
  end

  # Track creatures for killed/removed creatures
  current_ids = targets.map(&:id)
  (@cw_creature_timestamps.keys - current_ids).each do |missing_id|
    creature_name = GameObj.npcs.find { |npc| npc.id == missing_id }&.name || "Unknown"
    CreatureWindow.track_creature_kill(missing_id, creature_name)
  end

  # Dead creature listing (dead_creatures itself was computed early, up
  # near hazards/cols, so it's available for the combined header row too)
  add_hazards_section.call if CreatureWindow.hazard_display_mode == "between"

  # id='deadcount' already shown in the combined row above when
  # combine_headers; otherwise emitted here on its own row (blank when
  # headers are off, or when *cwdead already merged dead creatures into
  # the live grid above -- see the comment above the Avg TTK block for why
  # a blank value is emitted rather than the id being left out entirely).
  unless combine_headers
    output += "<label id='deadcount' value='#{CreatureWindow.dead_inline ? '' : header_value.call(dead_count_text)}' left='0' top='#{current_top}' />"
    current_top += row_height if dead_count_text && !CreatureWindow.dead_inline
  end

  unless CreatureWindow.dead_inline
    dead_render_list, dead_render_cols = CreatureWindow.flow_grid(dead_creatures)
    dead_render_list.each_slice(dead_render_cols).with_index do |group, row|
      group.each_with_index do |t, col|
        label_id = "dead_#{row}_#{col}"
        left = col * col_width
        top = current_top + row * row_height
        output += CreatureWindow.creature_cell_xml(label_id, t, left, top, col_width, row_height, false)
      end
    end
    current_top += (dead_render_cols.zero? ? 0 : (dead_render_list.size.to_f / dead_render_cols).ceil) * row_height
  end

  add_hazards_section.call if CreatureWindow.hazard_display_mode == "below_dead"


  output += "</dialogData>"
  _respond(output)
end

def CreatureWindow.targets_snapshot(targets)
  current_target = XMLData.current_target_id
  creature_part = targets
                  .map { |t| "#{t.id}:#{t.status}:#{t.name}" }
                  .sort
                  .join("|")
  hazard_part = CreatureWindow.current_hazards
                              .map { |hazard| "#{hazard.id}:#{hazard.name}" }
                              .sort
                              .join("|")
  "#{creature_part}|hazards:#{hazard_part}|hazard_mode:#{CreatureWindow.hazard_display_mode}|current:#{current_target}|claim:#{CreatureWindow.claim_status_text}"
end

def CreatureWindow.refresh_creature_windows(targets)
  dead_creatures = CreatureWindow.dead_creatures_now
  hazards = CreatureWindow.current_hazards
  CreatureWindow.assign_sequence_numbers!((targets || []) + dead_creatures)
  CreatureWindow.reset_kill_metrics_if_inactive(dead_creatures)
  CreatureWindow.track_owned_room_kills(dead_creatures)
  CreatureWindow.track_empyrean_kills(dead_creatures)
  kpm_display = CreatureWindow.calculate_owned_room_kpm

  CreatureWindow.push_creatures_to_window(targets) if Frontend.supports_room_window?

  return unless CreatureWindow.gtk_enabled?

  CreatureWindowGtk.update_creatures(
    targets,
    hazards: hazards,
    avg_ttk: CreatureWindow.calculate_avg_ttk,
    last_ttk: @cw_last_kill_time ? format("%.2f sec", @cw_last_kill_time) : "N/A",
    kpm: kpm_display,
    bounty_task: CreatureWindow.bounty_task_line,
    bounty_status: CreatureWindow.bounty_status_line,
    bounty_action: CreatureWindow.bounty_action_line,
    display_avg_ttk: CreatureWindow.display_avg_ttk,
    display_last_ttk: CreatureWindow.display_last_ttk,
    display_kpm: CreatureWindow.display_kpm,
    display_bounty: CreatureWindow.display_bounty
  )
end

upstream_hook_id = "#{Script.current.name}_upstream"
downstream_hook_id = "#{Script.current.name}_downstream"

UpstreamHook.remove(upstream_hook_id)   rescue nil
DownstreamHook.remove(downstream_hook_id) rescue nil

DownstreamHook.add(downstream_hook_id, proc do |line|
  begin
    CreatureWindow.push_recent_line(line.to_s.strip)
    # DownstreamHook fires on the RAW server line (see
    # Game::Sge#process_downstream_hooks in lib/games.rb), before Lich's own
    # XML parser strips it down to plain text -- so a monster-bold-wrapped
    # "Empyrean"/"captain" (<pushBold/>...<popBold/>, common for creature
    # nouns in combat text) would otherwise sit INSIDE the raw line and
    # break a plain contiguous-text match. Strip all tags first so the
    # captain-encounter-end patterns match regardless.
    plain_line = line.to_s.gsub(/<[^>]*>/, '')
    if plain_line =~ CreatureWindow::CAPTAIN_FLEE_PATTERN || plain_line =~ CreatureWindow::CAPTAIN_DEFEATED_PATTERN
      CreatureWindow.reset_empyrean_since_captain_count!
      CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push("update_window")
    end
  rescue StandardError => e
    echo "Creaturewindow line capture error: #{e.message}"
  end
  line
end)

UpstreamHook.add(upstream_hook_id, proc do |command|
  window_settings = CreatureWindow.load_window_settings
  window_settings["creaturewindow"] ||= {}

  case command
  when /\*cwbty/i
    CreatureWindow.display_bounty = !CreatureWindow.display_bounty
    window_settings["creaturewindow"]["display_bounty"] = CreatureWindow.display_bounty
    CreatureWindow.save_window_settings(window_settings)
    CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push("update_window")
    respond "Bounty display: #{CreatureWindow.display_bounty ? 'ON' : 'OFF'}"
    nil

  when /\*cwttk/i
    enabled = !CreatureWindow.display_avg_ttk
    CreatureWindow.display_avg_ttk = enabled
    CreatureWindow.display_last_ttk = enabled
    CreatureWindow.display_kpm = enabled
    window_settings["creaturewindow"]["display_avg_ttk"] = CreatureWindow.display_avg_ttk
    window_settings["creaturewindow"]["display_last_ttk"] = CreatureWindow.display_last_ttk
    window_settings["creaturewindow"]["display_kpm"] = CreatureWindow.display_kpm
    CreatureWindow.save_window_settings(window_settings)
    CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push("update_window")
    respond "Average TTK display: #{CreatureWindow.display_avg_ttk ? 'ON' : 'OFF'}"
    respond "Last TTK display: #{CreatureWindow.display_last_ttk ? 'ON' : 'OFF'}"
    respond "Kills per minute display: #{CreatureWindow.display_kpm ? 'ON' : 'OFF'}"
    nil

  when /\*cwcol\s*(\d+)?/i
    if $1
      n = CreatureWindow.apply_grid_cols(window_settings, $1)
      respond "Grid columns: #{n} (used when *cwflow is row)"
    else
      respond "Grid columns: #{CreatureWindow.grid_cols} (usage: *cwcol <1-10>)"
    end
    nil

  when /\*cwrow\s*(\d+)?/i
    if $1
      n = CreatureWindow.apply_grid_rows(window_settings, $1)
      respond "Grid rows: #{n} (used when *cwflow is col)"
    else
      respond "Grid rows: #{CreatureWindow.grid_rows} (usage: *cwrow <1-10>)"
    end
    nil

  when /\*cwflow\s*(\S+)?/i
    modes = CreatureWindow::GRID_FLOWS
    requested = $1&.downcase
    requested = "col" if requested =~ /^col(umns?)?$/
    requested = "row" if requested =~ /^row(s)?$/

    next_mode = if modes.include?(requested)
                  requested
                else
                  modes[(modes.index(CreatureWindow.grid_flow).to_i + 1) % modes.size]
                end

    CreatureWindow.grid_flow = next_mode
    window_settings["creaturewindow"]["grid_flow"] = next_mode
    CreatureWindow.save_window_settings(window_settings)
    CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push("update_window")

    label = { "row" => "ROW (left-to-right first, then wraps top-to-bottom, using *cwcol's count)",
              "col" => "COLUMN (top-to-bottom first, then wraps left-to-right, using *cwrow's count)" }[next_mode]
    respond "Creaturewindow grid flow: #{label}"
    nil

  when /\*cwdead/i
    CreatureWindow.dead_inline = !CreatureWindow.dead_inline
    window_settings["creaturewindow"]["dead_inline"] = CreatureWindow.dead_inline
    CreatureWindow.save_window_settings(window_settings)
    CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push("update_window")
    respond "Creaturewindow dead creatures kept inline: #{CreatureWindow.dead_inline ? 'ON' : 'OFF'}"
    nil

  when /\*cwclaim/i
    CreatureWindow.display_claim = !CreatureWindow.display_claim
    window_settings["creaturewindow"]["display_claim"] = CreatureWindow.display_claim
    CreatureWindow.save_window_settings(window_settings)
    CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push("update_window")
    respond "Creaturewindow claim status: #{CreatureWindow.display_claim ? 'SHOWN' : 'HIDDEN'}"
    nil

  when /\*cwhazard/i
    modes = CreatureWindow::HAZARD_DISPLAY_MODES
    next_mode = modes[(modes.index(CreatureWindow.hazard_display_mode).to_i + 1) % modes.size]
    CreatureWindow.hazard_display_mode = next_mode
    window_settings["creaturewindow"]["hazard_display_mode"] = next_mode
    CreatureWindow.save_window_settings(window_settings)
    CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push("update_window")

    label = {
      "above" => "ABOVE creatures",
      "between" => "BETWEEN creatures and dead creatures",
      "below_dead" => "BELOW dead creatures",
      "off" => "OFF"
    }[next_mode]
    respond "Creaturewindow hazard display: #{label}"
    nil

  when /\*cwheaders/i
    modes = CreatureWindow::HEADER_MODES
    next_mode = modes[(modes.index(CreatureWindow.header_mode).to_i + 1) % modes.size]
    CreatureWindow.header_mode = next_mode
    window_settings["creaturewindow"]["header_mode"] = next_mode
    CreatureWindow.save_window_settings(window_settings)
    CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push("update_window")

    label = {
      "text"  => "TEXT (\"Creatures: N\" / \"Hazards: N\" / \"Dead Creatures: N\")",
      "emoji" => "EMOJI (compact icon + bare count, combined onto one row)",
      "off"   => "OFF"
    }[next_mode]
    respond "Creaturewindow Creatures:/Hazards:/Dead Creatures: headers: #{label}"
    nil

  when /\*cwcustom1/i
    CreatureWindow.custom_layout1 = !CreatureWindow.custom_layout1
    window_settings["creaturewindow"]["custom_layout1"] = CreatureWindow.custom_layout1
    CreatureWindow.save_window_settings(window_settings)
    CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push("update_window")
    respond "Creaturewindow custom layout 1: #{CreatureWindow.custom_layout1 ? 'ON' : 'OFF'}"
    nil

  when /\*cwonslaught\s+timer\b/i
    CreatureWindow.onslaught_timer_enabled = !CreatureWindow.onslaught_timer_enabled
    window_settings["creaturewindow"]["onslaught_timer_enabled"] = CreatureWindow.onslaught_timer_enabled
    CreatureWindow.save_window_settings(window_settings)
    if CreatureWindow.onslaught_timer_enabled
      # Force an immediate poll instead of waiting up to
      # ONSLAUGHT_POLL_SECONDS for the main loop's own timer, so turning
      # this on shows something right away.
      @cw_last_onslaught_check = Time.at(0)
    end
    CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push("update_window")
    respond "Creaturewindow Gem Onslaught location/timer (*cwcustom1): #{CreatureWindow.onslaught_timer_enabled ? 'ON' : 'OFF'}"
    nil

  when /\*cwonslaught\s+counter\b/i
    CreatureWindow.onslaught_counter_enabled = !CreatureWindow.onslaught_counter_enabled
    window_settings["creaturewindow"]["onslaught_counter_enabled"] = CreatureWindow.onslaught_counter_enabled
    CreatureWindow.save_window_settings(window_settings)
    CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push("update_window")
    respond "Creaturewindow Empyrean kill counter (*cwcustom1): #{CreatureWindow.onslaught_counter_enabled ? 'ON' : 'OFF'}"
    nil

  when /\*cwonslaught\b/i
    respond "Usage: *cwonslaught timer | *cwonslaught counter"
    nil

  when /\*cwicon\s+(\S+)\s+(reset|default)\s*\z/i
    slot = $1.downcase
    if CreatureWindow.reset_custom_icon!(slot)
      CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push("update_window")
      respond "Creaturewindow #{slot} icon: reset to default"
    elsif CreatureWindow::CUSTOM_ICON_SLOTS.include?(slot)
      respond "Creaturewindow #{slot} icon is already at its default"
    else
      respond "Creaturewindow: unknown icon slot '#{slot}' (expected: #{CreatureWindow::CUSTOM_ICON_SLOTS.join(', ')})"
    end
    nil

  when /\*cwicon\s+(\S+)\s+(.+?)\s*\z/i
    slot = $1.downcase
    requested = $2
    if !CreatureWindow::CUSTOM_ICON_SLOTS.include?(slot)
      respond "Creaturewindow: unknown icon slot '#{slot}' (expected: #{CreatureWindow::CUSTOM_ICON_SLOTS.join(', ')})"
    elsif CreatureWindow.set_custom_icon!(slot, requested)
      CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push("update_window")
      respond "Creaturewindow #{slot} icon updated"
    else
      respond "Creaturewindow: could not read an icon from '#{requested}'"
    end
    nil

  when /\*cwicon\b/i
    respond "Usage: *cwicon <#{CreatureWindow::CUSTOM_ICON_SLOTS.join('|')}> <emoji>"
    respond "       *cwicon <#{CreatureWindow::CUSTOM_ICON_SLOTS.join('|')}> reset"
    nil

  when /\*cwtest/i
    CreatureWindow.test_mode = !CreatureWindow.test_mode
    if CreatureWindow.test_mode
      CreatureWindow.generate_test_data!
    end
    CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push("update_window")
    respond "Creaturewindow test mode: #{CreatureWindow.test_mode ? 'ON (24 fake creatures, 3 fake hazards)' : 'OFF'}"
    nil

  when /\*cwstatus/i
    modes = CreatureWindow::SAGA_STATUS_MODES
    next_mode = modes[(modes.index(CreatureWindow.saga_status_mode).to_i + 1) % modes.size]
    CreatureWindow.saga_status_mode = next_mode
    window_settings["creaturewindow"]["saga_status_mode"] = next_mode
    CreatureWindow.save_window_settings(window_settings)
    CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push("update_window")

    label = {
      "text"    => "TEXT (plain status words)",
      "unicode" => "UNICODE (\u{262E} \u{2744} \u{2327} \u{2693} \u{1DBB}\u{1DBB}\u{1DBB} \u{203B} \u{2739} \u{21D3} \u{21D1})",
      "emoji"   => "EMOJI (\u{1F60C} \u{2744}\u{FE0F} \u{26D3}\u{FE0F} \u{1FAB5} \u{1F4A4} \u{1F578}\u{FE0F} \u{26A1} \u{2B07}\u{FE0F} \u{1FABD} \u{1FAA6})"
    }[next_mode]
    respond "Creaturewindow Saga status display: #{label}"
    nil

  when /\*cwtargetnext\s*(\S+)?/i
    modes = CreatureWindow::TARGET_NEXT_MODES
    requested = $1&.downcase&.gsub(/[\s_-]+/, '_')
    requested = "no_numbers" if requested =~ /^no.?numbers?$/
    requested = "numbers" if requested =~ /^numbers?$/
    requested = "off" if requested =~ /^off$/

    next_mode = if modes.include?(requested)
                  requested
                else
                  modes[(modes.index(CreatureWindow.target_next_mode).to_i + 1) % modes.size]
                end

    CreatureWindow.target_next_mode = next_mode
    window_settings["creaturewindow"]["target_next_mode"] = next_mode
    CreatureWindow.save_window_settings(window_settings)
    CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push("update_window")

    label = { "off" => "OFF (current target floats to top)",
              "numbers" => "NUMBERS (target stays in sequence, numbers shown)",
              "no_numbers" => "NO NUMBERS (target stays in sequence, numbers hidden)" }[next_mode]
    respond "Creaturewindow target-next mode: #{label}"
    nil

  when /\*cwhp/i
    modes = CreatureWindow::TARGET_HP_MODES
    next_mode = modes[(modes.index(CreatureWindow.target_hp_mode).to_i + 1) % modes.size]
    CreatureWindow.target_hp_mode = next_mode
    window_settings["creaturewindow"]["target_hp_mode"] = next_mode
    CreatureWindow.save_window_settings(window_settings)
    CreatureWindow.ensure_hp_tracking! unless next_mode == "off"
    CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push("update_window")

    label = {
      "off"  => "OFF",
      "text" => "TEXT (###/### hp)",
      "bar"  => "BAR (10-segment bar + ###/### hp)"
    }[next_mode]
    respond "Creaturewindow target HP display: #{label}"
    nil

  when /\*cwtargetid/i
    icons = CreatureWindow::TARGET_MARKER_ICONS
    next_index = (CreatureWindow.target_marker_index + 1) % icons.size
    CreatureWindow.target_marker_index = next_index
    window_settings["creaturewindow"]["target_marker_index"] = next_index
    CreatureWindow.save_window_settings(window_settings)
    CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push("update_window")

    preview = ["\u{2297}", "\u{2A01}", "\u{1F3AF}"][next_index]
    respond "Creaturewindow target marker icon: #{preview} (Saga emoji mode only)"
    nil

  when /\*cwucs/i
    CreatureWindow.ucs_mode = !CreatureWindow.ucs_mode
    window_settings["creaturewindow"]["ucs_mode"] = CreatureWindow.ucs_mode
    CreatureWindow.save_window_settings(window_settings)
    # UCS position/tierup data only ever populates via Combat::Tracker's
    # downstream hook (lib/gemstone/combat), which is disabled by default
    # like *cwhp's HP tracking -- without this, *cwucs would just show
    # nothing forever since Creature[id].ucs_position/ucs_tierup never get
    # set. Same ensure_hp_tracking! helper *cwhp already uses; a no-op if
    # Combat::Tracker (or *cwhp) already turned it on.
    CreatureWindow.ensure_hp_tracking! if CreatureWindow.ucs_mode
    CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push("update_window")
    respond "Creaturewindow UCS display: #{CreatureWindow.ucs_mode ? 'ON (Pos: N     Tup: Action under the current target)' : 'OFF'}"
    nil

  when /\*cwherb/i
    CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push("run_herb_bounty_workflow")
    nil

  when /\*cwgem/i
    CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push("run_gem_bounty_workflow")
    nil

  when /\*cwguild/i
    CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push("run_guild_bounty_workflow")
    nil

  when /\*cwguard/i
    CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push("run_guard_bounty_workflow")
    nil

  when /\*cwfurrier/i
    CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push("run_furrier_bounty_workflow")
    nil

  when /\*cwskin/i
    CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push("run_skin_bounty_workflow")
    nil

  when /\*cwgtk/i
    CreatureWindow.use_gtk_window = !CreatureWindow.use_gtk_window
    respond "GTK Creaturewindow is now #{CreatureWindow.use_gtk_window ? 'ENABLED' : 'DISABLED'}."

    # persist the new setting
    settings = CreatureWindow.load_window_settings
    settings["creaturewindow"] ||= {}
    settings["creaturewindow"]["use_gtk_creaturewindow"] = CreatureWindow.use_gtk_window
    CreatureWindow.save_window_settings(settings)

    if CreatureWindow.use_gtk_window
      if CreatureWindow.gtk_available
        Gtk.queue { CreatureWindowGtk.create_main_window }
        Thread.new { CreatureWindow.start_gtk_main_if_needed }
      else
        CreatureWindow.use_gtk_window = false
        settings["creaturewindow"]["use_gtk_creaturewindow"] = false
        CreatureWindow.save_window_settings(settings)
        respond "GTK unavailable. Install gtk3 gem to enable GTK Creaturewindow."
      end
    else
      # close it if it exists
      if CreatureWindow.gtk_available && defined?(CreatureWindowGtk) && CreatureWindowGtk.instance_variable_get(:@window)
        Gtk.queue do
          CreatureWindowGtk.instance_variable_get(:@window).close
        end
      end
    end

    nil

  else
    command
  end
end)

before_dying do
  UpstreamHook.remove(upstream_hook_id)
  DownstreamHook.remove(downstream_hook_id) rescue nil

  if CreatureWindow.gtk_available && defined?(CreatureWindowGtk) && (cw = CreatureWindowGtk.instance_variable_get(:@window))
    Gtk.queue do
      begin
        cw.close
      rescue StandardError
        cw.hide rescue nil
      end
    end
  end
end

echo "Creaturewindow is active." if Frontend.supports_room_window?

CreatureWindow.ensure_hp_tracking! if CreatureWindow.target_hp_mode != "off" || CreatureWindow.ucs_mode
CreatureWindow.capture_bounty_origin_context
CreatureWindow.parse_bounty_from_checkbounty
@cw_last_bounty_signature = CreatureWindow.bounty_state_signature
@cw_last_bounty_check ||= Time.now
# Time.at(0), not Time.now, so *cwcustom1's first onslaught poll fires on
# the very next main-loop pass instead of waiting a full
# ONSLAUGHT_POLL_SECONDS after startup.
@cw_last_onslaught_check ||= Time.at(0)
@cw_onslaught_active = nil
@cw_onslaught_location = nil
@cw_onslaught_remaining = nil
@cw_onslaught_next_at = nil
CreatureWindow.test_mode = false
@cw_test_targets = []
@cw_test_hazards = []

Thread.new do
  loop do
    cmd = CreatureWindow::TARGET_CMD_QUEUE.pop
    begin
      fput cmd
    rescue => e
      echo "Creaturewindow target command error: #{e.message}"
    ensure
      CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push("update_window")
    end
  end
end

loop do
  current_targets = CreatureWindow.current_targets_now
  snapshot = CreatureWindow.targets_snapshot(current_targets)

  # Refresh when creature/status snapshot changes or on heartbeat interval.
  if snapshot != @cw_last_targets_snapshot || (Time.now - @cw_last_ui_refresh_at) > 1.0
    @cw_last_targets = current_targets
    @cw_last_targets_snapshot = snapshot
    @cw_last_ui_refresh_at = Time.now
    CreatureWindow.refresh_creature_windows(current_targets)
  end

  # - when you flip one of the toggles via commands -
  unless CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.empty?
    cmd = CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.pop
    if cmd == "update_window"
      CreatureWindow.refresh_creature_windows(current_targets)
      @cw_last_targets_snapshot = CreatureWindow.targets_snapshot(current_targets)
      @cw_last_ui_refresh_at = Time.now
    elsif cmd == "run_herb_bounty_workflow"
      CreatureWindow.run_herb_bounty_workflow
    elsif cmd == "run_gem_bounty_workflow"
      CreatureWindow.run_gem_bounty_workflow
    elsif cmd == "run_guild_bounty_workflow"
      CreatureWindow.run_guild_bounty_workflow
    elsif cmd == "run_guard_bounty_workflow"
      CreatureWindow.run_guard_bounty_workflow
    elsif cmd == "run_furrier_bounty_workflow"
      CreatureWindow.run_furrier_bounty_workflow
    elsif cmd == "run_skin_bounty_workflow"
      CreatureWindow.run_skin_bounty_workflow
    elsif cmd.is_a?(Array) && cmd.first == "hazard_action"
      hazard_id = cmd[1]
      hazard = CreatureWindow.current_hazards.find { |obj| obj.id == hazard_id }
      CreatureWindow.perform_hazard_action(hazard)
      CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push("update_window")
    end
  end

  # - periodic bounty refresh -
  if Time.now - @cw_last_bounty_check > CreatureWindow::BOUNTY_POLL_SECONDS
    CreatureWindow.capture_bounty_origin_context if @cw_bounty_origin_npc_id.nil?
    previous_signature = @cw_last_bounty_signature
    CreatureWindow.parse_bounty_from_checkbounty
    current_signature = CreatureWindow.bounty_state_signature
    if current_signature != previous_signature
      CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push("update_window")
      @cw_last_bounty_signature = current_signature
    end
    @cw_last_bounty_check = Time.now
  end

  # - periodic gem onslaught refresh -- independent of *cwcustom1, only
  #   gated on *cwonslaught timer itself, so it works whether or not
  #   *cwcustom1 is on -
  if CreatureWindow.onslaught_timer_enabled && (Time.now - @cw_last_onslaught_check > CreatureWindow::ONSLAUGHT_POLL_SECONDS)
    before_active = @cw_onslaught_active
    before_location = @cw_onslaught_location
    CreatureWindow.refresh_onslaught!
    if @cw_onslaught_active != before_active || @cw_onslaught_location != before_location
      CreatureWindow::CMD_QUEUE.push("update_window")
    end
    @cw_last_onslaught_check = Time.now
  end

  sleep 0.1
end
